INSERT INTO `capstonebooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(1, 12, 'BSIT', 'GRADUATE TRACER WITH DIGITAL COMMUNICATOR FOR BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY ALUMNI OFFICE', 'In today’s fast-paced world, effective communication is crucial for success in both personal and professional spheres. Clear, concise, and respectful interactions can significantly impact relationships, productivity, and overall satisfaction. Communication involves not only the exchange of information but also the ability to listen actively, understand various perspectives, and convey thoughts in a way that is both engaging and respectful.\r\nOne of the key components of effective communication is active listening. This means fully concentrating, understanding, responding, and then remembering what is being said. It’s not merely about hearing words but comprehending the message behind them. Active listening helps build trust and resolve conflicts, as it shows that one values the speaker’s viewpoint. Furthermore, non-verbal communication, such as body language, facial expressions, and eye contact, plays an essential role. It often conveys more than words and can enhance or contradict verbal messages. Being aware of one’s non-verbal signals and interpreting those of others accurately can lead to more successful interactions. In professional settings, effective communication can lead to improved teamwork, higher efficiency, and better problem-solving. It fosters a positive work environment where team members feel heard and valued. On a personal level, it can enhance relationships, reduce misunderstandings, and contribute to a more harmonious life. Ultimately, investing time and effort in honing communication skills is a valuable endeavor that can lead to greater success and satisfaction in various aspects of life.\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Bolina Alfredo Jr., B. Jose, Lalorence, C., Lopez, Ronan Angelo, Santos, Marc Nathaniel'),
(2, 15, 'BSIT', 'WEB-BASED POINT OF SALE AND ONLINE ORDERING SYSTEM FOR ZSAKERS CAFE HAGONOY BRANCH', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a Web-based Point of Sale and Online Ordering System for Zsakers Café Hagony Branch. The system has the following features: Point of Sale, Inventory Management, Sales Monitoring, Online Ordering, and Online Payment. The researchers collected data on all the business operations of Zsakers Café Hagony Branch by observing the companys operations and interviewing its personnel. This information was used to create the Web-based Point of Sale and Online Ordering System, which can be utilized for daily transactions by Zsakers Café Hagonoy Branch. The Agile Model was utilized in the creation of the system. This approach assisted the researchers in identifying the companys issues, defining business requirements, and designing the information system through analysis and Visualization. The current system of the company slows them to provide a more efficient, fast and convenient way of serving their product. It leads also in data inaccuracy in their inventory and sales. The new system aims to solve these issues by providing more reliable and secure data management and attracting more customers through the convenience of online ordering and payment through GCash. The system also streamlines the company s operations by allowing them to quickly view and manage customer orders and provides better monitoring through inventory and sales reports.', 2022, 'Estrada, Arthur P. | Libao, Jade J. | Regidor Jeffrey DR. | Salamat, Romnick B. Zaspa, Joshua B'),
(3, 8, 'BSIT', 'BULSU-HAGONOY WEB-BASED CAMPUS SECURITY CONTROL SYSTEM', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a Security Control System for Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus. The system has the following major function: Campus Vicinity Monitoring Management, CCTV Control Center Management, Campus Community Monitoring Management and Emergency Locator Mobile Application. The researchers gathered information of the entire activity of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus while observing in the school premises, by interviewing and making a survey questionnaire on different personnel in the campus. The information gathered was properly documented and analysed which leads the researchers to develop the BulSUHagony Web-based Campus Security Control System which can be used to monitor the security of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus. The methodology used in the development of the system is the Model-Driven Methodology. This methodology helps the researchers to analyze and visualize the problems of the university, define the requirements and design the security control system. The existing system of the campus was found to be inconsistent in terms of data entry specifically the duplication and loss of security related data. It produced inaccurate data resulting to a negative effect in the school. With the current system maximum effort is required in handling data because it uses manual data entry and are prone to errors. The developed system eliminates these problems and will help the school to be more secure, produce reliable results and prevents data loss. The Security Officers will know who enters and exits the campus with the help of the barcode scanner. CCTV (Closed-circuit television) and DVR (Digital video recorder) is primarily utilized for the CCTV Control Center Management function. The system can generate a report such as student violations, statistics of any person who enters and exits the campus by type, date and time. To develop the system, the researchers utilized PHP for the functionality of the system, XAMPP Server for the database, Microsoft Windows 7 for the workstation, and Google chrome is used as the browser to access the system and display each individual web page. The system was tested both in the development environment and the environment of the user. The users acceptance testing resulted with 85.33 percent completion of all the requirements and specifications. The researchers recommends the use of the developed system this coming 2nd semester of academic year 2018-2019.', 2018, 'Bernabe, Alfred C. | Calonzo, Reinne Clark S. | Paguia, Relito M. | Palma, Mark Jason M. | Perez, Leo Patrick L'),
(4, 11, 'BSIT', 'ONLINE STUDENT INTERNSHIP MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH MATCHING ALGORITHM FOR BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY CAREER DEVELOPMENT AND STUDENT INTERNSHIP SERVICES', 'The Purpose of this study is to develop a Online Student Internship Management System with Matching Algorithm for Bulacan State University Career Development and Student Internship Services. The system Has the following main functions: Student Interns Information Management, Host Training Establishment Information Management, Internship Status Monitoring, Internship Portfolio Management, Internship Matching Algorithm, Chat Facility and Comment Section for Portfolio Management. The researchers gathered the information of the entire activity of the Career Development and Student Internship Services, by interviewing and making a survey questionnaire on the Head of the CarDSIS office and the graduate student that experienced the internship. The Information gathered by the researcher was properly documented and analyzed which leads for the researcher to develop the Online Student Internship Management System with Matching Algorithm for Bulacan State University Career Development and Student Internship Services which can be used to monitor the progress of the student interns of Bulacan State University. The Methodology used in the development of the system is the Rapid Application Development Methodology. This methodology helps the researcher to analyze and visualize the problems of the CarDSIS office, define the requirements and design students internship management system. The existing system of the CarDSIS office was found to be inconsistent in terms of the data, specifically the duplication and loss of Internship related data. It produced inaccurate data resulting in difficulties in locating the desired information. With the current system effort is required in handling data because it uses a manual process of data entry that is prone to errors. The developed system will eliminate these problems and will help the CarDSIS office to be more secure, produce reliable results and prevent data loss. The Admin can now monitor the current interns and the top location where interns take their internship, also can easily generate the related information. The SIP coordinator can view the progress of student interns and can interact directly with them. Interns can save time when they submit needed documents for OJT and submit their weekly report electronically. The system can generate reports such as student information, weekly reports of interns. To develop the system, the researchers utilized PHP for the functionality of the system, XAMPP Server for the database, Hostinger Web Hosting is used by the researcher to facilitate transactions inside the Online Student Intens Management System and a Web browser to access the system and display each individual web page. The system was tested both in the development environment and the environment of the user. The developed system is very convenient for the Head of CarDSIS office, SIP coordinator and student interns because it is easy to use. Therefore, the researchers recommend the use of the developed system this coming 2nd semester of academic year 2021-2022.', 2022, 'Fautino, Mark, R., Fautino , Wendell M., Jore Aaron Den DC., Ruaya, Aaron Japheth O.'),
(5, 31, 'BSIT', 'HUMAN RESOURCE INFORMATION SYSTEM WITH EMPLOYEE PORTAL FOR BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a Human Resource Information System with an Employee Portal for Bulacan State University. The system has two main functions: The Employee Information Management and the Employee Payroll Management. Employee Portal, Employee Training and Development Record, and Employee Time Keeping Management are the features included in the system. The researchers gathered information from different Human Resource Information Systems. Interviews with faculty members from the university were also facilitated. This information was then properly documented and investigated which serves as the basis of the researchers to develop the system. The methodology used in the development of the system is Rapid Application Development Methodology. The researchers can easily adapt to changes as it is needed continuous feedback from the end-users resulting to a fast delivery of the system. The developed system speeds up the day-to-day transactions in the Human Resource Management Office and helps increase productivity in the workplace. The system will greatly contribute to the tasks of HR personnel since data, after being stored, processed, and updated, can be viewed, and printed by both HR and faculty. The system will generate necessary reports and documents required to be submitted regularly. The regular and excess salary of permanent faculty, and the salary of part-time faculty can be processed easily using the system. Moreover, faculty will benefit from using the system because it will provide features like being regularly informed and updated on some important announcements Likewise, chat support is included to immediately address the faculty concerns and queries. To develop the system, the researchers utilized Hypertext Markup Language, Cascading Style Sheets, javascripts, and bootstrap for the design of the system, XAMPP Server for the database, Microsoft Windows 10 for the workstation, and Google chrome is used as the browser to access the system. The system was tested both in the development environment and the environment of the user. The users acceptance testing resulted with 91.7 percent completion of all the requirements. The researchers recommend the system may be used by the HRMO of Bulacan State University.', 2022, '	Aserit, James Ronel A | Casia, John Ronnel | Pangan, Krizia Carrise | Robles, Ma. Donita'),
(6, 6, 'Information Technology', 'BULSU HC MOBILE APP FOR STUDENT SERVICES', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a BulSU HC Mobile App for Student Services. The system was designed to provide services to the students such as viewing of health records, guidance records, violation records, announcements, notifications, grades and class schedule. It has the following features: Student Information Management, Health Record Management, Student Violation Management, Guidance Record Management and Geofence. The system was developed using the Agile Methodology. The researchers utilized Android Studio and Java Programming Language in creating the mobile application. For the functionality of the system, PHP Scripting Language and MySQL were used. The system undergone a thorough User Acceptance Testing. A test plan was prepared to guide the users in testing all the functions of the system. Appropriate test cases for each function were included to determine if the system satisfies the requirements. It was tested by ten students and five personnel of Bulacan State University - Hagony Campus which resulted to 92 percent completion of all the requirements and specifications of the system. The BuISU HC Mobile App for Student Services was created as designed to allow the viewing of health records, guidance records, violation records, grades and class schedule of the students, posting of announcements and notifications if the Students Services Personnel are within the campus premises.', 2018, 'Aguilar, Jan Michael Vincent F. | Binene, John Restine B. | Fajardo, Daren Jhenez P. | Gonzales, Johnazze C. | Timblique Jr. Crisanto P |'),
(7, 14, 'Information Technology', 'WEB-BASED SCHOOL PORTAL SYSTEM FOR IBA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL - SENIOR HIGH DEPARTMENT', 'The \"Web-based Schoo! Portal System for Iba National High School - Senior High department\" is a web-based research project that will assist staff and students in school processes by acting as an information kiosk for students and faculty because it is web-based and can be seen from anywhere and at any time, the web-based school portal system may offer a straightforward way to effectively manage information that is extremely simple for schools to utilize. The method is created to speed up the educationai process. Lowering the deiay using the manuai approach is the systems total benefit. The teachers often need help organizing grades and other student information. So, to increase administration and transparency, we researchers deveioped the siudent poriai sysiem, a web-based piatform that enables educational institutions to collect student data online. The main features of the Web-based School Portal System for Iba National High School - Senior High Department are the following: The school portal has an early enrollment function for old and incoming students, the administrator will manage the information filed in the early enrollment form, and it will give an estimation that can be view in early enrollment graph, For the sign up/registration function, The admin will manage all incoming data and gives permission to create an account if theyre already enrolled, and the registrar manage all account of the enrolled students. The system allows the administrator to manage the events/announcement, admission, and grade submission period. Users can view the announcement on the website homepage. The system added a strand test function to give future senior high students an insight into their possible strand by answering a simple test. provided on the homepage. The teacher can submit the students grades through the schooi portai, and the student will receive the grades in their respective accounts. The developed school portal system is valuable and functional, intended to help the students, teachers, and school adminisiration improve and reduce the resources consumed by their aging process. The developed system was satisfied and able to meet the specification of the users. The user acceptance test for teacher management is 85.71%, student and administrator management are 100%, and registrar management is 84.94%. Resulted for the overall percentage of 92.66% indicated that the researchers were able to comply with the user requirements. The remaining 7.34% percent is from the login function, the teachers grading function and the registrar manage accounts for teachers and students. However, the system is improved before its deployment and implementation.', 2022, 'Baluyot, Kevin C. | Batusan, Jaydelyn R. | Dela Cruz, John Orly D. | Insular, Daniel S. | Mayor, Samantha Zia Dr'),
(8, 38, 'BSIT', 'MALWARE WARS: DEFENDING YOUR NETWORK FROM DIGITAL THREATS - A MOBILE GAME', 'Malware Wars, an advanced educational mobile game, addresses the essential need for increased cybersecurity education in our technologically driven day. Leveraging a rapid application development (RAD) methodology, this study meticulously crafts an immersive and educational gaming experience tailored for users aged 10 to 25. Through the innovative tower defense mechanism, players engage in self-paced learning, acquiring essential skills to identify and thwart diverse malware threats effectively. The studys defined objectives, including risk reduction, game design, cybersecurity integration, and acceptability evaluation, result in strong findings. The games quality in numerous aspects is demonstrated by evaluation criteria, confirming its effectiveness as an instructional tool. Utilizing Google Forms to conduct evaluations showcases the adaptability and accessibility of modern tools in educational research, enhancing the efficiency of data collection and analysis. Users reported excellent levels of interest, improved cybersecurity awareness, and supported the games user-friendly layout. These findings not only verify Malware Wars as a good instructional resource but also have larger implications for the potential of gamified approaches in cybersecurity education, implying a viable path for effective and interesting learning experiences. The success of Malware Wars suggests a forward-thinking initiative in leveraging gaming technology for educational purposes, setting a precedent for transformative potential in fostering a cyber-resilient generation.', 2023, 'Agapay, Ian Xander S. | Bernal, Sharmainne Emmanuelle | Fabian, Dustin L. | Granadel, Lucia May V. | Santos, Kin Mathew S. | Siren, Ed Mark Angelo, L.'),
(9, 37, 'BSIT', 'BULSU-HAGONOY CAMPUS WEB-BASED DIGITALIZED CLASSROOM RECORDS MANAGEMENT SYSTEM', 'This study will mtroduce a lot of benefits to Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus such as teachers can easily access and update student records from anywhere with internet access and without the need of requiring their students to bring an index card. PHP was the selected programming language to undergo the study. The researchers use the mixed-method research design and by combining with the 150 25010 standard for evaluation, the research findings provide insights into the development of diverse tools and funcionalities geared toward enhancing both student productivity and faculty interaction within educational settings. The project got an overall mean of 4 64 with the equivalent of Very Satisfied user. By following the Agile Methodology, the researchers are able to track and develop the project dynamically. The implementation of the study involved utilizing personal smartphones or laptops of users to access the Classroom Record Management System. Additionally, the evaluation criteria employed provide a comprehensive understanding of the systems acceptability, highlighting its strengths and areas for potential improvement.', 2023, 'Castillo, Elijah John B.| Dela Cruz, Airah Lynn DC.| Dela Cruz, Karl Nathaniel S.| Gonzales, Jovi Mhar L.| Pagdanganan, Katz Cedric C.| Pineda, Robin Jeffrey V.'),
(10, 36, 'BSIT', 'HARNESSING DATA FOR EFFECTIVE GOVERNANCE: A WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH DEMOGRAPHIC ANALYTICS FOR BARANGAY SAGRDA FAMILIA, HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'This study was developed to describe the daily operations and its encountered problems of Barangay Sagrada Familia, Hagonoy, Bulacan. These problems were addressed and analyzed to be the features in the developed system Harnessing Data for Effective Governance: A Web-Based Management System with Demographic Analytics for Barangay Sagrada Familia, Hagonoy, Bulacan. The system covers managing residents information, managing clearance and permits, barangay informations security, and blotter cases. This study also determined the users that will navigate the system. This study also covered resolving problem of the barangay upon the implementation of the developed system. Ensuring the integrity of the Data Privacy Act of 2012 was the primary objective of this study. This study is evaluated the performance of the system using a software evaluation instrument, ISO 25010/IEC in terms of Functionality, Reliability, Usability, Maintainability, and Portability. The researchers conducted interviews, observations, and surveys to determine the objectives of this study. Mixed method research used as an approach to analyze and interpret both quantitative and qualitative data. On developmental research, a process was methodically studied, developed, and evaluated to ensure that it satisfied the requirements for users to accept the developed system. The research methodology utilized is Agile Software Methodology to develop the system agile process. To avoid direct involvement in long-term planning, the Agile development methodology divides tasks into smaller iterations. Using the software evaluation instrument, the weighted means ranging from 4.66 to 4.86 Strongly Agree, and the analyzed mean value of 4.78 shows that the developed system was Strongly Agree, and it is accepted as perceived by experts and end-users, respectively.', 2023, '	Lapiquera, Lemshie O. | Mendoza, Allysah G. | Nilo, Nina Ricci C. | Ramos, Katlyn Joy B. | Sabino, Wilmarc DG'),
(11, 42, 'BSIT', '	INTEGRATED POINT OF SALE AND PATIENT SKIN CARE TREATMENT SERVICE MONITORING SYSTEM FOR PS SKIN SOLUTION', 'In response to PS Skin Solutions operational challenges, this research introduces an Integrated Point of Sale and Patient Skin Care Treatment/Service Monitoring System. The goal is to revolutionize clinic procedures by leveraging advanced technologies for enhanced treatment monitoring, streamlined transactions, and personalized skincare services. ISO/IEC 25010:2011 criteria were employed to assess system acceptability. The system includes key features such as patient progress tracking through journaling, an efficient scheduling system, a streamlined point-of-sale interface, comprehensive sales analytics, transaction monitoring, and an informative dashboard for quick assessments. The evaluation results prominently showcased the systems excellence across various dimensions, including functional suitability, performance efficiency, compatibility, usability, reliability, security, maintainability, portability, and training/documentation. These findings underscore the systems effectiveness in meeting and even exceeding user specifications. The overall mean score was 4.34, indicating a very good performance level. In conclusion, the Integrated System promises to transform PS Skin Solutions operations and patient care. Recommendations include prioritizing cross-platform compatibility, user-centric customization, and facilitating integration in other clinics. This research significantly contributes to healthcare technology, offering an innovative solution for dermatology clinics to optimize operations and elevate patient care, emphasizing growth, sustainability, and excellence in service delivery and business operations.', 2023, 'Baltazar, John Denver M. | Bolante, Christine Joy | Dayao, Kimberly M. Glico, Benedict D.R. | Jumaquio Jr., Norberto M. | Santos, Hidie Ky | Villarin, Joemari C.'),
(12, 5, 'BSIT', 'AGRI-FISHERY MOBILE APP FOR BULSU-HC', 'The purpose of this study is to develop Agri-Fishery Mobile App for BulSU-HC capable of monitoring fish using water parameters such as water turbidity, salinity, temperature and dissolved oxygen. The system has the following features: Fish Information Management, Water Monitoring Management and Harvesting Timetable Management. The system allows viewing of the current condition of the water in the fish tank, It gives notifications if some abnormalities on the water are found and if the fish inside the fish tank is ready to be harvest. The system was developed using the system development life cycle. Android Studio was used for developing android application, Arduino IDE for coding the functions of all sensors, and for online development, MYSQL and PHP scripting language were used. The system was tested by the students form Technology and Livelihood Education and personnel from Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic resources. The Agri-Fishery Mobile App for BulSU-HC was created as designed thus, researchers recommend that the system may be used by BulSU Hagonoy Campus for it can easily monitor the status and condition of water and fish in the fish tank.', 2018, 'Manuel, John Padua D. | Maturingan, Ashley T. | Montero, John Jecsel A. | Perez, Mc Kenneth B. | Robles, Jose Emmanuel A'),
(13, 43, 'BSIT', 'SPELIDAD: DEVELOPMENT OF A FILIPINO SPELLING CHECKER USING MOBILE APPLICATION', 'The purpose of the study was to develop a Filipino spelling checker mobile application called \"Spelidad\" that helps users understand and improve their use of the Filipino language. Additionally, researchers developed \"Spelidad\" for improving Filipino users written communication, addressing issues related to spelling checker tools, which are relatively new in the Filipino language. It is developed using React Native, CSS, and MySQL using Visual Studio. It offers features like secure login and registration, personalized user experience, spelling detector and checker, Filipino word quiz, and a word of the day feature to enhance learning of the Filipino language. The system was tested and evaluated using ISO 25010:2011 by various respondents, receiving positive ratings in functionality (4.60), reliability (4.70), usability (4.62), efficiency (4.69), maintainability (4.72), portability (4.71), compatibility (4.82), and security (4.86) and with the total ratings of 4.72 \"Excellent\". The application benefited the users from Next Generation Technological College. Overall, the mobile application \"Spelidad\" effectively fulfills its purpose and excels in technical robustness and user-centric design, positively impacting the proper use of the Filipino language.', 2023, 'Borlongan, Gheimy G. | Caparas, Kris Anne C. Campita, Eldrin C. | Espiritu, Aubreylheane A.| Libor, Max Aurelius Y. | Maclid, Marishella Mae DR. | Reyes, Mico Kyle A.'),
(14, 33, 'BSIT', 'ENHANCING CAMPUS DEMOCRACY THROUGH DEVELOPMENT OF ONLINE VOTING SYSTEM FOR BULSU HAGONOY', 'The web-based voting system developed for Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus Local Student Council (LSC) represents a significant advancement in the efficient and secure management of student votes. This capstone project addresses the growing need for a streamlined electoral process by integrating essential features such as secure student login, a user-friendly voting interface, a candidate mission statement display, and a comprehensive administration dashboard for both regular administrators and super Administrators. To assess the systems quality, an evaluation was conducted using ISO/EC 25010:2011 Software Quality Evaluation Criteria. A diverse set of respondents, including students, IT professionals, IT instructors, and LSC members, participated in the evaluation. The criteria encompassed functionality, reliability, usability, maintainability, and portability. The research methodology employed in this project follows the descriptive developmental approach. This method is chosen to systematically examine and enhance the processes related to \"Enhancing Campus Democracy Through Development of Online Voting System for BulSU Hagonoy.\" Within the developmental research framework, the researcher systematically studied existing processes, strategically developed solutions, and meticulously evaluated these processes against predefined criteria. The primary objective was to ensure user acceptance of the proposed enhancements to the online voting system. Using the standard software evaluation criteria, the overall weighted mean of the study was 4.62 meaning Excellent which shows that the system was accepted as perceived by experts and end-users, respectively.', 2023, 'Acuña, Joshua M. | Alosa, Lemuel E. | Blanco, Mark Steven L. Halili, Jennylyn DR. | Lacsina, Catherine A. | Laruan, Adrian Louie M'),
(15, 0, '', 'WEB-BASED PSYCHOTHERAPY ONLINE RESERVATION FOR PSYCHSPHERE PSYCHOLOGICAL SERVICES', 'It is essential to examine the frequency of dangerous psychiatric conditions in a population during this pandemic and prevent psychological risks and repercussions. Unfortunately, there has been no research too far that looks at the psychological effects of the COVID-19 epidemic on the Philippines general populace. As things go, this research aims to discover the incidence of mental symptoms among social media users in the Philippines during the COVID-19 pandemic and to identify risk and protective factors that contribute to psychological stress. This website can help them have a companion wherein they can tell their problem because some don t know their situation to their friends, classmates, or even their parents. After all, maybe they hesitate because of anxiety. The World Health Organization (WHO) proclaimed the coronavirus epidemic on March 11, 2020. It could be similar to the 1918 influenza epidemic that afflicted one-third of the countrys population. Too far, the virus that causes COVID-19 disease, severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2), has spread to 213 nations and territories worldwide, resulting in 14 million cases and half a million deaths (WHO, 2020). Due to control measures, travel bans and restrictions have been enforced worldwide. On March 16, 2020, President Rodrigo Duterte declared an intensified community quarantine for the Luzon archipelago in the Philippines (Official Gazette, 2020). There were curfews, checkpoints, and travel restrictions (PCOO, 2020; Yap and Jiao, 2020). Business and school operations have been halted indefinitely. People have no choice except to remain at home.', 2022, 'Marjorie B. Ancajas | Danilo B. Ortega III | Jhona Vill T. Villarta Emmanuel N. Suarez | Framie Rose T. Robles'),
(16, 44, 'BSIT', 'SMART PLASTIC BOTTLE BIN: A REVERSE VENDING MACHINE', 'The research addresses the plastic waste issue in Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus by introducing the Smart Plastic Bottle Bin—a Reverse Vending Machine. The major objective of the study is to manage plastic bottle waste effectively, incorporating features such as collection, bin status notifications, web notifications for administrators, and grade-based rewards for users. The methodology employs a quantitative and developmental approach, utilizing surveys aligned with ISO standards. Results reveal the successful development of the Smart Plastic Bottle Bin, achieving an overall weighted mean of 4.59, indicating excellence. The system efficiently collects and monitors plastic bottles. Grade-based rewards incentivize student participation in recycling, fostering a sense of responsibility for sustainable practices. The generated income from collected bottles contributes to environmental projects, aligning with the universitys commitment to becoming a Dark Green University. Plastic detection and hardware improvement were recommended to the future researchers to further improve the validation for the type of waste inserted by the users. Expanding the scale of the study is also recommended to reach a variety of new respondents and to come up with another form of rewards.', 2023, '	Balmeo, Kyle Erol S. | Clemente, Aemee Nicole L. | Dela Peña, Noah Mark S. Roxas, Carl James M. | Santos, Rhiza Mae M. | Yap, Gio Edrian L.'),
(18, 26, 'BSIT', 'SOFTWARE SPECIFICATION QRAVIARY: SIMPLIFYING AVIARY MANAGEMENT WITH IOT SMART TEMPERATURE MONITORING AND QR INTEGRATION', 'Researchers introduces the state-of-the-art technology, the \"Raviary: Simplifying Bird and Egg Management with loT Temperature and Humidity System and QR Integration\" that uses IoT based smart temperature monitoring system and QR code technology project addresses issues with avian management focuses on temperature monitoring and inventory management for the birds for a convenient use and awareness of aviary condition. The researchers propose a mobile application and hardware that can be connected to each, which has features like statistical analysis, editing capabilities, bird monitoring, alerts, QR code integration, and login protection, makes record-keeping for bird breeders easier. The features that been mention will ensure and convenient use improves the information that can be use of the bird owners when tracking their because it consist of QR scanning that will redirecting them to the cage/bird easily it also consists images, id of their own and more this can easily prevent/minimize the error of the records it also secures the datas that the owners have. Implementing Agile Methodology, the investigation employed Kotlin, Arduino, and Firebase for the mobile application development. The researchers follow the five phases of the Agile Methodology to properly utilized and ensure the quality of the mobile application and its hardware. After the study researcher achieve all the objectives and successfully delivered the Raviary Management and can finally can be download for the bird breeders for the hardware have been deployed and also can be buy by other bird breeders. Utilizing ISO/EC 25010:2011 Software Quality Evaluation Criteria, the study assesses the system. The Raviary smartphone app and hardware the software and hardware are effective in addressing a variety of issues in the aviary environment, including inventory management and temperature monitoring, according to survey responses. The study concludes by showing how well the Raviary hardware and mobile application have improved aviary operations. The hardwares advantages and value highlight a thorough and efficient approach to addressing important aviary management issues, while the softwares positive reception and effectiveness contribute to increased functionality and efficiency.', 2023, '	Adriano, Li-yan Ma. | Evangelista, Christian T. | Dela Rezma, Zsarissa P. Gregorio, John Federick A. | Sangalang, Harold A. | Lacson, Zaccheus Elijah R.'),
(19, 7, 'BSIT', 'HYDROPONICS MAINTENANCE SYSTEM', 'The study aims to develop a Hydroponics Maintenance System for Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus. The system has the following features: Greenhouse Monitoring System, Water Quality Monitoring System, and Hydroponics Plants Information Management System. The researchers gathered information about hydroponics by researching and interviewing persons that have knowledge about hydroponics. The information gathered helps to guide the researchers in developing the Hydroponics Maintenance System that can be used by the Technology Livelihood Economics Students in their subject and by the future researchers that has the same study, also for those who want to enhance the system. After research and interviews, researchers learned everything that could be done to innovate the hydroponics system by using technology. Thus the researcher came up with an idea to make a greenhouse monitoring system, water quality monitoring system and hydroponics plants information management system. The researchers used the model-driven methodology to develop the system. It helps define all the requirements and design of the maintenance system by analyzing and visualizing the hydroponics owners problems. For the development of the system, the researchers use VB. NET for the design and functionality of the system so it can access the system and display the pH meter that monitor the level of acidity and alkalinity of water, to view the temperature of the surrounding area of greenhouse, and Reservoir to show the water level. SQL for database to store all of the information that be needed, Microsoft Windows 8 for the workstation, and all of the device will connect to Arduino IDE for the functionality of the system. The system was tested both the development and user environment to ensure that all the functions were working. Then conduct a User Acceptance Test - UAT, to see if the system is fully functional and ready to use by the users. The researchers recommend adding an SMS notification to notify the user if the pH buffer and nutrient solution containers are already empty. It helps the user know the containers status without the need for the frequent visit.', 2018, 'Yuuichi C. Buensuceso | Navy-Lhen A. Celso | Nikko Louise T. Delrosario | Rodolfo M. Malonzo | Aron Jobert V. Salim | Chandler P. Santos | Mark Rayson S. Victoria'),
(20, 39, 'BSIT', 'RISE OF THE HEROES:DEFEND AGAINST PHILIPPINE MYTHOLOGICAL CREATURES TOWER DEFENSE', '\"Rise of the Heroes: Defend Against Philippines Mythological Creatures Tower Defense\" is a 3D immersive tower defense game that sets the richness of history lore in the Philippines. The players task is to safeguard the tower against creatures who intend to destroy and defeat the player. The National Heroes are from Region IlI and the Mythological Gods or heroes are from the historical lore of the Philippines, and the creatures that battle against heroes. The tower defense game uses used Agile model, to follow its phases for development. Agile emphasizes the step-by-step life cycle for development. The game invites the players for an epic journey of the richness of the Philippines. It classifies the history and banded into the form of a game to entertain the players for the advantages and knowledge that the game gives to the players. This purpose is to get the attention of students or players to let them focus and learn about what the Philippines has.', 2023, 'Bautista, Juan Jerico D. | Dela Cruz, Shann Marc B. | Flores, Aries C. Manapat, Jerome A. | Narciso, Noriel L. | Santos, Janver S. | StaCruz, Kevinroy B.'),
(21, 27, 'BSIT', 'INTEGRATED DENTAL RECORD AND APPOINTMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CRUZ-PALMOS DENTAL CLINIC', 'The purpose of \"Integrated Dental Record and Appointment Management System for Cruz-Palmos Dental Clinic\" is to help the Cruz-Palmos Dental Clinic to track its patients data and schedule since the clinic is still using the traditional method, which is the paper-based system of managing dental records and appointment of its patients. The \"Integrated Dental Record and Appointment Management System for Cruz-Palmos Dental Clinic\" is a web-based system specifically designed to manage patient records and appointments in a dental clinic. It also focuses on providing an intuitive and user-friendly interface that simplifies patient record-keeping and can provide a dental record chart used by dental professionals to record information about a patients teeth and oral health. Also, the system can store and manage all patient-related information, including medical history, treatment plans, and notes. The researchers chose the Agile methodology in developing the said system since it has the ability to carry out iterative software development. Iterative releases help to increase productivity by enabling researchers to specify goals and identify defects early in the development cycle. The said system will help dentists to have secure data and a proper storing of information of their patients. Furthermore, the appointment system will provide both users with a more streamlined and conventional appointment scheduling process. On top of that, patients can request their dentists to access their dental records and treatment plans online and have the capacity to see the whole calendar schedule of their dentists and choose which date and time they want to make an appointment. In addition, patients may receive', 2023, 'Bucad, Lycka May M. | Cruz, Ana Kathlyn P. | Fucanan, Ranvie S. Gutierrez, Lean Danica O. | Macario, Marc Angelo D.R. | Manio, John Daniel M'),
(22, 31, 'BSIT', 'SKILL TEST: A WEB-BASED EXAM CREATOR FOR JAVA, C++, AND PYTHON', 'This study was developed to help IT instructors and IT students of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus in administering a prgramming examination. This study also aims to improve the existing system of Bulacan State Univeristy Hagonoy Campus in administering a programming exam. The system covers programming exam in Java, C++, and Python. This study also determined the advantages of using online IDE as tool for evaluation of exam for IT instructors. This study also covered resolving common problems and issues upon answering and evaluating an exam for both IT instructor and IT Student such as the need on installing an IDE to be able to run a code. This study was focused on ensuring the accessibility and efficiency of exam management for IT instructors. Furthermore, this study was evaluated using standard ISO/IEC 25010 software quality evaluation by its intended users and experts. Meanwhile, the researcher conducted observations, interviews, and surveys to acquire the objectives of this study. The research methodology utilized in this project was the Agile Development Methodology. The Agile methodology is a project management approach that involves breaking the project into phases and emphasizes continuous collaboration and improvement. This methodology is a paradigm for writing and implementing computer programs quickly, effectively and at minimum cost. This methodology also allows the researchers to go back at the previous phases for some revision and errors without finishing the whole cycle. Using the standard ISO/IEC 25010 software quality evaluation criteria, the overall mean of the study was 3.89 with descriptive meaning of Very Good, which shows that the system was accepted as perceived by its beneficiaries which is IT instructors and IT students of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus as well as IT Expert, respectively.', 2023, 'Bagalay, John Ernie L. | Crisostomo, Princess Angel R. | Dabu, Jeanryl L. | Eboña, Antonette H. | Goleña, John Ranielle A.'),
(23, 13, 'BSIT', 'SMART RESTAURANT: AUTOMATED SELF-ORDERING MENU SYSTEM', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a Self-Ordering Menu System for Potatonis Restaurant in Malolos Bulacan. The researchers gathered information of the entire activity of Potatonis Restaurant in Malolos Bulacan while observing in the restaurant premises, by interviewing and making a survey questionnaire on different personnel in the resto. The information gathered was properly documented and analysed which leads the researchers to develop the Smart Restaurant: Automated Self-Ordering Menu System. The methodology used in the development of the system is the Agile Methodology. This methodology helps the researchers to manage a project by breaking it up into several phases. This will help the team to visualize and improve workflows, reduce waste and inefficiency, and increase team focus by limiting work in progress. The researchers will conduct a system that will help the customer to select an order using the provided, and the cashier/admin will use a laptop for them to view and manage orders, devices, and menus. To develop the system that the researchers utilized PHP for the functionality of the system, XAMPP Server for the database, Microsoft Windows 11 for the workstation, and Google Chrome is used as the browser to access the system and display each individual web page. The capstone researchers successfully proposed a system that helped the client (Potatonis Restaurant) to their problems, it will effectively keep track of users orders, where customers may place an order or create a custom- designed meal with a single click. By using a self-ordering menu system, customers can go straight to the dine-in table, check the menu, choose what they want, and pay for their meal easily with your e-wallet. This system used ISO 25010 Evaluation Form to the IT Experts, IT Faculty, Customers, Staffs, and Kitchen.', 2023, 'BORJA, Marco Roneo DC. | DE ARCE, Erick John B. | DE JESUS, John Lenard A. | DE JESUS, Rossel M. | LAVA, Pette Zeimon N.'),
(24, 32, 'BSIT', 'HUMAN RESOURCE INFORMATION SYSTEM WITH EMPLOYEE PORTAL FOR BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY', 'This study introduces a comprehensive Web-Based Point-of-Sale (POS) and Inventory Management System designed for DaveTeo Classic Bike Shop, integrating Barcode Technology to streamline transaction monitoring and inventory control, addressing the challenges associated with manual inventory management in their operations. The researchers propose a web-based system to simplify inventory management and enhance pricing accuracy. The new system incorporates a Point of Sale (POS) feature that ensures precise billing for customers by automatically updating inventory levels through barcode scanning. This maintains an up-to-date database and facilitates online transactions through an integrated web shop, providing convenience for cusiomers and enabling remote business management regardless of the owners location. Implementing this innovative system is expected to boost efficiency, minimize errors, and elevate the overall customer experience at DaveTeo Classic Bike Shop. Employing Agile Methodology, the study utilized HTML, JavaScript, Bootstrap, MySQL, and Django Python, ensuring a robust and user-friendly interface for the developed system. The researchers employed a dual approach, incorporating both developmental and descriptive methodologies throughout the research, enriching the depth of the study and providing a comprehensive understanding of the systems design and functionality. The study successfully achieved its objectives, delivering a seamless POS, realtime Inventory Management, and a web-based platform accessible from any location. The ISO/TEC 25010:2011 evaluation substantiates the systems excellence, with an overal! score of 4.60, indicating an \"Excellent\" rating in functionality, reliability, usability, maintainability, and portability. In conclusion, the implemented system exceeds initial expectations, transforming day-to-day operations at DaveTeo Classic Bike Shop. Beyond immediate operational improvements, this research underscores the vital role of technology-driven solutions in navigating the complexities of the retail industry, projecting a sustained impact, and positioning businesses for strategic growth in a dynamically evolving technological landscape.', 2023, 'Garcia, John Luis B. | Geronimo, Anthony Nicky L. | Lopez, Russel G. Lugue, Cyra Reine L. | Marucot, Ranzel L. | Mendoza, Mac Mac A'),
(25, 40, 'BSIT', 'DEVELOPMENT OF LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM USING QR CODE FOR IBA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL', 'The main objective of this study is to develop a Library Management System using QR Code for Iba National High School to improve the management of library resources and streamline library transactions. The study utilizes a modified standardized survey questionnaire designed for evaluating database interfaces to analyze the descriptive data. The system was evaluated with the participation of fifty grade ten students, thirty-three faculties, and two Information Technology (IT) experts. The results showed that the system operates as intended and is capable of handling any user request without making any errors. The Scan Attendance Manager program was found to be a trustworthy program that teachers could easily use to check on students attendance by simply scanning the QR code affixed to each students ID. The findings of the software evaluation, which was answered by fifty grade 10 students, three faculties of IBA National High school, and one information technology expert, indicated that the library could utilize the Library Management System using QR Code to simplify laborious processes such as attendance tracking, planning, and the decision-making process, helping the library stay relevant and engaged with the school. This study is geared towards evidence-based practice using this type of computer system that will serve as a preference towards continuous improvement and work on the recommendation on how this system can be adapted in the school context.', 2023, 'Ken Andrew G. Borlongan | Jiewil Q. De Vera | Aira P. Domingo Anne Christine J. Llarenas | Andrei John B. Pallasigue | Mila Mae A. Pascual | Richard Glen DG. Reyes');
INSERT INTO `capstonebooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(26, 0, 'BSIT', 'LEARNING AND COURSE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM OF ASIA TOP VA', 'Virtual Learning has been used since early 2000s but only for the past two years when it has been utilized by almost everyone due to the rapid increase of COVID-19 cases. It has not only affected the health but also the natural process of education in the Philippines. March 16, 2020, when the government implemented the immediate Enhanced Community Quarantine in Central Luzon, it was initially planned to last for a week, but the number of cases becomes out of hand and lasted for a couple of months. During these months of ECQ, classes are suspended, and process of learning also stops. As a result, an alternative learning method was introduced to all academic institutions specifically in State Universities and Colleges. Online learning provides a way to escape the limitation of education by giving a way to still acquire knowledge without the need of physical presence in school. Therefore, the core objective of this capstone project is to develop a web-based Learning and Course Management System to allow our client company to conveniently manage, host, and track all the learning progress of their students. In terms of students perspective, enrolling in an online based class will give them a more flexible time. The website was designed to display all the offered courses - free and paid courses. Assessments are assigned in between lessons to identify if the learner studies the given topic. Once the student completed the course with passing grade, certificate will be automatically sent to their email addresses and can also be viewed in their dashboard - My Certificate tab. To test the effectiveness of the developed website, evaluation was conducted to thirty respondents using the software and data quality evaluation criteria. Technology acceptance model proposed that the key factors for a system to be accepted by users is when the system serves its purpose and if it is easy to manipulate or use. The result shows that most students learned more if they feel less pressured and can express their ideas more actively. One feature of the offered courses is it has an option of one-on-one training/lesson where trainers can mentor their students and help nurture their talents.', 2022, 'Bernardo, Jonalyn A. | Pangan, Maria Angelica P. | Reyes, Anniemae G. | Santos, Jorlie Marie S. | Santiago, Vincent SP. | Soteco, Eric John M.'),
(27, 34, 'BSIT', 'DEVELOPMENT BULSU HC HEALTH SERVICES: A WEB - BASED APPROACH TO ENHANCING THE SYSTEM FOR FACULTY AND STAFF IN BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'Researchers created a BulSU HC Health Services website to help nurses at Bulacan State Universitys Hagonoy Campus for faculty, student, and staff health needs. It is a website that makes it easy for university nurses to access health information of the University faculty, students, and staff. Also, it helps the university nurses not to consume a lot of time processing the inventory and summarization of the medicine. BulSU HC Health Services website is made just for the universitys faculty, student, and staff. It is made to be convenient for everyone who needs medical help at the university. It facilitates monitoring the health status of faculty, student, and staff. BulSU HC Health Services is different because its focused on making health services smoother for the university nurses. While there are other similar systems, ours is about making things easier for the nurses who use it daily. If this system gets approved and used, we hope it becomes a very important tool for the universitys health services. When talking to people who might support it, well proudly say we made it and explain how its based on lots of research and understanding what our university needs. We worked hard on this system, studying a lot and getting help from our professors. Our goal is to keep making BulSU HC Health Services better for the university nurses. Based on the evaluation requirements in user acceptance testing conducted by the researchers the system resulted in 94.63% completion. The website offers users the flexibility to access it at any time, provided their device is connected to the internet. This feature is particularly advantageous for university nurses, who traditionally document records on paper. In the future, other researchers might make the system even better by adding more new things to it.', 2023, 'Sacdalan, Kimberly Shane J. | Montemayor, Via Jane M. | Escarza, Jenna Marie J. | Angeles, Marielle E. | Soriano, Rendell S'),
(28, 23, 'BSIT', 'WEB-BASED PATIENT RECORDS AND SALES MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR HEALTH TRUEVALUE DIAGNOSTIC LABORATORY', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a web-based patient records and sales management system that will be capable of several features that will benefit the Health TrueValue Diagnostic Laboratory by providing them with an accurate record with sales and database system, The main purpose of the proposed system is to eliminate and reduce the time consumed in the manual processes including the logbook, transferring of results and records in the computer, and also filling up worksheets by developing a system. For developing the System, the developers used various software for creating the different parts of it the programmer utilized Query as a framework, phpMyAdmin as a database, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for the graphical user interface, and the researchers use Hostinger as a web hosting in developing the system. The database which will be phpMyAdmin shall support handling different types and various numbers of entities. It shall also allow the insertion and retrieval of data at any time of the day. To access and use the web-based site, software such as the windows 10 operating system is required, using a web application such as Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge, etc. To ensure quality, the game was tested for its Authority, Purpose, Coverage, Currency, Accuracy, Functionality Training, and Documentation through the questionnaire distributed to the 50 respondents. The developer used a scale of 1.00 as the lower or poor and 5.00 as excellent. The data reveal the system was rated \"Very Good\" in terms of Purpose (4.47), Coverage (4.25), Objectivity (4.08), Accuracy (4.36), Functionality (4.41), and Training and Documentation (4.32). The lowest rating is a currency that is rated as \"Good\". The Highest rate is (excellent) which is Authority with a general mean of (4.51). As a result, the obtained overall mean (4.22) indicates that the system is working properly and is recommended to use inside the office of the client. In order to eliminate and reduce the amount of time on manual operations like filling up worksheets, transferring results and records to computers, and keeping a logbook, the web-based patient record and sales management system for Health TrueValue Diagnostic Laboratory was created', 2022, 'Macabenta, Jerome F. | Fernandez, Joaquin Mark M. | Trinidad, Christine Mae S. | Reyes, Mark Jayson DC. | Tamayo, Paulo R. | Ignacio, Marphilip D'),
(29, 29, 'BSIT', 'WEB-BASED STUDENT PORTAL AND MONITORING SYSTEM IN ABULALAS ELEMENTARY SCHOOL', 'The Abulalas Elementary School is introducing a Web-Based Student Portal and Monitoring System to enhance the day-to-day work of students, teachers and administration. For the admin, the system includes a dashboard for displaying real-time counts of teachers and enrolled students, interactive charts and statistics, and a school map for all the rooms and buildings of the school. View the request documents of the students, update the enrollment which can also create an account for students, Add a new school year, monitor the location of the students, create an announcement and lost and found system. For students, the portal facilitates monitoring of the location of the students and attendance, alongside features for creating document requests, streamlining enrollment, and managing lost and found items. An announcement section ensures timely communication of important information. Teachers benefit from automated attendance tracking, access to school-wide announcements, and a dedicated space for monitoring their assigned students. The system also includes an administrative module for efficient school year management and centralized tracking of lost and found items. The integrated features aim to create a comprehensive and user-friendly platform for effective school management.', 2023, 'Arida, Yuto | Atienza, Mark Bryan Ayop, Arnel | Dela Rezma, Zsarinna | Martinez, Chloe Em | Nagal, Sherwin | Santiago, Enid Angelo | Umali, Ivan'),
(30, 30, 'BSIT', 'DEVELOPMENT OF A HEALTH CENTER MONITORING SYSTEM FOR BARANGAY SAN PEDRO HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'The purpose of this study was to provide a system called the Development of a Health Center Monitoring System for Barangay San Pedro Hagonoy, Bulacan, to provide a more comprehensive and integrated platform for the health center to monitor and manage the health status of the community. The system was built with JavaScript, HTML, and CSS for the front-end, while for the back-end, researchers used PHP and MySQL for the database. Also, the system has important features, which are an announcement board, record management, health statistics, and health mapping. These features help personnel and the community identify some important information. Additionally, to evaluate the system, the researcher used ISO 25010:2011 to test its functionality, performance, compatibility, usability, reliability, security, maintainability, and portability. Overall, the systems done with the important features.', 2023, 'Ayag, Jose Mari | Dela Cruz, AC | Dela Cruz, Lana Mae | Dillague, Keanu | Manzano, Ace Martinez, | , Robertson, Marjorie Simbulan'),
(31, 20, 'BSIT', 'CUSTOMER SERVICE MOBILE APPLICATION FOR AIRWAVE FIBERNET', 'The primary objective of this study is to develop a customer service mobile application, that will improve the management of client requests and concerns at Airwave Fibernet. The developed system also helps employees in resolving customer tickets more quickly. Employees can also access a list of commonly asked questions to answer to consumer concerns more quickly and enhancing customer satisfaction. The system will also provide frequent status updates on their tickets. The researchers gathered data to discover certain issues with the present system. It checks for functional stability, dependability, compatibility, usability, maintainability, and portability, which improves the applications development. The researchers develop the application to automate the Airwave Fibernet system. It will benefit both Airwave Fibernet employees and customers. This will enhance response time to customer concerns such as unit repair and replacement requests, bandwidth upgrade and downgrade requests, account, and billing statement requests, also accommodate the internet speed and latency complaints efficiently. The researchers work to provide a comprehensive solution to efficiently answer customer concerns by simply automating the complaint resolution process with ticket management to reduce the processing time for client complaints. As a result, the companys backlogs and delays will be reduced. Customers complaints will be resolved in less time than versus the previous system.', 2023, 'Absalon, James Mark G. | Areniego, Jan Jonelle B. | Cajucom, Emmanuel V. | Cruz, John Jorie M. | Del Rosario, Angelo Jio DC. | Manalo Mike, Laurence B.'),
(32, 0, 'BSIT', 'AN ECOMMERCE WEBSITE WITH SALES AND INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR PC VILLAGE', 'The goal of this research is to create an Ecommerce Website with Sales and Inventory Management System for Pc Village. Product Inventory, Sales Report Generation, Attendance monitoring. Sales Trend Report were all included in the system. In addition, the researchers created an Ecommerce Website to increase customer reach To obtain information about Pc Village daily operations, the researchers used a variety of methods. The studys principal data collection methods were on-the-spot observations and interviews. The researchers gathered useful information for the systems development using these strategies. The system was designed to make the entire Pc Village transaction as simple as possible for all parties involved. Pc village, owner, employee, and its customers. To make record keeping more accurate, dependable, and efficient Every transaction must be documented in the databases, and reports must be generated to provide the proprietor with a fast overview of the businesss state. The system was built with Microsoft Visual Studio Code, Xampp Server and Hostinger. For workstations, Microsoft Windows 10 is recommended. In terms of hardware, a printer was used to generate receipts.', 2022, 'De Leon, Jeremi | Engay, Gywl France| Faustino, Rafael | Jose, Lady Lyn| Lugue, Christian Benedict| Ramos, Eugene Joseph'),
(33, 28, 'Information Technology', 'ETERNALEASE: DEVELOPMENT OF A WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CHERUBIM OF HEAVEN MEMORIAL PARK', 'The Eternalease: Development of a Web based Management System for Cherubim of Heaven Memorial Park was developed especially for Cherubim of Heaven Memorial Park Inc. located at Purok 4 San Pedro Hagonoy, Bulacan, the system will help the cemetery challenges in manual information recording and management that includes paper documentation for files, reports lot pricing, record of deceased individuals, consuming valuable time in date retrieval and could be source of risk in document misplacement. The system added features that will help the cemetery with ability to inquire about reservation and make appointment for interment without physical presence and an interactive sight for the user or client side. The researchers used the ISO/IEC 25010 to evaluate the systems performance and functionality and Black-box testing to assess and enhance the systems functionality. The researchers used the Scrum Methodology to develop the web based system. It is used in software development across a range of sectors to manage projects where cooperation and adaptability are essential allowing the researcher to present the system to the cherubim and makes changes. Using the ISO/IEC evaluation the overall mean of the study was 4.51 meaning of Excellent which shows that the system was accepted and strongly recommend to use for the users.', 2023, 'Alfaro, MarkAngelo | Cuizon, Jennyca D. | Dearce, Adrian F. | De Guzman, Syd Derick Lorenz O. | Talucod, Ariza Joyce M'),
(34, 20, 'Information Technology', 'BULSU ITUGON SERVICE DESK MOBILE APPLICATION', 'The major objective of this study is to develop a service desk mobile application for Bulacan State University Media Relations Office, that can be used for providing university information. The researchers conducted a comprehensive study on the relevance of helpdesk systems to the students. The data was gathered to learn about the offices current system and to identify the problems with the current manual process, which led to the development of the BulSU iTugon Service Desk Mobile Application to improve the offices everyday operations. The researchers used Hypertext Preprocessor (PHP) for the web application of BuSU iTugon, Flutter for mobile application, Javascript as the client-side scripting language, and MySQL as database management software. The researchers conducted testing and produced test forms in order to determine if the system is efficient for use by the stakeholders and staff of the office. System improvements were recommended for future researchers to come up with new ideas to improve the system, such as making the mobile app available in the web browser and adding an offline feature to the knowledge baseboard so the user does not need an internet connection to browse in it.', 2022, 'Agustin, Eve Jaira C. | Magsakay, Evan Andrei D. | Payongayong, Jeremiah A. | Talucod, Mark Januel S.'),
(35, 0, 'BSIT', 'E-SEGREGATE: DEVELOPMENT OF WASTE MANAGEMENT FOR BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY - HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'The introduction of this machine will contribute to the realization of Bulacan State University - Hagony Campuss commitment to promoting an Environment Friendly environment, aligning with the broader university campaign. Dr. Felicidad A. Eleogo, the Campus Dean, is a steadfast advocate for the Go Green University initiative, encouraging eco-friendly practices such as caring for planted trees, fruits and vegetables, tree planting, and maintaining clean and safe university areas. The developed machine can be integrated as part of the Go Green Campaign, representing a worthwhile investment in projects that align with the universitys environmental goals. The developed machine aims to assist Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus, located at Brgy. Iba-Carillio, Hagonoy, Bulacan, in addressing its waste management challenges. Currently, the campus grapples with issues such as plastic cups, papers, and other waste scattered throughout various areas. Although the campus has implemented three designated trash bins labeled as BIODEGRADABLE, NON-BIODEGRADABLE, and RECYCLABLE, intended to facilitate proper waste disposal, the system is rendered ineffective due to human negligence. Recyclable materials, such as bottles and papers, are often disposed of in the biodegradable bins, while snacks and food waste end up in the recyclable bin.', 2023, 'Luisito C. Alvarado | Remiline M. Cruz | Jerico D. Cunanan | Jayanne Pearl T. De castro | Roan Adrian V. Matic | Philip Joshua DJ. Regalado'),
(36, 16, 'Information Technology', '	TIME SQUARE ENTERPRISE: POINT OF SALE AND INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM', 'The main access for Time Square Enterprise is inventory, where the management of stocks of product is necessary. This paper identifies challenges for reliable Point of Sale and Inventory Management with effective distribution systems regarding transactions and product availability. The companys data analysis regarding inaccurate and incorrect data during the inventory record is the foundation for the findings in this study. It identifies the main problem, outlines good practice based on Time Square Enterprise specific instances and recommends approaches to improve and enhance transaction system and product inventory management. The objective of the study is to develop a Point of Sale and Inventory Management System for Time Square Enterprise and integrate the following functions: Sales Management, Inventory Management with Stock Notification, Information Management, Sales Report Generation, Barcode Scanning, Printing Receipts, Sending Sales Report in Email, and Printing Sales Report in PDF format. In this study the researchers utilized the Agile Scrum Methodology under Agile Development Cycle of the Software Development Life Cycle which consists of five (5) important stages such as Ideations, Development, Testing, Deployment and Operations. The future research should explore and improve understanding for Point of Sale and Inventory Management, along with the utilization of new innovative technologies and incentives and digital transformation strategies to enhance the systems accuracy and reliability and hence improve the operations and processes of the Enterprise.', 2022, 'Alis, Merry Jane A. | Fajardo, Kris Jurist N. | Faustino, Paul Justine R.| Guia, Cassandra Tricia | Sebastian, James Emerson DC. | Suerte Felipe, Ericka C.'),
(37, 0, 'BSIT', 'AN ECOMMERCE WEBSITE WITH SALES AND INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR PC VILLAGE', 'The goal of this research is to create an Ecommerce Website with Sales and Inventory Management System for Pc Village. Product Inventory, Sales Report Generation, Attendance monitoring. Sales Trend Report were all included in the system. In addition, the researchers created an Ecommerce Website to increase customer reach To obtain information about Pc Village daily operations, the researchers used a variety of methods. The studys principal data collection methods were on-the-spot observations and interviews. The researchers gathered useful information for the systems development using these strategies. The system was designed to make the entire Pc Village transaction as simple as possible for all parties involved. Pc village, owner, employee, and its customers. To make record keeping more accurate, dependable, and efficient Every transaction must be documented in the databases, and reports must be generated to provide the proprietor with a fast overview of the businesss state. The system was built with Microsoft Visual Studio Code, Xampp Server and Hostinger. For workstations, Microsoft Windows 10 is recommended. In terms of hardware, a printer was used to generate receipts.', 2022, 'De Leon, Jeremi | Engay, Gywl France| Faustino, Rafael | Jose, Lady Lyn| Lugue, Christian Benedict| Ramos, Eugene Joseph'),
(38, 21, 'BSIT', '	TODAGO: ANDROID-BASED TRANSPORTATION BOOKING SYSTEM FOR SAMPJ TODA IN HAGONOY,BULACAN', 'The tricycle role in the public transportation in most of the cases it is a primary means of transportation, Whereas here in San Agustin, San Miguel, Palapat and San Juan Barangay of Hagonoy Bulacan is commonly used for commuting via tricycle the arise once in a while and the once is when you need it the most, the developer had solution to create an android-based Transportation Booking System called TodaGO a mobile application for hiring tricycle that turns the daily commuters as a companion. A smartphone with its location turned on required while using the application and connected to the internet needs a load to have an internet connection. With this TodaGo mobile application, is a new platform created for tricycle drivers and commuters in San Agustin, San Miguel, Palapat and San Juan Barangay of Hagonoy Bulacan with an option for efficient and more convenient public transportation. This idea is the progress of todays transportation scene in San Agustin, San Miguel, Palapat and San Juan Barangay of Hagonoy Bulacan toward innovation and modernization. The mobile application aims to provide a new opportunity for its users, drivers, and passengers. Hiring a tricycle for a ride can be more convenient for the passenger user through the new access to it through a smartphone with the install application and an addition to that is the transparency of details such as drivers reliability, estimated fare, exact location of passenger etc. The importance of those kind of information the most accessible and a credible tricycle driver for a ride transaction estimated fare are standardized, so passenger do not need to worry about the overcharge fare because it is written in the system and estimated it check the fare and exact location before they book and tricycle. Once there is a transaction, the user may converse through the built-in messenger that they can talk about it by using the message or chat. The driver is chosen by the president of the TODA who was responsible to take care of the passenger. This means more access to a comfy for the passenger to trust the driver. The driver will have an additional income by accepting booking for the passenger. And the more they accept and complete a successful transaction make them as a proficient driver of the tricycle TodaGo mobile application a result from the rating process by passenger for every finished transaction. Also, this indicates to the future researcher for a collaboration of angkas, wherein tricycle as mode of transportation and technology trend such as a mobile application. The concept of the project is mainly from an observation of daily concern of a person who is commuting. Hence, thorough research about the common public transport around Agustin, San Miguel, Palapat and San Juan Barangay of Hagonoy Bulacan which is a tricycle and then implementing it on a ride and improving wireless infrastructure nowadays. It is mainly observation of the developers followed by a thorough research and conduct of interviews additional to software quality evaluation. This resulted in the creation of TodaGo, a ride-hailing mobile application for the tricycle platform for its driver and passenger user. TodaGo application is an option for transportation that turns commutation as a companion.', 2022, 'Genesis M. Andres | Diana Rose D. Estrella | Joshua L. Montealegre Janathan James P. Obstaculo | Daniel M. Orot | Patricia Jhane V. Cruz'),
(39, 25, 'BSIT', 'PARKING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM USING RFID AT BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS: EFFICIENCY AND SECURITY', 'The major objective of this study is to have an organized parking area using RFID card for Bulacan State University that can be used to limit the vehicles entering the university. To begin the project, the researchers discussed the projects problem and how we will assist the Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus in resolving the parking lot and parking system issues. The researchers primary goal is to assist the school in providing organized and secure parking spaces for all visitors to the campus. The researchers discuss the projects scope as well as the schools limitations. By determining the scope and limitations, we can determine where the project can go and what it can do. The following step was to gather information from the others. Related research assists us in creating or idealizing how the project will look. We develop our own ideas by studying what others do. The researchers used Hypertext Preprocessor (Php) for the website of Parking Management System and Implementing RFID, Python to developing the website and software, JavaScript used both on the client-side and server-side that allows you to make web page interactive, while HTML and CSS that give structure and style to website page, and MySQL as database management software. The chapter 3 of our document will discuss the needs to perform, the features or functionality that must be shown, and the essential uses. The needed tasks or circumstances to establish a parking system at Hagonoy Campus are outlined in the requirement analysis. Here are the requirements that must be completed based on user ideas in the Requirement specification. Highlighting the functional and non-functional requirements Diagrams in system design indicate features and information on where it will come from and for what purpose. System development refers to the tools required to finish our project. It is described in System testing how we should test our system. The methods or steps to achieve our projects goal are outlined in the implementation.', 2023, '	Cruz, Jasper John Paul | Joven, First Patrice L. | Del Rosario, Laika Joi N. | Torres Jr, Jesus B.'),
(40, 2, 'BSIT', 'BROWSER-BASED INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR PRODUCTS AND RAW MATERIALS WITH PRODUCT RELEASING SCHEDULING USING BARCODE FOR M2000 IMEX COMPANY INC.', 'The main purpose of this study is to develop a system that is suitable and applicable for M2000 IMEX Company Inc. The researchers developed a Browser-based Inventory Management System for Products and Raw Materials with Product Releasing Scheduling Using Barcode that facilitate the proper way of monitoring of raw materials, products and finished goods. It provides ease of process in retrieving of information or records and keeps several reports. It also supports the first-in-first-out policy of the company through the use of appropriate barcode technology. The researchers developed a system which benefits the Customer, Production, Quality Assurance and Warehouse Departments. The system was developed using Model Driven Methodology. Preliminary investigation is conducted to identify problems, opportunities, and directives to fully understand and provide a solution. The researchers used the ASP. NET and MS SQL Server for the development of the system. The system was tested using the Unit, Integration and User Acceptance Testing. The developed system was tested through the test of modules and interfaces performed by the researchers and test scripts distributed to the Department heads, and resulted to 100% passed and completed test cases. By the use of these testing, the researchers concluded that the Browser-based Inventory Management System for Products and Raw Materials with Product Releasing Scheduling Using Barcode for M2000 IMEX Company Inc. can be implemented. The researchers recommended the hosting of the system and the use of mobile barcode scanner to maximize the monitoring capability and efficiency of the system.', 2016, 'Bautista, Renz Michael M. | Bulacan, Andrew Lloyd A. | Cruzado, Janine DC. | Magbitang, Rica T. | Manio, Jericson L. | Orbe, Marco A. | Seda, Mary Jane S'),
(41, 0, 'BSIT', 'BULSU HC: A WEB-BASED FACULTY EVALUATION AND STUDENT GUIDANCE COUNSELLING SYSTEM', 'The studys goal is to create a web-based system that will replace the old system, which wastes a lot of time and effort for everyone on the campus. Facuity Evaluation and Guidance Counseling were designed into the system. Reading University-related information, requesting vital documents, and publishing University-related announcements are all possible with the system. The Scrum Agile Methodology was used to create the system. The website was designed using HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap by the researchers. Javascript, Query, Ajax, PHP Scripting Language, and MySQL were used to make the system work. User Acceptance Testing (UAT) was performed on the developed system to allow end users to express their opinions on whether or not the developed system met their needs and met the specifications. It was put to the test by thirty-two (32) students, three (3) IT experts, five (5) faculty instructors, and two (2) administration personnel, and received a 4.57 (Highly Accepted) rating for meeting all of the systems standards and specifications.', 2022, 'Aguirre, Jasper Joren C. | Dela Cruz, John Francis T. | Fajardo, Jhon Edward P. | Vicente Jr. Danilo M. | Victoria, Ericka M'),
(42, 0, 'BSIT', 'WEB-BASED RESIDENT INFORMATION MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR BARANGAY SAN AGUSTIN', 'The objective of this study is to develop a system that is suitable for Barangay San Agustin to cope with new emerging technologies. The researcher developed Web Based Resident Information Management System which provides automated services like issuing clearance and permit, automated filing of residents complaint, gathering residents information through the use of Android Application which used to monitor Barangay Situational Analysis and Economic Profile and disseminating Barangay Information through SMS. The system was developed using the System Development Life Cycle. The researchers conduct preliminary investigation to identify barangay problems, opportunities, and directives by using Interview Method then the proponents come up with initial findings and established a solution to enhance the barangay transaction. For the development of the web application, MS SQL Server Express and ASP.NET were used. In addition, Android Development Toolkit was used for the Android Application. The system was tested in terms of its Performance, Users Friendliness, Reliability, Functionality and Security through the questionnaires distributed among 30 respondents. The overall acceptability was rated to be highly acceptable by System Users, IT experts and Non-IT experts. Based on the evaluation, the researchers concluded that the Web Based Resident Information Management System for Barangay San Agustin Hagonoy, Bulacan can be implemented.', 2014, 'Jan Michael Vincent I. Trinidad | Sherlyne S. Borromeo | Justin M. Flores | Paul Mark P. Miranda | Jia Mae N. Rubio | Jeffrey C. Valencia'),
(43, 22, 'BSIT', 'MOBILE DELIVERY BUSINESS APPLICATION: A FOOD DELIVERY START-UP APPLICATION FOR FOOD MALOLOS DELIVERY', 'The Mobile Delivery Business app for Food Malolos Delivery is designed to provide a fast and convenient way for merchants, delivery riders, and administrative staff to manage and track food delivery orders. One key feature of the app is its ability to facilitate quick transactions, which can help streamline the delivery process and increase efficiency. In addition to improving the efficiency of food delivery, the app also aims to enhance the overall experience for users in Malolos by offering a user-friendly interface, real-time tracking of orders, and other helpful features. The Mobile Delivery Business app was developed using the Agile Development Cycle, a process that allows for the continuous evolution of the product through the collaboration of cross-functional teams. The app was built using a range of technologies, including Android Studio, Firebase, JAVA, and XML. To evaluate the effectiveness of the app, the researchers used the ISO 25010 Software Quality Evaluation Criteria and gathered feedback from 41 respondents, including 1 administrative staff member, 10 IT experts, 10 sellers, and 20 delivery riders from Food Malolos. The results of the evaluation, which had a general weighted mean of 4.68 (rated as \"excellent\"), showed that the a pp is effective and successful. The researchers concluded that the Mobile Delivery Business app is a more effective and accurate solution than a manual system for managing food delivery orders in Malolos.', 2022, 'Bunton, Mark Robin N. | Cabantog, Tricia Lae S. | Calonzo. Arvin Y Jr. Caparas, Jomarck F. | Gamba, Ramzon Renz | Martin, Ezekiel T. | Santos, Marnie M'),
(44, 0, 'BSIT', 'FACULTY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR SAN PEDRO NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL', 'This project aims to develop a Web-based Faculty Management System (Information Management and Document Management) and Attendance Monitoring using biometrics with automated Daily Time Record (DTR) for San Pedro National High School (SPNHS). Faculty Management System can eliminate and reduce hardships of the teachers by changing the manual system. This system was developed by following the model-driven methodology. Web-based Faculty Management System was built using Laravel Livewire, Sublime, CSS, Bootstrap, PHP, and HTML, while Attendance Monitoring was created using VB.NET and MS Access. Digital Persona U.are. U 4500 Fingerprint Scanner was utilized to operate the biometrics. The researchers used Website Evaluation Criteria to prove the effectiveness of the system. Forty-six respondents (1 IT Expert and 45 Teachers from SPNHS) were asked to answer the evaluation. The general weighted mean of 4.66 (Excellent) proved that the developed system was effective and successful. The researchers concluded that a Web-based Faculty Management System is more effective and accurate than a manual system. In addition, attendance monitoring using biometrics is much organized and secured.', 2022, 'De Guzman, Mary Ann J. | Guioguio, Raymart P. | Omega, Ma. Rodelyn M. | Sandoval, Bart Simon G'),
(45, 0, 'BSIT', 'WEB BASED SUBSCRIBERS BILLING SYSTEM FOR HOMECHOICE CABLE TV, INC.', 'The major objective of this study is to develop a billing system for Home Choice CableTV, Inc. that can be used for an e-bill distribution. The researchers conducted interviews, observation and distributed questionnaires using descriptive method that uses quantitative data collection. The information was gathered upon knowing the current system of the company leads with a better solution to develop the Web Based Subscribers Billing System to improve the companys daily operation. The researchers used ASP.Net 4.5 Framework, Visual Studio 2012 as the programming language, Query as the client side scripting and MSSQL as database management software. The researchers conducted testing and provided test documents in order to check and evaluate if the system is efficient for the use of the subscribers and employees of the company. The system was noted \"Passed\" in terms of functionality and expected results using the user acceptance criteria of the system. System improvements were recommended for the future researchers to generate PayPal mode in terms of billing transaction and improvement of the SMS notification by replacing the USB modem to SMS Gateway API (Application Program Interface).', 2015, 'Aquino, Angelica C. | Eclarinal, Viel P. | Honrubia, Yowieh Harrah B. Layug, Mariel R. | Lagdamen, Yovelinda S. | Talucod, Jemuel Portia S.'),
(47, 0, 'BSIT', 'INTERACTIVE FOREIGN LANGUAGE TRAINER FOR COLLEGE OF INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATIONS TECHNOLOGY STUDENTS	', 'Filipinos are undoubtedly competitive worldwide; people of different ethnicities have seen many of them succeed in various fields, and harness plethora of awards through their achievements. One ingredient to a successful career is the ability to communicate well; to address the problem of misunderstanding amongst other nations, English has long been set as the universal language. However for the purpose of precisely communicating with the clients of different nationalities, professionals in various fields are often advised to study a foreign language. According to the book of Sydelle Seiger-Ehrenberg in \"Developing Minds: A Research Book for Teaching Thinking\", humans learn by connecting a new concept to what they already know. Connections in the human brain make up ones knowledge and skills, these connections determine how well one thinks. Hence, a faster way to teach a new idea to a person is the use of analogy. Interactive Foreign Language Trainer for College Information and Communications Technology (CICT) Students is designed to help the students learn from one or all of the four most commonly used foreign languages in the field of Information Technology that are included in the program namely; Korean, Mandarin Chinese, Japanese and Spanish, composed of set of words, phrases and sentences, the program is intended to quickly teach the students in the form of basic, intermediate and advanced levels. Audio prompts are available for every word and phrases in the program to aid in the proper pronunciation. Quizzes will also be given at the end of each training sessions.	', 2013, 'Cabrera, Abigael C. | Carasco, Raymond Led E. | Mesina, Abigail B. Oliquino, May S. | Reyes, Marien J.'),
(48, 0, 'BSIT', 'CISCO 1841 NETWORK TRAINERWITH E-LEARNING SOFTWARE	', 'The study focused on the development of \"CISCO 1841 Network Trainer with E-Learning\". The project was designed to train the users about networking; introduce a new way of interaction between the user and the computer, enable the users to enhance their skills regarding both basic and advanced networking, also preparations for the Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) exam for their future purposes- familiarized about the environments of a Cisco graphical user interface (GUI) and manually configures a Cisco network interface. Hardware specifications were considered an used as follows: 1841 Cisco routers, swant serial cable, console cable, UTP Cables, WIC 2T Module, power Cables and switches. For software specification, the proponents used Adobe Flash CS4 to meet the special effects, animation, and the code that is inputted on the software application that the proponents provided on the e-learning software. During the development of the project, different specifications were considered to have a good output. The proponents handed a list of hardware for its physical components- 1841 cisco router, Wic 2t Module, Console Cable, Swant Serial, Power Cables, 9-pins Gender converter Female to Male,CD-R King Switches and Unshielded Twisted Pair Cables. Adobe Flash CS provided the computer-aided-instruction that helped the user to be familiarized with the environment of designed network trainer and introduced lessons about the basic and advanced networking. In order to evaluate and assess the acceptability of the developed network trainer with e-leaning software, selected CICT faculty members and CICT 2nd year and 3* year students were asked to evaluate the project. Developed project was tested and evaluated by (45) forty-five evaluators consisting of (5) five CICT faculty members, (40) forty students in BIT Second year and third year students. The said respondents were selected in a appropriate section that was said by the research adviser. However to be specific, the researchers chose the 2nd year and 3à year students were enrolled in Basic Networking and Advance Networking. Presented in the table is the computed mean of each criterion in the CICT standardized tool for hardware evaluation. Functionality inputted 4.22 computed mean with an interpretation of \"Acceptable\". Reliability gathered 4.36 computed mean. Usability has the mean of 4.45 and maintainability with the mean of 4.39, portability with the mean of 4.32, workability with a mean of 4.33, Projects Safety with a mean of 4.32 and training and documentation with a mean of 4.42 which are all interpreted as \"Acceptable\" and the overall mean computed was 4.35 which means that the network trainer is \"Acceptable\" Presented in the table is the computed mean of each criterion in the CICT standardized tool for software evaluation. Functionality inputted 4.68 computed mean with an interpretation of \"Very Acceptable\". Reliability gathered 4.54 computed mean. Which is also \"Very Acceptable\" Usability has the mean of 4.09 which is interpreted as \"Acceptable\", portability with the mean of 4.54, speed with a mean of 4.63 and training and documentation with a mean of 4.59 which are all interpreted as \"Very Acceptable\" and the overall mean computed was 4.51 which means that the E-Learning Software is \"Very Acceptable\"	', 2013, 'Gian Franco M. Abrea | Paul Simon O. Bacasno | Angelo M. Dela Cruz | Joselito Joel D. Faustino | Herish P. Garzota | Aaron Rad. M. Manalaysay | Neil R. Mendoza | Christian Niño Padasas | Dennis S. Pangilinan | Reymare C. Robielos Kenneth M. Ronquillo |'),
(49, 3, 'BSIT', 'TAX REVENUE SYSTEM FOR THE OFFICE OF THE MUNICIPAL TREASURER OF HAGONOY, BULACAN	', 'This study aimed to develop a Tax Revenue System for the Office of the Municipal Treasurer of Hagonoy, Bulacan. The system contained the following features: Tax Revenue Management, Tax Report Management, Tax Payers Information Management, User Prevention security, Information SMS Notification. The researchers engaged numerous strategies to gather information about the operations of the Office of the Municipal Treasurer. The researchers performed interviews and observation in order to gather data and to know the daily transaction of the office. The system intended to make the entire tax transactions of the office and to give convinience to the main parties involve which are the Office of the Municipal Treasurer and Taxpayers. The system guarantees that the records are safe and accurate. The daily transactions and the data of the office are stored in the database. The system has the capability to generate reports needed by the office to monitor the tax collection progress. The system was developed using the Microsoft Visual Basic 2013 as the programming languange and Microsoft SQL Server 2014 for the database. The hardware requirements are Personal Computer, Windows Based Personal Computer used as the server, Broadband Modem inorder to send messages to the Taxpayers. LAN Cables and Switch for the network inorder to connect the client PC to the server. The developed system underwent testing process to ensure the quality of the developed system. The researchers used the two basics of software testing which are the black box testing and the white box testing. The developed system will be implemented in the Office of the Municipal Treasurer in Hagonoy, Bulacan. The implementation plan, contains the overview of the system, the tasks involved in the implementation, and the overall resources needed to support the implementation effort (hardware, software, facilities, materials, personnel, and any site-specific implementation requirements). The researchers concluded that the developed system can fulfill the needs of the office in terms of tax management. The system also allows the staff to send SMS to the taxpayers for the notifications which can reduce the expenses of the office. The researchers also recommends to the Office of the Municipal Treasurer of Hagonoy, Bulacan to use the Tax Revenue System in their daily transactions.	', 2016, 'Mendoza, Vladymer R. | Almazan, Kevin I. | Angeles, Ezekiel E. | Finez, Rodelyn DC. | Legaspi, Crisan V. | Reyes, Dyever R. | Torres, Judie-Ann S.'),
(50, 10, 'BSIT', 'WEB BASED TRACKING AND COURIER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR BEACON EXPRESS CORPORATION	', 'The major objective of this study is to develop a system that will benefit and help the Bedacon Express Corporation from the daily transaction within the company. The researchers conducted interviews, observations, and distributed questionnaires using descriptive method that uses quantitative data collection. The researchers found various problems in their day-to-day business such as delay in responding to unanswered calls and texts, lack of necessary information, and delay of producing different reports. The Information was gathered upon knowing the current system of the company leads with a better solution, to develop a Web Based Tracking and Courier Management System for Bedacon Express Corporation to improve the companys daily operation. Web Based Tracking and Courier Management System aims at securing data and helps to increase operational efficiency. The features of the developed system are, the user can view the customer order history, has a tracking number that generate uniquely, can import and export data from excel, and the notification SMS text for customers. The system will help the users for easy tracking down of deliveries. Support for courier management that helps record on the basis information of deliveries. Optimize the security and validity of the number of delivery, and income every month. Uses less of time for the accessing data or information. All data or information that currently stored in the drawers or racks will be transfer to the database system that will be safely saved in the computer. The system is convenient for the users, because it is user friendly, the system is very simple, practical and easy to use and in storing and accessing data and information are uncomplicated. The system will automate some of the processes that user supposed to do it manually. The transaction become faster, all finding records activities will be done by the system. The customers wouldnt have to wait too long. And to prevent from losing data and information, the system will have its own backup system that will be updated daily. This developed system demonstrates the efficient and effective data tracking and courier management. It uses less of time for accessing data or information about the client and at the same time makes the process become faster. The system will help the management system more efficient, data consistency, and provide a comfortable and easily services for clients. Therefore, the researchers recommend the Web Based Tracking Management System to eliminate data redundancy errors and inconsistency of data.	', 2018, 'Jerome T. Angellano | Merely Mae C. Bardos | John Cris M. Santos | Eugene F. Tiongson | Adrian D. Villafuerte'),
(51, 1, 'BSIT', 'INVENTORY MANAGEMENT AND SALES TREND SYSTEM FOR APO APAZ GENERAL MERCHANDISE	', 'This study aims to develop an Inventory Management and Sales Trend System for Apo Apaz General Merchandise. The system encompassed the following features: Product Inventory, Sales Report Generation, Payment and System Security and user privileges. The researchers also developed a Sales Trend Report Generation to predict the future sales growth. The researchers employed various tactics to gather information regarding business operation of Apo Apaz General Merchandise. First hand observation and interviews became the primary data gathering method of the study. Through these methods, the researchers obtained relevant information in developing the system. The system intended to make the entire transaction in Apo Apaz General Merchandise convenient to all parties involved: Apo Apaz General Merchandise and its customers. To make record keeping reliable, accurate and fast. Every transaction has to be recorded in the databases. Report generation is also included in order to give the proprietor a quick over review of the business status. The system was developed using ASP.Net and MSQL Server Management Studio for constructing the system and for database. Microsoft Windows 7 for the workstation. As for hardware, barcode scanner was used for reading the barcode and thermal printer for receipt generation.	', 2015, 'Agustin, Michael B. | Capili, Christiana Jayne D.C.| Dela Cruz, Nohr Monique P. | De Leon, Erwin R.| Dy, Mark Francis H. | Paguia, Rommel M.');
INSERT INTO `capstonebooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(52, 0, 'BSIT', 'MY.BULSU HAGONOY CAMPUS WEB PORTAL FOR BULSU-HAGONOY CAMPUS	', 'The Objective of this study is to develop a system that is appropriate for Bulacan State University- Hagonoy Campus. The researchers developed a Web Portal which benefit the student, faculty and the campus administration. The Web Portal can keep the student updated to the different announcements, information, and events of the University. It can also provide convenient way of accessing information about their academic records, facilitate easy communication with their instructors, and provide necessary educational information that can assist them in their school work. The Web Portal can also assist the faculty members to facilitate immediate communication to their students for any concerns and help the campus administration to disseminate the information to the whole BulSU-Hagonoy Campus community. The system was developed using the Model Driven Development. The researchers conduct preliminary investigation to identify the campus problems, opportunities, and directives by using interview method, afterwards the researchers come up with initial findings and established a best solution to improve the campus operation. The proponent used ASP.NET and MS SQL Server Express for the development of the Web Portal. The system was tested using user acceptance test through the test script distributed among the 50 students, 4 faculty members, and the administration. Based on the evaluation the researchers concluded that the My.Bulsu Hagonoy Campus Web Portal for Bulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus can be implemented.	', 2015, 'Alarcon, Camille A. | Alejo, Richard R. | Anib, Anabelle A. | Arellano, Glen Christopher E. | Enriquez, Crisel T. | Tiongson, Tyron Ed F.'),
(53, 0, 'BSIT', 'ROOM UTILIZATION USING RFID	', 'Radio Frequency IDentification (RFID) is rapidly emerging technology that has received much attention both from the industry and the academic world. RFID is continuously being introduced into different areas of life around the globe. This study was developed for the College of Information and Communications Technology as a mean of improving security provided by the college to the faculty and personnel. This project was developed by using Radio Frequency Identification system to monitor all the appliances inside the room and to be operated by the user. In this project, the user only taps his/her RFID tag for him/her to be recognized as a user. By this, the users are able to access the controls of each and every workstation and appliances in the entire room in which the project will be implemented. The study was able to produce a system in order to lessen the management tasks, to have efficient monitoring, retrieval and maintenance of its holdings. The study also helped the researchers to understand the emerging technology, implementation and methodologies of RFID which is a great help in the field of both Computer and Information Technology. After the study has been made, it was evaluated by several respondents. These include technical consultants, students from Bulacan State University particularly in the College of Information and Communication Technology and the faculty members of the entire college. The project was evaluated based on the following criteria; Functionality, Reliability, Usability, Maintainability, and Portability. These criteria were used to determine the acceptability of the project. And the evaluated forms were computed if the project was accepted based on the university standard.	', 2013, 'Areja, Cedric G. | Bautista, Jericson D.| Carpio, Allan T. | Florentino, Darwin G. | Gramo, Kim A. | Ramos, Arcel John C. | Regalado, Ronnel P.'),
(55, 0, 'BSIT', 'KEY SECURITY SYSTEM USING RFID	', 'This study about the developing of the KEY SECURITY SYSTEM USING RFID. The project focused on the security of the keys, which will be used by the faculty members and to be used in the other facilities under the College of Information and Communications Technology. It is important that users know how to use the technological advancements nowadays, such as RFID system, they much no how to troubleshoot and how to fix possible problems that may occur either on hardware and software. The researchers concentrated on a Key Security System Using RFID. To make the Key Security System Using RFID for the CICT works better, the researchers choose a good specification for the computer system. For the main, RF reader, RF cards, Servo motors, Microcontroller, and a Touch Screen Monitor. For the program development of the project the researchers use Visual Basic 6 and Java. The system underwent the development method. This method consists of phases of planning, data gathering, analysis, system designing, system development and testing and debugging. To conduct the system evaluation, the researchers made use of survey technique to evaluate and asses the function and features of the developed system. In this survey, selected CICT faculty member, who are the major benefactors of this study, were asked to answer the evaluation sheet that will measure some indicators like functionality, reliability, usability, maintainability, workability, safety, and training development. Results of the evaluation shows that on each indicator the system was approved and met the standards, the overall mean for the acceptability of the Key Security System of 4.17 with an interpretation of \"Very Good\" by the users. This means that the quality of the project attains the desired and target output. To conclude, the system has the capacity to give reliable record of room users and can replace the conventional way of room viewing. For this study to further developed, the researchers welcome new ideas and enhancement to better improve the whole system.	', 2012, 'Christian James C. Banag | Norberto B. Bueno | Hadji Ryan S. Jumaquio | Mark Adrian M. Manuel | Darren John D.C Pantanilla | Mariza B. Ractis | Clarisse C. Santos | Greggie B. Santos'),
(56, 0, 'BSIT', 'WIRELESS MOBILE PROJECTOR	', 'This project focuses on the development of Wireless Mobile Projector. The researcher used two boards in making the transmitter and receiver such as PC to TV board and Media Player board. The device is capable of displaying data wirelessly through Radio frequency signal. It has 800 X 600 resolution and has a range of 30 feet in distance. The project will be an effective teaching aid for the faculty of College of Information and Communications Technology. Hardware development life cycle was used as a developmental method in doing the Project. The project was evaluated by distributing questionnaire to 60 respondents. The area of acceptability are divided into 8 criterion namely functionality which got a mean of 4.27; Reliability got a mean of 4.27; Usability, 4.42; Maintainability, 4.44; Portability, 4.47; Workability, 4.26; Safety, 4.25; and Training and Documentation, 4.46. The total mean distribution of the project is 4.35 corresponding to an \"Acceptable\" interpretation. The project reaches its desired output and the evaluators liked the developed project. And based from the output of the project evaluation the researchers made a conclusion: 1) that the Wireless Mobile Projector is usable for individuals where in the project dont give them hard time in setting it up 2) the project satisfy the needs of the evaluators 3) the machine is portable and not heavy because the researchers use aluminum as the frame of their enclosure and recycled pu casing as their base while for the transmitter and receiver the researchers use central board for the enclosure. The researchers recommend making usb as the source energy for transmitter to make it more portable and less electricity required and use transceiver that has higher quality for better displaying of data.	', 2012, 'Erika Ivy C. Cruz | Jameson C. De Jesus | Raymark V. Estrella Kevin F. Geluz | Burt Lemuel N. Manapat | Richard L. Manaoat | Mark Vincent B. Sanchez | Clarisse Sharmaine T. Santos'),
(57, 0, 'BSIT', 'MAGNIFIED ANALOG AND DIGITAL TESTER FOR BASIC SHOP PRACTICE: DESIGN AND EVALUATION	', 'The concern of this study is to design and develop a Magnified Analog and Digital Tester for Basic Shop Practice\" in order to help the BIT Computer Technology 1* year students to easily learn how to use multi-tester. The project has features which include illustrational panel and measurement display which is compact for indoor and outdoor use. The project is capable of measuring and checking AC volts, DC volts and resistance. In order to assess the developed mock up, the researchers conducted an experimental research. Selected section in the Ist year BIT Computer Technology students were divided into two groups, one group is the Control Group and received no exposure to the project, while the other group is the Experimental Group who have used the project. In this study, the Control Group was taught the lesson on Multi-tester in a traditional manner whereas the Experimental Group used the mock up panel board with multi-tester. Since there are 700 students in the said course, only seventeen percent (17%) of the total population were asked to be the study participants. To be specific, the researchers chose four (4) sections which composed of 30 students as a group. So, one hundred twenty (120) students participated in this research. Initially, for the Control Group, they were given a Pre-test and afterward the researchers discussed the lessons about Multi-testers, and the procedure of setting its ranges, reading voltages, resistance and capacitance. To be specific, the researchers demonstrated the actual measuring and reading multi-tester to BIT Comp. Tech 11 group 1 and group 2. After the discussion, the students were given the same set of exam which is the Post test and were asked to apply the knowledge in measuring and reading multi-tester. BIT 1J groupl and group 2 students became the Experimental group and were exposed to the developed magnified project with minimal guidance from the researchers. But before they used the magnified, the researchers gave them Pre-test in order to assess the initial knowledge on Multi-tester. After finishing the lesson, they were given the same exam as to the Control group which is the Post-test and were asked to use a multi-tester to determine the effectiveness of the developed ILS. From the result of the exam of each group, the researchers were able to determine which among the two procedures were effective and whether the developed project is also effective and can be used as instructional aid for teaching the subject. To compare the two procedures, the Pre-test and Post Test of the Control Group were treated using T-Test as well as the Pre-test and Post-test of the Experimental Group. Results were presented in Chapter IV. The level of performance of the students in the control group after employing the traditional method of teaching as well as the level of performance of the students in the experimental group using the developed BSP Magnified project were also measured and described using frequency, percentage distribution and grade scale system. Grade equivalent with descriptive interpretation were used to interpret the computed grades acquired by the students.', 2011, 'Joey E. Alzate | Karlo Antonio B. Cue | Magnolia L. Enriquez | John Loreto R. Libuet | Melvin D. Navarro | Ma. Elena B. Pangan | Aldrin Kiel DH. Reyes | Marvin Q. Reyes | Florizell G. Santos'),
(58, 18, 'BSIT', 'SCHOOL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM OF STA. MONICA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL DEPARTMENT	', 'The objective of this research is to create a School Management System for Sta. Monica National High School (SMNHS) to aid the school in managing student information and records. It also aims to streamline the process of obtaining student documents. The web-based platform for the School Management System at Sta. Monica National High School provides students with easy access to their educational resources, information, and services. This system streamlines daily operations, including student and faculty information, grading, and announcements, among others. The system acts as a centralized database for all school data, enabling administrators, teachers, students, and staff to make informed decisions with ease and efficiency. The system enhances efficiency and provides quick access to essential information for school operations. The researchers gathered data to discover certain issues with the present system. It checks for functionality, performance efficiency, usability, compatibility, security, and reliability, which improves the web application\'s development. The supporters found that the system is beneficial to the school as it streamlines the enrollment process, allows for attendance tracking, provides grade visibility, facilitates record requests, and offers precise information about the student based on collected data and feedback throughout the chapter.	', 2022, 'Cervantes, Alex G. | Evidente, Joshua DB. | Faustino, Daryl T. | Palad, Jaypee I. | Payongayong, Tristan R. | Santos, Carlo E.'),
(59, 0, 'BSIT', 'PIC16F MICROCONTROLLER SERIES SIMULATION PANEL	', 'The project focused on burning and programming selected PIC16 family with 8 to 40 pins and test its functionality with the use of mobile. It benefits those who are not familiar in programming and burning a microcontroller. In the College of Information and Communications Technology, only the InfoTech students have the subject Embedded System so the researchers developed something intended for the CompTech students. The researchers developed a PIC16F Microcontroller Series Simulation Panel for the CompTech student so that, they can have a simple understanding of what embedded system is and how does it work. The researchers chose the PIC16 family because they are the most common used family from the PIC families. The PIC16F simulation panel includes the PIC burner, PIC programmer and the mobot trainer. The mobile robot will test the functionality of the burned/programmed microcontroller. The researchers used PIC16F84A (18 pins), PIC16F876A (28 pins) and PIC16F877A (40 pins) for programming/burning. The PIC16 Family uses BASIC programming language. It is the simplest language and much easier to use. The project can also read program from other PIC family such as 18 families. The project is not capable of burning and programming simultaneously because it can affect the resistance of other components. Also ray of sunlight can cause intrusion to the sensor enough to limit its movement. The user will generate the code using BASIC language in the computer. Then the PICKit2 will serve as the interface for programming and debugging the codes. The burner will compile the codes to the MCU. After processing, the MCU will do the action that has been directed by the MCU. The project was evaluated by selected students form BulSU, selected faculty members and Professionals outside the campus with the following criteria; Functionality, Reliability, Usability, Maintainability, Portability, Workability, Safety and Training and Documentation. Base on the surveys that the researchers had conducted, the project is acceptable. After analyzing the result of the evaluation, it has been proven that the developed project can accommodate the needs of the target users. This project will be more functional if the future user will implement it as a whole not just a prototype.	', 2011, 'Kevin Wilson P. Asuro | Angeli V. Bagsik | Arturo A. Buensuceso | Mariza P. Giganto | Elmerson T. Gonocruz | Michelle C. Ladera | Eydrian I. Magkasi | Jenielyn B. Magsakay | Michael Angelo A. Marasigan | Joseph Reynald S.P. San Pedro | Shyrene Joy C. Vida'),
(60, 0, 'BSIT', 'ONLINE ORDERING AND INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM OF GOLD PLACE PH STA. MARIA, BULACAN	', 'The capstone researchers propose Gold Place Ph to help them have their own website to sell and market their business. The inventory management system will help them organize and handle all the data and reduce the work. They have been using all these platforms to manage their business for almost two years. Gold Place PH is an online jewelry shop. Their office is located in Sta. Maria, Bulacan. It has been a trusted seller of 18-karat Saudi gold jewelry since 2020. The methodology we use is Agile Development for planning, requirements analysis, design, coding, testing, and implementation of this project. The software and languages we use to develop this system are HTML, CSS, PHP, and JavaScript for the design and functions of the system Microsoft Visual Studio, MySQL, XAMPP, GitHub, GoDaddy, and Google chrome for the platforms to execute the code. The evaluation criteria, we use the ISO 25010. We have 30 respondents to evaluate our system. The total of every part of the questions are for the Functional suitability with the mean of 4.75 described as excellent, for performance efficiency with the mean of 4.38 described as very good, for compatibility with the mean of 4.38 described as very good, for the usability of the system, the mean is 4.63 described as excellent, in reliability with the mean of 4.41 described very good, for the security with the mean of 4.45 described as very good, fir the maintainability with the mean of 4.33 described as very good, portability 4.51 mean and described as Excellent. And the overall weighted mean is 4.48 describes as very good.	', 2022, 'Acuna, Jeremiah | Parole, Angelo | Perez, Mark Anthony | Perez, Cielo | Sinag, Ma. Richelle Ileana | Villarojas, Sharmay Ann'),
(61, 4, 'BSIT', 'WEB STORE AND WAREHOUSE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH E-PAYMENT FOR HAGONOY SPORTS INTERNATIONAL INCORPORATION	', 'The purpose of this study is to develop a Web Store and Warehouse Management System with E-Payment for Hagonoy Sports International Incorporation. The system has the following features: Ordering Management with E-Payment, Warehouse Management, Product Management and Order Management. The researchers gathered information of the entire business transactions of Hagonoy Sports International Incorporation while observing in the business place, and by interviewing different personnel in the company. The information gathered leads the researchers to develop the Web Store and Warehouse Management System with E-Payment which can be used in the day to day transactions by the Hagony Sports International Incorporation. The methodology used in the development of the system is the Model-Driven Methodology. This methodology helps the researchers to analyze and visualize the problems of the company, define the business requirements and design the information system. The existing system of the company was found to be inconsistent in terms of data entry specifically the duplication of data. Different departments produced different reports resulting to a negative effect in sales. Having this kind of system requires effort in handling data because it is prone to errors. More so, it is not secured. Thus, the developed system eradicates the problem for this will help the company to make records more reliable and prevents data loss. In addition, the system will help the company gain more clients because people now a days, are comfortable in buying products online rather than going somewhere for shopping. The customers can easily shop anytime and the payment can be made through PayPal which makes it more convenient to the customers. An SMS will be sent to the customer notifying that the payment was received by Hagonoy Sports International Incorporation. The system provides convenience as well to the company because when orders are posted by the customers, the assigned department can immediately view and check if the needed materials for the orders are available. Moreover, the system can generate reports to monitor the warehouse inventory and sales. To develop the system, the researchers utilized PHP for the functionality of the system, WAMP Server for the database, Microsoft Windows 10 for the workstation, and Google chrome is used as the browser to access the system and display each individual web page. The system went through testing both in the development environment and the environment of the user. The researchers recommends that the system may be used by Hagonoy Sports International Incorporation for it can easily handle the management of warehouse and selling of products	', 2017, 'De Roxas, Angelica S. | Dela Cruz, Victor Leandro R. | Estrada, Analyn P. Estrella, Nicaela Shein F. | Perez, Paul John T. | Tuazon, Mark Joshua G.'),
(62, 17, 'BSIT', 'MEMBERSHIP MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR SAMAHAN NG MAKABAGONG KABATAANG PROGRESIBO INC.	', 'The capstone researchers propose Samahan ng Makabagong Kabataang Progresibo (SAMA KA PO) Inc. to help them have their own website to easily manage its members information. The database management system will help them organize and handle all the data and reduce the work. SAMA KA PO Inc. is Non-Government Organization. Their office is located in Look 1st E/S Compound, Purok 2, Look 1st, the City of Malolos, consists of more than 200 members.. The methodology we use is Agile Development for planning, requirements analysis, design, coding, testing, and implementation of this project. The software and languages we use to develop this system are HTML, CSS, PHP, and JavaScript for the design and functions of the system WordPress MySQL, XAMPP, and Google chrome for the platforms to execute the code. The evaluation criteria, we use the ISO 25010. We have 30 respondents to evaluate our system. The total of every part of the questions are for the Functional suitability with the mean of 4.45 described as very good, for performance efficiency with the mean of 4.31 described as very good, for compatibility with the mean of 4.4 described as very good, for the usability of the system, the mean is 4.34 described as very good, in reliability with the mean of 4.17 described very good, for the security with the mean of 4.42 described as very good, fir the maintainability with the mean of 4.21 described as very good, portability 4.03 mean and described as very good. And the overall weighted mean is 4.29 describes as very good.	', 2022, 'Baluyot, Cris Laurence | Carlos, Lance Christopher | Prijoles, Angel Grace Reyes, | Cristine Joy Reyes | Justine Mae | Santos, Yla Nicolette | Uy, John Joshua'),
(64, 0, 'BSIT', 'ONLINE SCHOOL PORTAL SYSTEM FOR RAMONA S. TRILLANA SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL', 'The \"Online School Portal System for Ramona S. Trillana Senior High\r\nSchool\" is a web-based study initiative that will help the faculty and students in\r\nterms of process of the school wherein it acts as an information kiosk for students\r\nand faculties. The online school portal system can provide an efficient handling of information that is very easy for school to use since it is web-based and can be viewed from anywhere and at any time. The actual purpose in designing the\r\nsystem is to make the school process to get speed up. The overall benefit of the system is enhanced by reducing the latency that occurs while using the manual process. The computer-based architecture in this project was introduced using the\r\nPHP language, CSS, HTML and the software database as MySQL. This research work uses the compilation of data from the school, materials and the program has been designed to accomplish the project objective efficiently.', 2022, 'Arellano, Ronnel C. | Balita, Ronce Allyson P. |De Erit, Michole Joshua Y. | De Leon, Cristel P. | Payongayong, Marjorie S. | Raymundo, Alyza Claire R.'),
(65, 0, 'BSIT', 'Web-Based Health Center Information Management System for Barangay San Jose Hagonoy, Bulacan	', 'Currently, the Barangay San Jose Health Center employs a manual method. The healthcare workers are ineffective at doing their daily tasks since every transaction should be manually recorded and stored in a file cabinet. The proponents conducted a thorough investigation at Barangay San Jose Health Center and found various problems in their day-to-day transaction this includes the health workers and doctors are having a hard time working manually since the process of recording each patients data takes time. Due to the manual process used to collect patients data the healthcare professionals encountered inaccuracy when manually recorded patient information. The healthcare professionals also ran into issues with losing important patient records or paperwork due to manual data storage. In order to simplify daily operations at Barangay San Jose Health Center, increase productivity, and for the convenience of healthcare professionals and patients, the proponents developed a solution - to create the Web- based Health Center Information Management System. The proponents utilized the scrum and agile techniques for the project. It allows the client to participate in the systems development. Any changes or requests from clients are integrated into the developers specifications for the next version. This technique was used by the proponents since it is effective and flexible to any changes. The system was developed using a variety of development tools. The core development tools that were utilized are HTML, CSS, Bootstrap and JavaScript. Additionally, Python Django is used as the backend framework and PostgreSQL is used for the database in developing the system. Web-based Health Center Management System features the following significant functionalities such as registration and login, patient record management, generating of reports, appointment booking with email notifications, managing appointments, work scheduling, inventory of medicines, announcements, Q&A chat and restore are the features included in the system. The systems overall acceptability was measured based on the Software Quality Evaluation which has the following criteria: The system was evaluated based on its functional suitability, performance efficiency, compatibility, usability, reliability, security, maintainability, and portability. IT experts, IT Students, Midwife, Barangay Health Worker as well as the Residents of San Jose evaluated the system using said criteria. Based on the feedback from the evaluators, the system got general weighted mean of 4.24 which is rated as \"Very Good.\" In conclusion, the proponents understand the significance of the proposed system, which would help both healthcare professionals and patients. The proponents claims that the proposed system was created as the best solution to simplify all the tasks at Barangay San Jose Health Center. The developed system is incredibly useful for healthcare professionals and patients. Due to the systems simplicity yet well-designed, it is user-friendly, easy to manage and gives user helping functions.	', 2022, 'Currently, the Barangay San Jose Health Center employs a manual method. The healthcare workers are ineffective at doing their daily tasks since every transaction should be manually recorded and stored in a file cabinet. The proponents conducted a thorough'),
(67, 0, 'BSIT', 'FOOD PARK: A MOBILE PLATFORM	', 'EXECUTIVE SUMMARY Food Park: A Mobile Platform can assist you in determining which food park is the closest to you. This application can assist clients in learning about the food parks that are nearby as well as small business owners who run stalls or less well-known food parks. This will be advantageous for them in that lots of people would see their business on this application, which would even have helped them become well-known business owners. Small company owners and people of all ages will be the target market for our team. This application can be used in rural, suburban, and urban areas if cellular networks and wireless networks are available. This will be a fantastic application for people who appreciate trying new foods, going on food hunts, and writing food blogs. This app is for anyone of any age who wants to try new cuisines. The application that we developed is one that has never been done before; while some of its functions may be comparable to those of other apps, we created it with the goal of assisting small stall owners in becoming renowned. If this application is approved, it may be turned into a new firm. If investors inquire as to who is behind this application, we will gladly and confidently state that we created it, and we will assure them that the research and application developed will match the clients expectations. This research was created after many sleepless nights, extensive investigation, sweat and tears, and with the assistance of our professors. We intend to enhance this application gradually but steadily. The system resulted in 81.15 % completion based on the evaluation requirements in user acceptance testing conducted by the researchers. The system has a map that shows the available food parks in Bulacans district 1. It has a map marker with an information window that shows the available stalls. On the other hand, the application allows food park owners to upload their stalls and further information to it including the menu and contact information. Future researchers may add further developments to the system.	', 2022, 'Jaimee Lyka C. Baisa | Nicole B. Bernal | John Francis S. Candaza | Sarah Hazel Moces S. Pulumbarit');
