INSERT INTO `thesisbooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(1, 17, 'BSHM', 'WORKPLACE ENVIRONMENT AND JOB PERFORMANCE OF EMPLOYEES IN SELECTED FAST FOOD IN MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'Workplace Environment and Job Performance of Employees in Selected fast food in Malolos, Bulacan was conducted to know the factor of job performance of the employees based on their workplace environment. In these studies, it discussed three parts of condition in workplace environment namely: mental condition, ergonomic condition and indoor condition. many things can discover to the employees who was working in the fast food. And all the problem that we had given to the worker was answering in the good way and honestly. And the result of this study will help to other researcher, and they will help too in the employees who was working in the fast food and how workplace environment can simply affect their job performance. Even our theory they help in our research, because they determine all the data or gathering a information. According to O\'Neill & Davis, 2011, This high turnover is attributed to a lack of job satisfaction, and it is thought that the hospitality industry\'s explosive growth has resulted in stress and work overload\r\nKeywords: Workplace, Job performance, Fast Food\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Crisostomo, Ceazar Ian O. | Deimos, Mariel | Perez, Jerico| Perez, Joyce | Pineda, Renz | Santos, Dana Clarisse'),
(2, 21, 'BSHM', 'TEAMBUILDING INITIATIVES AS TOOL IN INCREASING MOTIVATION AND EMPLOYEES\' PRODUCTIVITY IN THE FOOD SERVICE SECTOR', 'Successful teamwork doesn\'t work overnight, what makes teamwork potent is team building. (Plagiarism) According to Abdullah, et. al., (2022) team building training can improve group cohesiveness or the quality of sticking together or unity teamwork more likely to be higher with a significant score difference. This study used mixed methods both qualitative and quantitative data collection, and an analysis method to answer the research method, random sampling is named as such because the data set is chosen via random selection, where every member of the population has an equal probability of being selected (Tao, 2023). The respondents were 100 restaurant employees and 10 managers from the chosen restaurant in Malolos City in Bulacan. The subcategories of team building, including activities, communication, skills, personality, problem-solving, and values, have all received a consensus of strong agreement, with weighted averages falling within the range of 3.26 to 3.44. This level of agreement aligns with the scores for motivation at 3.43 and productivity at 3.38. These values have been calculated by determining the mean, which spans from 3.25 to 4.00. The advantages of team building that is being observed by the managers is to create familiarity and teamwork among the employees, to improve the quality of service and the quality of the food especially the respondents are in the food service sector, development, and training for the employees to achieve the establishments\' goal and lastly rebuilding and build a relationship with one employee to another. However, for the disadvantages, it costs a lot of money to conduct team building in the management. Therefore, the null hypothesis is rejected. Despite the fact that there is a low correlation between teambuilding activities and motivation and employee productivity, there is still a significant relationship between\r\nthe variables. \r\n\r\nKeywords: teambuilding initiatives, motivation, productivity, random sampling, food service sector, correlation\r\n', 2022, 'Locsin, Decie Claire A. | Marasigan, Arvin A. | Martin, Jenny Rose H.| Miralles, Mark Angelo L. | Ramos, Allyssa Marie B.'),
(3, 32, 'BSHM', 'THE EFFECT OF DIGITAL MARKETING ON CONSUMER DECISION IN RESORTS', 'This study was conducted to evaluate The Effect of Digital Marketing in Resort. It\r\nuses descriptive research methods. This is covered by 71 random respondents utilizing the study questionnaire and assessed by experts from the course.\r\nDuring the current research period, the weighted mean was employed to estimate client satisfaction in the selected resorts in Hagonoy, Bulacan. The descriptive analysis of the procedure was carried out using Descriptive Statistics, which were utilized to simply describe what data was received from the respondents in the study.\r\nThe findings revealed the participants\' responses in terms of Client Satisfaction in\r\nthe selected resorts in Hagonoy, Bulacan. In the collected data, it is based on the people who visit different resorts or experience different types of digital marketing. Out of 71\r\nrespondents, 55, or 77.5% are clients, 10 or 14.1% are employees, and the remaining 6 or 8.5% are owners of the resort. Findings show that the most effective digital marketing strategy is social media rely on Digital Marketing has a 40.8% or 29, the second highest percentage is influence marketing that has 23.9% or 17, and the least effective digital marketing tool according to respondents is pay-per-click optimization which has 0%.\r\n', 2023, ' Bautista, Beverlyn B.| Jimenez, Raymart G. | Santiago, Lara C. | Santos, Ryka Diane L.'),
(4, 0, '0', 'EFFECTIVENESS OF ONLINE MARKETING STRATEGIES IN THE SELECTED FAST FOOD CHAIN IN MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'To accomplish its marketing objectives, Online Marketing Strategies makes use of digital\r\ntechnologies and additional online advertising tools. Modern businesses depend heavily on online ordering to stay competitive and retain sales.\r\nFor fast food companies, putting an online order is advantageous as well, as it saves time and effort compared to in-person visits. Fast food chains will benefit from the opposite side as well, as it will raise income and present an opportunity to grow the firm.\r\nThis study contributes to our understanding of whether online ordering is satisfactory for customers. The influence of internet marketing on customer purchasing decisions is also measured by this study. This research paper focuses on the Effectiveness of Online Marketing Strategies in the Selected Fast food chains in Malolos, Bulacan.\r\nKeyword : Online Marketing, Fast Food, Satisfaction\r\n', 2022, 'DOMINGO, JHANE DARREL D.| LOMOTAN, REGINA D.| BUENAVISTA, KYLA EUNICE P. | RAMOS, ARLHIE JOHANNES L.'),
(5, 29, 'BSHM', ' DEVELOPMENT OF UNTILIZATION OF CUSTARD APPLE TO PRODUCEFRUIT CANDY', 'The Custard Apple or \"Cherimoya\" is vert abundant here in the Philippines because we are one of the tropical countries. The said fruit can be found to almost every rural place in the country. It is enjoyable to taste because of its sweet and creamy texture. The researchers target to use Custard Apple as the main ingredient on making a soursop candy to make it of a use and for the fruits do not go to waste on its every season. Furthermore, the researchers\' targets to attract ages 12 and\r\nbelow for it is a candy that is very enjoyable to many children.\r\n', 2022, 'Buensuceso Diana T. | Coronel Robin S. | Hernandez Elaine F. | Precilla, John Kenneth DJ. | Vistan Christopher P.'),
(6, 22, 'BSHM', 'TO GO OR NOT TO GO: ROLE OF ONLINE REVIEWS TOWARDS CUSTOMER DINING INTENTIONS', 'The objective of this study is to investigate the role of online reviews towards customer dining intention in casual dining restaurants. Specifically, this study sought to answer the\r\nquestions (1) How does online reviews affect customer casual dining intentions? (2) What are the attributes of online reviews that greatly influence customer dining intention?, and (3) What is the extent of the effect of online reviews on customer casual dining intentions?\r\nThe research was carried out in the city of Malolos, Bulacan, and respondents are\r\nMalolos residents who have dined at a casual dining restaurant at least once and who chose a\r\nrestaurant based on online reviews. Descriptive Quantitative research was utilized in the study.\r\nAn adapted questionnaire from the study of Thomas, et al. (2019) was used and a random\r\nsampling method was employed to gather 100 respondents. Most respondents agreed that\r\nonline reviews affect customers\' casual dining intentions. A closer look at the study reveals\r\nthat all proposed online review attributes greatly influence customer dining intention. This agreed with the previous study by Thomas et al. (2019), where the identified factors were derived. Product/ service rating, website reputation, and review quantity show the strongest positive effects.\r\nKeywords: customer dining intention, online reviews, E-wom, hospitality industry:\r\n', 2022, 'ALLANIGUE, Mark Joseph S. | ZABALLA, Alisandra V. | ZAPATA, Christian Sherwin S. | ZAPATA, Christine S.'),
(7, 20, 'BSHM', 'FACTORS INFLUENCING ONLINE IMPULSIVE PURCHASES AMONG HOSPITALITY MANAGEMENT STUDENTS', 'Technology has significantly changed the shopping experience, particularly when they shop online using digital platforms. Online purchasing has become an alternative way of purchasing a product or service. The internet is rapidly becoming a significant shopping channel, with growth rates surpassing all other forms of shopping (Brohan, 2007).\r\nThis study aimed to determine the factors affecting impulsive purchases of Bachelor\r\nof Science in Hospitality Management working students from Hagonoy Campus because of online platforms and to determine how they are affected because of impulsive buying.\r\nThe dependent variable of the study is the factors influencing impulsive online purchases, while the independent variable of the study is the working students of Hospitality Management.\r\nA quantitative research method is used in this study. The quantitative research approach is to quantify data collecting and analysis. To find out the solution to different problems in this study, this study used a Likert scale questionnaire, distributed to 50 participants of 1st to 4th-year BSHM working students of the Hagonoy Campus. The questionnaire consists of Profiles of the Respondents Tendency to impulsive purchase, Tendency to enjoy shopping, Students Mood, Web page design of the online shop, Seller promotional activities, and Product characteristics.\r\nThe researchers recommend supporting this study to make this studying today more convenient for working students who are experiencing impulsive buying in different online shops.\r\nKeywords: Impulsive purchases, product, digital platforms, factors influencing, online\r\nshops.\r\n', 2022, 'BORROMEO, Rizalie G. | CHICO, Christian Angelo S. | CHICO, Ronnie B.| DELA CRUZ, Mark Bryan R. | LUCAS, Michael Florence F.'),
(8, 26, 'BSHM', ' INFLUENCE OF CURRENT DINING TRENDS IN CUSTOMERS BEHAVIOR', 'This study explores the intricate connection between contemporary dining trends and customer behavior within the food service industry. Given the constantly shifting landscape of culinary preferences, technological advancements, and societal changes, it is essential for businesses aiming to maintain competitiveness to comprehend the impact of present dining trends on consumer choices and behaviors. The research employs a\r\ncomprehensive approach, utilizing both qualitative and quantitative methods, to scrutinize the fundamental factors that shape customer behavior in response to prevalent\r\ndining trends.\r\nThe primary objectives of the research include the identification and examination\r\nof various elements that contribute to the current dining environment. These elements\r\nencompass, but are not limited to, the increasing prevalence of food delivery platforms, the growing popularity of sustainable and locally sourced ingredients, the influence of social media on dining preferences, and the emergence of innovative dining concepts.\r\nThrough the investigation of these trends, the study seeks to reveal their impact on customer decision-making processes, preferences, and brand loyalty.\r\nMoreover, the research delves into the practical implications for businesses operating in the food service sector. It provides insights into how industry participants can adjust their strategies to align with evolving consumer expectations. The anticipated findings of this study are poised to furnish valuable knowledge to the field, offering actionable recommendations for restaurateurs, marketers, and policymakers seeking to navigate and capitalize on the dynamic changes within the modern dining landscape. The researchers choose quantitative research. Quantitative research is referred to as a systematic investigation of phenomena by gathering quantifiable data and performing statistical, mathematical, or computational techniques.\r\nThe respondents for this study are one hundred Hospitality Management students of Bulacan State University who cooperated unselfishly to gather the data needed for this research study.\r\nTo answer statistically the specific questions, the researcher used statistical tools like frequency count, percentage and mean. For accurate mathematical computation of the\r\nnumerical data, they used computer programs like EXCEL.\r\nBase on the findings of the study, it shows that most of the Hospitality\r\nManagement students are aware of the current dining trends popular in the province of\r\nBulacan. And they are more likely go to or queue up at ghost kitchens is because they prefer convenient. By observing and analyzing to their response they do enjoy trying and dining in a restaurant that is popular, the researchers also provide a conclusion to\r\nconclude the possible result of this study and recommendation to suggest more and to have an improvement.\r\n', 2022, 'Alincastre, Michael Angelo Gumabat| Cabantog, Kenneth Angelo Raymundo| Castro, Timothy Llegue | Santiago, John David Dela Cruz'),
(9, 10, 'BSHM', 'Best Practices of Selected Resorts in Hagonoy, Bulacan: Basis for Sustainability', 'The study focuses on the green practices of prominent tourist sites in Hagonoy,\r\nBulacan, especially resorts, by giving best practices for one resort that outperforms others in the region. The researcher aims to improve services by developing a resort in Hagonoy, Bulacan. The purpose of this research is to determine whether resort practices will boost the areas recreational value and economic advantages. This study was measured utilizing a survey form, and the researcher used a Pie Chart to show a somewhat favorable association. There were 50 responders who have visited resorts in Hagonoy, Bulacan. This research may be useful for existing and prospective resort owners to understand some successful best practice strategies that may help them make a lot of income. The findings indicate that there is a relatively favorable association between operation and service offered. To summarize, a resorts best practices have an influence on its profitability.\r\n', 2022, 'Andea, Jhumel B. | Andico, Jasmin A. | De Jesus, Danica M. | Durante, Angela B.'),
(10, 27, 'BSHM', 'A CORRELATIONAL STUDY ON THE ADVERTISING STRATEGIES OF HAGONOY-BASED SELLERS IN FACEBOOK MARKETPLACE AND ITS IMPACT ON THE REVENUE OF THE BUSINESS', ' This study was conducted on the area of Hagonoy, Bulacan, Philippines. Through different advancement that the innovative technology has bring in the world, everything has been made possible. Daily transactions like shopping that requires us to make effort before, can now be done in just few clicks away. The aim of this study is to find out if Advertising Strategies correlate with the Revenue of Online Sellers through the use of Facebook Marketplace. This study is measured using survey form and the researcher use Pearson\'s r Data Analysis to reveal moderately positive correlation in this study. The respondents were 70 online sellers from Hagonoy, Bulacan. This study may be beneficial to current and future online seller to learned some effective advertising strategy that can help to gain a lot of profit. The finding shows that there is moderately positive correlation between advertising strategy and business profitability. To conclude, the advertising strategies has an impact to the revenue of the business.\r\nKeywords: Facebook Marketplace, Pearson\'s r, Revenue, Advertising Strategies\r\n', 2022, 'ESCALERA, Djenne Marc L. | NUQUI, Nivea S.REYES, John Elize Q. | ROBLES, Krisha Mae C. | TOLENTINO, Karen F.'),
(11, 1, 'BS HRM', 'FACTORS AFFECTING RESORT SERVICES AND ITS CUSTOMER SATISFACTION IN BULAKAN, BULACAN', 'This study was designed to determine the factors affecting hotel and resort services\r\nand its customer satisfaction in bulacan, bulakan. It sought to describe The demographic profiles includes for the customer includes for the Age, Gender and Civil Status employee age, Gender, Civil Status, Educational Background and Seminar attended includes that might influence the way they utilized the study.\r\nThe descriptive type of research was utilized in this study. The main instrument was the\r\nresearchers developed questionnaire to find out the factors affecting\r\nA significant issue shows the factors affecting and resort services and its customer\r\nsatisfaction in Bulacan, Bulakan is the kind of services that they give to their customer. They must focus on the services which give them a better impression. Resorts are one of the revenue center of municipality of bulakan. They patronized by the guest because they value the concerns\r\nand expectation of its guest. Based on the statistical test result that there is a significant relationship between the factors affecting the promotion in the income of the resort which means\r\nthat the more they get a customer they could get a high profit with their resort business.\r\n', 2013, 'ALLEN LEXTER M. AGUSTIN | RICHARD REY S. DALABAJAN'),
(12, 4, 'BS HRM', 'SPORTS DEVELOPMENT PROGRAM OF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITYHAGONOY CAMPUS: AN IN DEPTH ASSESSMENT', 'The study is about Sports Development Program of Bulacan State University\r\nHagonoy Campus conducted by Louigi C. Buensuceso, Queenee Lou D. Arellano, Kimberly Mae L. Bernardo, Jerwin R. Perez and Juan Paolo P. Salvanera.\r\nThe study evaluated the sports program of BulSU Hagony Campus and determined the profile of the athletes and performers in terms of 1) age, gender, course, marital status, favorite sports, games played/performed during the recent Intramurals and length of experience.\r\nThe respondents of the study are the athletes/performers who are identified based\r\non their participation in the most recent Intramurals in Bulacan State University. These are the games/competition that they participated specifically: Basketball, Volleyball, Table Tennis, Badminton, Lawn Tennis, Beach Volley, Chess, Taekwondo, Archery, Athletics and Dance Sports.\r\nBased on the findings of the study, it is concluded that a) the Assessment of\r\nSports Development Program at BulSU Hagony Campus was found to be not effective in terms of the recruitment process happened during the last Intramurals according to the athletes and performers; b) the Campus Sports Facilities used by the athletes and performers were found to be not adequate according to the athletes and performers because the facilities of the campus were not well developed; c) the Campus Sports Equipment used by the athletes and performers were found to be enough according to the athletes and performers; and d) the Assessment on the Support of Stakeholders such as the students/SCO, alumni and parents/PTA were found to be not adequate according to\r\nthe athletes and performers.\r\nFrom the conclusions,\r\nthe following are recommended: 1) The Campus\r\nAdministration must improve the facilities especially on the playing or training venues for the Development of Sports Program and also for the athletes and performers; 2) The Campus Administration must encourage the students to join in any sports development\r\nprogram offered by the school. Likewise, the Campus Administration must conduct a monthly training for the coaches and trainers; and 3) The Campus Administration should make aware the students/SCO, alumni and parents/PTA of the existing Sports\r\nDevelopment Program at BulSU Hagonoy Campus.\r\n', 2015, ' Louigi C. Buensuceso | Queenee Lou D. ArellanoKimberly Mae L. Bernardo | Jerwin R. Perez | Juan Paolo P. Salvanera'),
(13, 2, 'BS HRM', 'THE EFFECTS OF ICT LITERACY TO HRM STUDENTS OF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS TO THEIR ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE', 'The study is all about effects of ICT literacy of HRM students in Bulacan State University in relation to their academic performance by Emanoel G. Pahati, Mark Anthony B. Go, Elaine Denniece I. Perez, Veronica Thea DL. Reyes and Arlou Niño L Perez.\r\nICT or Information and Communication Technology are any\r\ntechnological/digital equipment and some various applications software. These\r\nare some typical basic applications software that are commonly used are\r\nMicrosoft Office, Microsoft Excel, Microsoft PowerPoint, Photoshop and etc. which help the users easily done the tasks. Some of these applications software\r\nare used by the students in their personal or educational purposes, to excel in their academic performance, and to make their task easily done.\r\nThe purpose of the study is to identify the effect of literacy of HRM students of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus to their academic\r\nperformance, the literacy of students, usefulness of the applications software,\r\nand how iCT literacy affeci their academic performance.\r\n', 2015, 'Pahati, Emanoel G.| Go, Mark Anthony B.| Perez, Elaine Denniece I.| Perez, Arlou Niño L. | Reyes, Veronica Thea DL.'),
(14, 7, 'BSHM', ' IMPACT OF MILLENNIAL CULTURE IN THE RESTAURANT INDUSTRY ', 'This research aimed to find out if the millennial culture has a role in the\r\nprogression and development of the restaurant industry in Malolos, Bulacan. The main purpose of this study is to find out whether the millennial culture can have enough impact to affect the way the local restaurants present their products, conduct their promotions, adjust their prices, and showcase their facilities. In order for the researchers to garner sufficient data, the researchers have handed out questionnaires. The interpretations of the results, analysis and gathering of data, followed by findings, and the summary is presented in this study. The Research Methodology showcases all of the methods and techniques used, the research instrument, and the statistical treatment where the data has been gathered and summarized. Lastly, the major findings and conclusion are all presented in this research. With the researchers being able to garner out a \"somewhat agree\" as a result from the target demographic. It is no secret that the millennial culture has had somewhat of an impact in the restaurant industry. All it needs now is the further acknowledgement and recognition from other restaurant owners.\r\n\r\n', 2019, 'Apolonio, David Kenneth M. | Cervantes, Allan G. | Chico, Louie Mark V.| Cruz, Kerwin A. | Fortiveros, Ivan Russell J. | Lorenzo, Jayser A. | Santos, Jan Alvin DC. | Sunga, Maria Faith P.'),
(15, 3, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'THE FACTORS AFFECTING THE COURSE SELECTION OF FRESHMEN STUDENTS AT BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY-HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'The study is about the factors affecting the course selection of freshmen students at Bulacan State University by Jane V. Realizan, Brenda L. Perez, Rhonalyn O. Legaspi, Anjo B. Binalla and Benrad Santos.\r\nChoosing a course is a hard decision because students consider the impact of their course choice to his/her future. One has to be serious about choosing his/her course. It is important to take the fields that interest you the most and the course that will help you acquire the skills and knowledge you will need to succeed as a professional. In choosing the right course for yourself in college, you should know at least the basic things about it.\r\nUpon finishing college, you should be aware of what possible jobs that you can apply such aspect pressure and parents decision.\r\nThe purpose of the study is to identify the most influential factors that affect the\r\ncourse selection, the top the courses that selected and the interest to the course of the freshmen students at Bulacan State University-Hagony Campus.\r\n', 2015, ' Realizan, Jane V. | Perez, Brenda L. | Legaspi, Rhonalyn R. | Binalla, Anjo B. | Santos, Benrad S '),
(16, 0, '0', 'DEVELOPMENT OF HOMEMADE SWEETENED STYLE BANGUS', 'One of the foremost important food species worldwide is milkfish. In Indonesia, Taiwan, and the Philippines, more than one-quarter of a million tons of milkfish are cleared annually in brackish swamps, adding nearly 60% of the total production of South-East Asia, this enormous development of an equivalent fish commodity is predicted to extend more within the next few years to satisfy the food protein requirements of Southeast Asias ever-growing population.\r\nThis study indicates that a lot of people consume milkfish not just within the Philippines, numerous individuals may become curious by innovating it, and its also certain that our commodities are going to be marketable Bangus is additionally one among the staple foods of Filipinos. Bangus account for about 60% of the national protein consumption ranking second to rice as the most important staple food of Filipino. (Kirkens-Nodhjelp 1997) thanks to the recognition of Tocino, different variants evolved from the standard port ingredient of tocino.\r\nThe researchers aim to form Homemade Sweetened Style Bangus function as an alternate or innovation to the usual tocino. Unlike pork tocino, Homemade Sweetened Style Bangus is healthier, nutritious, and also inexpensive compared to pork, to be ready to create a livelihood for the people of Bulacan, and to be ready to maximize the use of the \"Bangus\" fish, the researchers came up with the thought of making an innovative product Homemade Sweetened Style Bangus which can be liked by many.\r\nThis study covers the essential aspects of developing Homemade Sweetened Style Bangus in terms of the product description, ingredients, procedure, and tools and equipment needed in its preparation.\r\n', 2021, 'Bayani, James S. | Cordero, Mathew M. | Enriquez, Kitt S. | Manansala, Marcelino Jr. P. | Vivar, Hannah Angelica dL.'),
(17, 6, 'BS HRM', 'PERCEPTION OF CUSTOMERS TOWARDS THE SERVICE OF CANTEEN IN BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS: A BASIS FOR MARKETING PLAN', 'The researchers conducted the study to evaluate the perception of customers satisfaction towards the service of canteen in Bulacan State\r\nUniversity Hagony Campus and to recommend a marketing plan to improve the quality of service. Random respondents were asked if they had experienced dinning in the entire seven subject school canteenand then were given survey questionnaires. Majority of the respondents are college students and the rest of them are either teaching staff or non- teaching staff. The total computed sample size was 180.\r\nThe relationships of various area of canteen service and customers\r\nsatisfaction were determined using one statistical tool, descriptive statistic, using the SPSS software. By using descriptive statistics, it showed that majority of the\r\nrespondents are generally dissatisfied in terms of quality of service in areas of sanitation or hygiene and canteen ambiance, only the food offered and the food price are pleasing for the consumers. Based on these results, the researchers recommend to the subject school canteen to allot focus and importance on the areas of food and area of sanitation, and in improving the overall ambiance of the\r\nplace for a better overall customers satisfaction and patronage.\r\n', 2016, ' PEREZ, ELAINE DENNIECE I. | BINALLA, ANJO B. | GATELA, PRINCESS JANETTE C. | GOZAMO, IVAN SHIN P. | REYES, VERONICA THEA DL. | SANTOS, BENRAD S.'),
(18, 0, '0', 'TRACER STUDY ON THE WHEREABOUTS OF HOSPITALITY MANAGEMENT GRADUATES OF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'racer study refers to the investigations in which a sample of individuals are studied at a given time, and then located and studied again at one or more successive stages in their lives. This study helps the universities to identify the whereabouts of their students after they graduated. Tracer testing tracks graduates/ alumni, trace studies carried out from 1 to 3 years after graduation.\r\nIn the Philippines, only 33 of 100 Filipinos who should be in college are enrolled in higher education institutions. Meanwhile, 23% of the population of 15-30 years old who graduated college or higher are unemployed. Hence, the country is battling with both low participation rates in higher education and apparently low employability of educated youth even though unemployment correlates poorly with poverty (de Dios and Dinglasan 2014).\r\n\r\nThe researchers made use of appropriate tools in analyzing the data to secure substantial results and findings such as frequency and percentage.\r\nThis study primarily determined the employability of the graduates of Hospitality Management of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus from 2015-2019.\r\nSpecifically, it sought to determine the job placement profile of the graduates and relevance of school related factors to job placement in meeting the demand of the present job. This tracer study was conducted to improve employment rate for Hospitality management graduates.\r\n', 2021, 'Caparas, Kate Aubrey A. |Crisostomo, Christine Joy J. | Francisco, Ma. Sofia S. | Hotta, Mikaelah Akira S. | Medina, Lailanie V. | Trinidad, Trisha Ann DC.'),
(19, 5, 'BS HRM', 'DEVELOPMENT OF MALUNGGAY AND LACATAN BANANA PEEL PORK NUGGETS', 'The general problem of the study is how to develop Malunggay and Lacatan banana peel pork nuggets. Specifically, the study seeks to answer the microbial properties if Malunggay and Lacatan banana peel pork nuggets in terms of Aerobic plate count, Coliform count, Yeast and Mold count, Staphylococcus Aureus Detection, and Salmonella Detection. The study also seeks to\r\nanswer sensory evaluation and acelin terms of color, aroma, flavor, texture, and aftertaste, and what is the acceptability of Malunggay and Lacatan banana peel pork nuggets.\r\nThe researchers brought sample of Malunggay and Lacatan banana peel pork nuggets to DOST-BSU Food Testing Laboratory for Microbial Analysis. The sample has Aerobic plate count, Coliform count, Yeast and Mold count, Staphylococcus Aureus Detection, and Salmonella Detection values that are within the BFAD\r\nMicrobiological Standards. The sample has PASSED all the\r\nmicrobiological standards.\r\nThe researchers also included that Malunggay and Lacatan\r\nbanana peel pork nuggets are safe to eat and can be a new variety to the realm of desserts, specifically in the category of pastillas.\r\nAccording to respondents the Malunggay and Lacatan banana peel pork nuggets was to golden brown, no distinct flavor of Lacatan banana peel and has a crispy texture of outer part. the comments and recommendations were able to improve Malunggay and Lacatan\r\nbanana peel pork nuggets into more acceptable. To the next\r\nresearchers who want to further develop this present study you may\r\nuse Lacatan banana peel as a flavor of bake products such as\r\ncookies, pudding, muffins and cakes.\r\n', 2016, 'Markester U. Cruz | Aaron T. Dela Cruz | Ronnielo C. Mallari | Catherine P. Portes | John Mark P. Toledo | Lorraine S. Ventura'),
(20, 14, 'BSHM', 'DEVELOPMENT OF ALUGBATI POLVORON', 'Product development is the lifeblood of the food industry, from refining a mounted product vary to growing absolutely new products. The component alugbati is derived from an herbaceous vine known scientifically as Basella alba L. The researchers want to show that it is feasible to create a distinctive flavor for desserts and other uses. The purpose of the study is to create fresh polvoron fillings utilizing alugbati leaves. The researchers\' goal is to identify the key components of alugbati polvoron, which they will do by looking at terms like \"procedure,\" \"product description,\" \"ingredients,\" \"tools,\" and \"equipment.\" They will also evaluate the product\'s sensory quality by using the following criteria: \"texture/mouth feel,\" \"taste/flavor,\" \"color/appearance,\" and \"smell/aroma.\" The ingredients of Alugbati Polvoron consist Alugbati leaves, Powdered Milk, Sugar, Margarine and Flour. After series of trial the development of Alugbati polvoron.\r\nSeveral changes to the quantity of each ingredient and procedure were done. In every trial, the production results in a better product - it\'s a win-win situation for all involved.\r\nThe Healthy Alugbati Polvoron has a unique and rich flavor. Product can help you\r\nslow down absorption of sugar in your body. It is a fantastic source of calcium, zinc,\r\nmagnesium and iron so that it is a possible and edible ingredient. The researchers recommended to improve the texture/mouthfeel of the filling of Alugbati polvoron as this got the lowest weighted mean among the sensory quality attributes.\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Coronel, Christine Joy R | Flores Ericka Marie C. | Santos, Ernest Lloyd A. | Sebastian, Alyzza Janine M. | Suerte Felipe, Aivhann Mharck D '),
(21, 0, '0', 'EFFECTS OF MARKETING TECHNIQUES TOWARDS THE BUSINESS GROWTH OF SELECTED FOOD ESTABLISHMENT IN THE CITY OF MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'To determine the impact of marketing approaches on business growth of certain culinary enterprises in the City of Malolos, according to the study\'s executive statement the researchers made a self-design questionnaire using a rating scale method as the instrument of the study, researchers collected data from eighty (80) respondents from the supervisors, branch manager, employees and staff of selected food establishment. Specifically, it seeks to answer the following questions Effects of marketing techniques in the growth and development of business in selected food establishments in terms of distribution of flyers/leaflets, advertisement of updating products, and offering of discounted items. And the marketing techniques affect the business growth and development in terms of sales and profit. The study further concludes that offering discounted items had a positive effect on the sales performance of food establishments in the City of Malolos.\r\n', 2022, 'Cruz John Ace E. | Dalisay Patricia Anne A. | Gutierrez Sherlyn G.| Mercado Frederick Dan A. | Merino Ericka Rain R. | Reyes Katrina G.'),
(22, 0, '0', ' REPLACING HUMANS WITH AI: A TREAT OR THREAT', 'The study was conducted on the Paradise Hotel and Resort. It focused on the technology advances, the prevalence of robots in the workplace increases. From manufacturing to healthcare to logistics, robots are used to enhance work performance in numerous industries. Companies are increasingly employing robots in logistics, for instance, to boost efficiency and reduce expenses. This study used quantitative data collection, and an analysis method to answer the research method. Random sampling in which each sample has an equal chance of being selected. The purpose of a randomly selected sample is to\r\naccurately depict the entire population. The respondents were 100 hotels staff,\r\nhotel manager and guest. Keywords: replacing human, artificial intelligent, treat or threat.\r\n', 2022, 'Gaspi, Jerald P. | Manglicmot, Jerome A. | Ramos, Kyle C.'),
(23, 12, 'BSHM', ' DEVELOPMENT OF ENHANCE CHOCO FUDGE', 'Product Development is a Critical Process Product development strategies are important to ensure value for your potential customers, as well as ensuring demand and that your final product is of the highest possible quality before releasing it to the market. The products themselves help society, whether through the product line itself or through the employment and income generation that the new item provides. On the business side of things, a new product can increase a company\'s market share and create growth, ensuring economic sustainability through new revenue... Of course, it can take years for development teams to bring a product from the design phase to the point where it is ready for market and distribution. Chocolate fudge has a lot of chocolate in it, and it\'s richer and denser than regular fudge. It\'s also a one-layer chocolate cake that can be served with or without icing. Because it is prepared from basic dark chocolate, many people consider choco fudge to be a nutritious cake.\r\n', 2022, 'Justine Louie N. DeLuna | Mary Clarence M. Alcantara |Jerald P. Flores | Alfrance H.Pangilinan | Renz John R. Santiago'),
(24, 23, 'BSHM', 'CUSTOMER SATISFACTION TOWARDS FAST FOOD UTILIZING SELF ORDER KIOSK', ' In food service industry, it is necessary to have a unique and effective marketing strategy to satisfy your customers\' needs and wants. The repeat and loyal customer is the key to have a successful business in this industry. Customer satisfaction has been defined as an affective state or overall emotional reaction to a service experience (Beatson, et al. 2018).\r\nThis study investigates the customers satisfaction towards fast food utilizing self-order kiosk. The present data use Likert Scale to interpret the level of satisfaction of the customers while using the self-order kiosk. Structured interviews were conducted with 100 participants.\r\nThe findings presented shows that the effectiveness of self-order kiosk greatly impact\r\ncustomers satisfaction. Thus, this accepts alternative hypothesis (Ha) and rejects null hypothesis (Ho). This study has revealed that the majority of participants are happy with the use of self- service kiosks in fast food restaurants, as they could produce a practical, clear, and appealing menu design, increase ordering speed, and improve the precision of the order. Keywords: self - order, customer satisfaction\r\n', 2022, 'DE GUIA, Mark Albert L. | GUEVARA, Jexour Marie S. | SUICO, Earl Aldrin A  '),
(25, 18, 'BSHM', 'STATUS OF FOOD ESTABLISHMENT OFFERINGORGANIC FOOD IN BULACAN', 'The present study is to pinpoint the status of establishment offering organic food in Malolos Bulacan. As the research wants to give attention to the status of\r\norganic food that was presented to the market and how it will affect or what will be the impact of it to the establishment that will be offering this kind of food. This research will benefit the students, parents, economy and future researcher who want to know more about the stated subject. The data were collected using Survey Questionnaire related to the topic and there were 15 random respondents from Malolos Food Establishment who participated in this data collection. To assess the status of food establishment offering organic food in bulacan, the researchers use the Likert Scale Method to identify the respondents\' level of agreement in each statement provided. This study also aims to know the status and benefits of organic food to a food establishment including the resources from supplier to consumer, demand and popularity of the product.\r\nFor the purpose of clarification, the important terms used in this study have been defined. The following terms are: Status - Means position or rank in relation to others as used in this study, status will be the one who will be found by the researchers which is the status of food establishments offering organic food. Organic - Produced or involving production without the use of chemical fertilizers, pesticides, or other artificial agents. In this study organic vegetables will be the topic of the researchers.\r\nSustainability - Means meeting our own needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs. As used in this study, it will provide the needs without the inconvenience of lacking goods.\r\n', 2022, 'Cabrera, Mary Lourdes DG. | Castro, Anne Pauline M.Chavez, Catlyn Marie F. | Tolentino, Adrian M. | Trillana, Marjalette Elaine G. | Villafania, Cherry Joy C '),
(26, 28, 'BSHM', 'CUSTOMER SATISFACTION: EXPLORING FOOD QUALITY OF PORK SISIG AMONG SELECTED FOOD ESTABLISHMENTS IN HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'This study was conducted to assess the Customer satisfaction: Exploring Food Quality of Pork Sisig among Selected food Establishments in Hagonoy, Bulacan. It made used of the descriptive type of research. This covers the Customer satisfaction by 100 random respondents using the research questionnaires validated by experts from the course.\r\nWeighted mean was to be used to determine the customer satisfaction in the\r\nselected food establishment in Hagonoy, Bulacan during the present time period of the research. The descriptive analysis in the process were conducted using Descriptive Statistics were used to simply describe what is or what the data gathered shows in the study from the respondents.\r\nFindings revealed that the obtained responses from the participants in terms of Customer Satisfaction in Food Quality in Pork Sisig in Selected Food Establishment in Hagonoy, Bulacan. Based on the collected data, it is from the people who experience to eat to those food establishment in Hagonoy Bulacan. Among to the combined 100 male and female respondents, there are 98% of them that are single and 2% are married. Findings shows that the highest percentage of choosing food establishment in pork sisig got the percentage of 44% which is Food Establishment A, then 41% is Food Establishment C while Food Establishment B got 15%. It indicates that Establishment A have the most percentage of customers among the two establishment.\r\nKeywords: Customer, Corona Virus, Food Establishment, Business, Hospitality Industry, Employees.\r\n', 2022, 'ACUÑA, Niño V. | BARTOLOME, Aillen C. | CRISOSTOMO, Arvie T.ISIP, Carl Jimuel DC. | PIMENTEL, Angelo Ris S. | SUMERA, Joseph Emmanuel M '),
(27, 24, 'BSHM', 'SELECTED FAST FOODS\' GREEN PRACTICES AND THEIR INFLUENCE ON THE COMPANY\'S REPUTATION', 'The purpose of this research was to determine the relationships between green practices in selected fast-food establishments. It also aimed to identify the key green practices that affect customers\' perceptions of a fast food establishment\'s commitment to environmental sustainability. Moreover, the findings imply that customers\' opinions toward restaurants are influenced by their perception of a restaurant as having a positive image. Green practices are now affecting the fast food industry. In order to establish a distinctive brand that might set them apart from their competitors, fast food owners incorporate green practices into their business. Hence, by implementing green practices in their establishments, restaurant owners want to gain this competitive advantage. This study set out to determine whether environmentally friendly activities had a significant impact on a company\'s reputation. Furthermore, how does this relationship differ between various customer segments with strong attitudes or beliefs in their capacity to significantly impact the course of ecological problems and those without. The results showed that consumer perceptions toward the company are positively impacted by green practices that are consistent with how they view sustainability. Keywords: Fast Food, Green Practices, Restaurant\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'CARPIO, Kayla Mae Y. | DUCUSIN, John Paul T. | FAUSTINO, Annerose J. | GUEVARRA, Nicole A.'),
(28, 15, 'BSHM', 'THE DEVELOPMENT OF WAX APPLE PIE', 'This study has plan to make an impact to the market by developing unique filling of pie by using wax apple. The trial and error and descriptive research are included. The researchers used a survey questionnaire to be answered by a variety of respondents and consists of 50 respondents to assessed and find out if a lot of people will have a good response to the said product, As the study has aim to make an impact to the market by developing unique filling of pie by using wax apple. Findings revealed that the obtained responses from the respondents have mostly agreed that they like the taste/flavor and smell of Wax Apple Pie, Base on the collected data with the help of our respondents the result shows of How acceptable is the sensory quality of Wax Apple Pie in terms of the taste/flavor has a weighted mean of 6.92, the texture/mouth feel of the has a weighted mean of 6.72, the appearance/color has a weighted mean of 7.50, the smell/aroma of wax apple pie has a weighted mean of 7.74. Majority of the respondents were 15 to 19 years old and 20 to 29 years old and there are more female respondents than male respondents.\r\nTo summarized, the wax apple pie has a great potential to be marketable and it can be a source of income. The product is a proof that the wax apple is possible and edible ingredient. Keywords: Pie, Wax Apple, Baking\r\n', 2022, 'Felipe, Gabriel | Mercado, Dharyll John DC. | Pauig, Jharmaine Jayde V.| Perona, Rich Cielo R. | Roque, Rochelle | Tamayo, Graciela S'),
(29, 13, 'BSHM', ' INFLUENCE OF ORGANIZATIONAL CULTURAL DIVERSITY IN RESTAURANTS WORKERS\' PRODUCTIVITY IN MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'Influence of Organizational Cultural Diversity in Restaurant Workers\' Productivity in Malolos, Bulacan was conducted to analyze how managing organizational cultural diversity improves restaurant workers\' productivity. The study\'s main objective is to provide comprehensive information regarding workplace cultural diversity. It intends to establish a clear guideline to help various organizations worldwide embrace cultural diversity. The researchers gathered information using a questionnaire to quickly assess the information regarding the demographic profile such as gender, age, religion, ethnicity, race,and civil status of the respondents which are important to evaluate the respondents\' differences and how these differences affect their productivity in the workplace. To assessthe influence of cultural diversity on workers\' productivity, the researchers use the Likert Scale Method to identify the respondents\' level of agreement in each statement provided. Thestudy analyzes employees\' experience with cultural diversity in their workplace, the extentto which the employees see their organization in managing cultural diversity, and the extentto which cultural diversity affects employees\' performance and productivity. The studyshowed that most of the respondents\' age ranges from 20 to 30, and the female was the most dominant gender among the respondents who are currently working in a restaurant. The studyalso demonstrates that most respondents are Roman Catholic, Tagalog, and Asian. In termsof civil status, all the respondents are single. When it comes to the respondent\'s level of agreement, most of the respondents\' state that organizational cultural diversity supports the restaurant workers\' productivity.\r\nOn the other hand, most of them believed that their restaurant creates teamwork with diverse employees that helps exchange several ideas and knowledge and find the best way to solve the problem that results in a better outcome on tasks. The study\'s findings conclude that cultural diversity management program/education would enhance the performance ofthe employees in doing their job. Understanding cultural diversity will also help them to realize their strengths and weaknesses. When a culturally diverse workplace is properly managed, it will help the employees to develop new ideas, knowledge, skills, and new waysto work. Cultural diversity also contributes to the organization\'s success and profitability, anda working environment free from cultural discrimination increases the organization\'s productivity.\r\n', 2022, 'CAÑETE, Roy Christian I. | LUNA, Kelvin John T. | MAMANGON, Hazel Ann Z. | ROBERTO, Randolph A. | SANTOS, Sherilyn | TRINIDAD, Loiz Jean S.'),
(30, 10, 'BSTM', 'THE EFFECTS OF ONLINE CLASSES TO THE ACADEMIC ENGAGEMENT OF TOURISM STUDENTS IN BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY - HAGONOYCAMPUS', 'The COVID-19 pandemic impacted over 91 percent of the world\'s student population (UNESCO, 2022), making institutions to create various strategies to solve the crisis. Switching to online delivery of lessons is one of the considered solutions.\r\nHowever, online learning has been stigmatized as a weaker option as it provides a lower quality of education, affecting students\' academic engagement (Hodges et al., 2020).\r\nBulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus is one of the universities in the Philippines compelled by the outbreak. Thus, the researchers conducted this study to identify and discuss the effects of online classes on the academic engagement of tourism students at Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus. The respondents of the study were determined through purposive and random sampling. After identifying the respondents and receiving their conformations, survey questionnaires were given using Google Forms and social media platforms. Lastly, the data collected were analyzed using different statistical methods, which were discussed and interpreted. The gathered data indicates the significant relationship between online classes and the academic engagement of tourism management students at Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus.\r\n', 2022, ':CARLOS JR., Benjamin P. | ESTRELLA, Josielyn U. | FELICIANO, Erica Mae DL. | PREMACIO, Ryan Christian C. | RAYMUNDO, Kaye Inah Marie G. | SISPEREZ, Mariano DR. | TRAJIA, Marie Eli Neil P.');
INSERT INTO `thesisbooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(31, 0, '0', 'HANDICRAFTS AS TOURISM PRODUCTS AND ITS CONTRIBUTION IN PRESERVING THE CULTURE OF BULACAN', 'This study explores the potential of handicrafts as tourism products and their contribution to preserving the culture of Bulacan. The province of Bulacan is rich in cultural heritage, particularly in traditional crafts such as pottery, woodworks, and artisanal foods. These crafts have been passed down from generation to generation and are a\r\nsignificant part of the local culture. However, with the rise of industrialization, many of these traditional crafts have become endangered. This study argues that by promoting handicrafts as tourism products, they can be preserved and even revitalized. Handicrafts can offer tourists a unique and authentic cultural experience, and at the same time, generate\r\nincome for the local community.\r\nThe study uses a qualitative approach, employing interviews and focus group discussions with artisans, local government officials, and tourism stakeholders. The findings reveal that handicrafts have the potential to attract tourists, and there is a growing interest in promoting them as tourism products. Furthermore, handicrafts can contribute to preserving the culture of Bulacan by providing a platform for the transmission of traditional knowledge and skills. By involving local artisans in tourism activities, their crafts can be given new life and attract younger generations to learn and continue these traditions. The study concludes that handicrafts have significant potential as tourism products in Bulacan.\r\nBy promoting and preserving these crafts, the local community can benefit economically while maintaining their cultural identity. Therefore, it is recommended that the local government and tourism stakeholders work together to develop a comprehensive tourism strategy that integrates handicrafts as a key element.\r\n', 2022, 'Aguilar, Siegfried E. | Bantolino, Ryz Lourence B. | Carpio, Renan M.| Mina, Aira Mae M. | Romero, Lenie E.'),
(32, 0, '0', 'CONTRIBUTIONS OF SELECTED CULTURAL HERITAGEATTRACTIONS TO THE TOURISM SECTOR OF MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'This study aims to determine if the Selected Cultural Heritage Attraction greatly contributes or does not contribute to the tourism sector of Malolos Bulacan. The study conducted can help to identify the Contribution of cultural Heritage in the Tourism Business Industry in Malolos, Bulacan. Also, this study will serve awareness to Maloleños in terms of Long-term sustainability of tourist development, and Cultural Heritage Contribution in Tourism Business.\r\nFirst, due to the need for information, the survey questionnaire and interview guide were used to collect the necessary data and information to answer the questions. The perception and expression of the survey questionnaire using a four-point Likert scale. The researcher conducted a random survey and interviews with the indicated respondents, who included the owner or management of the selected cultural heritage, tourists and the residents. The results of this study reveals, Programme 5 was proposed for the government to give more attention on sustaining the environmental resources. Government also needs to focus on the improvement of tourist necessities and satisfaction. By the interview from the management of the historical sites, curators seek the support of the local government for improvement and preservation of the said cultural heritages. By proposing the programmed 5 this will help the management of the said historical site to improve and preserve the historical site for the history and carries and for the tourist satisfaction.\r\nFurthermore, in the result, it was revealed that the service delivery improvement plan can be proposed based on the results of the study is Programme 5: Government Services, Access and Improvement with its sub-programme \"Service Delivery Planning and Operations Management\" Using service standards, delivery models, and standard operating procedures, Service Delivery Planning and Operations Management handles Public Service delivery planning and operations management and creates toolkits and instruments to aid in better service delivery.\r\n', 2022, 'DELA CRUZ, Arthea Rose B. | BAYAN, lan C. | CRISOSTOMO, Rei Ann A. | GONZALES, Maria Sophia C.'),
(33, 20, 'BSTM', 'THE CONTRIBUTION OF THE FILIPINOS\' HOSPITALITY TOWARDSPHILIPPINE TOURISM: BASIS FOR TOURISM INITIATIVES', ' The abstract highlights the significant role of Filipino hospitality in the context of Philippine tourism and its potential as a foundation for tourism initiatives. It emphasizes the warm reception offered by Filipinos to foreign visitors, characterized by feasts and open homes, and how this practice showcases the essence of Filipino culture. The research alludes to challenges faced by the tourism sector, particularly during the pandemic, including workforce reductions, digital transaction mandates, and adherence to health protocols as detailed by Andulana et al. (2021), encompass embracing local tourism, enhancing digital and safety training for employees, image revamping, facility optimization, technological integration, and collaborating with risk management experts.\r\nHowever, the study asserts that while digitalization is important, the restoration of the\r\ntourism industry\'s vitality is closely tied to Filipino culture. The research aims to explore\r\nand analyze the extent of the contribution of Filipino hospitality to Philippine tourism.\r\nNotably, the abstract references Forbes Magazine\'s (2012) \"Expat Explorer\r\nSurvey,\" which positions the Philippines at the forefront of friendliest countries, ranking 8th globally and 1st in Asia. This distinction underscores the significance of Filipino hospitality on an international stage. The abstract closes by highlighting attributes intrinsic to Filipino culture-warmth, respect, religiosity, love, care, and strong family bonds— which collectively contribute to the exceptional hospitality extended to tourists and visitors. The enduring smiles and warm greetings of Filipinos encapsulate a culture of hospitality that continues to set the Philippines apart in the world of travel and tourism.\r\nKeywords: Filipino hospitality, Philippine tourism, culture, tourism initiatives, challenges, pandemic, identity, friendliest countries, warmth.\r\n', 2022, 'CRUZ, Princess Ericka A.| MAMITES, Mariz L.| TORRES, Kristine R.'),
(34, 0, '0', 'TRACER STUDY ON THE WHEREABOUTS OF BULSU HAGONOY CAMPUS TOURISM GRADUATES', 'This tracer study of the Bachelor of Science in Tourism Management Graduates of\r\nBulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus was conducted in order to track and locate the whereabouts of the graduates to be able to gain information such as their demographic profiles.\r\nAside from that, this was done for the purpose of curriculum analysis-to see how satisfied the graduates are, how much their major subjects and extra-curricular programs helped them in developing their technical and non-technical skills. Also, to know whether there is a significant gap between the BulSU Hagonoy Campus BS Tourism Management Curriculum and the technical skill requirements in the tourism industry. The study showed that most of the graduates\' ages range from 20- 30, and females are the most dominant among the graduates, their reason for enrolling at BulSU Hagonoy is mainly because of the availability of their preferred course and more than a half of the graduates are currently employed. When it comes to the level of satisfaction of the graduates in terms of services, they are very satisfied with the Seminars and skills trainings provided. For the Learning environment, they are very much agree that they are satisfied with the Teacher\'s Attitudes and Actions and when it comes to the facilities, the clinic ranked the highest. The graduates find that the curricular program contributed to their development in terms of communication skills, problem-solving skills, research skills, human relation skills and leadership skills. The graduates say that they acquired the skills they were taught from the curriculum and these were useful in their current jobs. Based on the T-Test, the decision is to accept the null hypothesis of the study. Through the findings briefly discussed, this study let the researchers conclude that there is no significant difference between the BSTM Curriculum and the technical skills required by the tourism industry.\r\n', 2021, 'ADRIANO, Criscia Nicole C. | BAGUIO, Abegail Pam D. | BAGUIO, Shania Gwyneth D. | DELGADO, Daniella G. | GARCIA, Jeanna Joy S. | TOLENTINO, Janah May L.'),
(35, 0, '0', 'THE EFFECTS OF COVID-19 TO THE HERITAGE SITES IN MALOLOS BULACAN', 'The Philippines has one of the world\'s highest COVID19 instances. When the enhanced community quarantine was implemented to guarantee the safety of Filipino citizens, the Philippine government shut down all airports. The government has placed restrictions on all those entering the country and placed them under quarantine for 14 days.\r\nThe tourist industry has suffered adetrimental impact as a result of the closure of most of\r\nthe underperforming tourism businesses; as a result, all travel within and outside of the country has been restricted. The COVID 19 pandemic has a significant impact on everyone\'s lives as well as the country\'s economy. This research will examine at every tourism site in Malolos City, Bulacan that has been affected by the pandemic and focus on what they have done to adjust to the changing circumstances as a result of the crisis. Its main goal is to reveal the effects of the coronavirus on tourism locations, as well as the benefits and challenges of the pandemic. Many people are not allowed to travel, especially because an enhanced community quarantine has been implemented to ensure that everyone is safe. The study used the descriptive type of research in part of fulfilling the final research process of the study. This method of research aims to answer the aspects, recovery and the situation of the tourism department in Malolos, Bulacan. The techniques in data collection are both analytical and survey methods that are sufficient in the study. Online questionnaires were used to perform the study.\r\n', 2021, ' Abanto, Kathleen Shenn S. | Laxamana, Khaey Ann C. | Mangahas, Monica M. | Maravilla, Regin Dale J. | Urbano, Glesty Nicole O.'),
(36, 36, 'BSHM', ' BEST MARKETING PRACTICES OF SELECTED FOOD SERVICE ESTABLISHMENTS IN HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'The Food Service Industry is an important sector in our society. It is a wide field in terms of hospitality and offers ranges of services which makes it more complex. This study objective is to know the profiles of various food establishments, the implications of marketing strategies focusing on the marketing mix and customer service in relation to the companies\' goals and objectives, and the problems associated with the operation of food service establishments. This study is guided with three relevant theories, the 7Ps of Marketing Theory, Maslows\'s Hierarchy of Needs, and the Consumer Decision-Making Process, to give enlightenment to the topic, This study chose fifty individuals from different food establishments which includes fast food and\r\nbaked shop in the town of Hagonoy in the Province of Bulacan. There are enumerated indicators of marketing strategies as identified by the\r\nindividuals who are working on food service industry during the survey and these were the basis of analysis as it tries to evaluate the effectiveness of marketing strategies used by the food service as perceived by the establishments and customers and to find out its impact to the present market status. To further evaluate the hypotheses posed in the study, T-tests were used to test the best practices of the food service industry in Hagonoy, Bulacan. According to the study\'s findings, the food service\'s primary focus is the marketing strategies used\r\nin operating a business products and services, prices, the location of the establishment, and sales promotion used to gain profit and customers. Also, all food service establishments observed the importance of good promotion to improve sales force and work efficiency, as it makes marketing awareness increase and motivates the staff to achieve customer satisfaction in the overall performance of the food service store. This study could assist future and existing food service establishments owners about the best marketing techniques from the study\'s findings. It might serve as their guide to learning more about effective marketing. They might be better able to plan for the future with the help of the knowledge obtained.\r\n', 2024, 'Bartolome, Jhasmin Liezel T. | De Guia, Rhod Daniel C. | Garceles, Glenn L. | Leron, Justin DC.'),
(37, 39, 'BSHM', 'Being COVID-19 Positive: Students\' Lived Experiences atBulacan State University Hagony and the Effect on their Academic Performance', ' The purpose of the study is to determine the lived experiences of students that contracted the virus during the COVID-19 pandemic and to formulate academic initiatives and provide effective and efficient alternatives that can be beneficial for both the students\r\nand the university in general. The study is qualitative in nature, through purposive sampling, the target number of respondents was 15, but only 8 responded; they were all enrolled in Bulacan State University Hagonoy. The findings indicate that the independent and dependent variables utilized in the study indeed have correlation which left an impact on students\' lived experiences on both academic and personal level, which in turn mostly\r\nhad a negative impact on the educational sector, mainly affecting the students\' mental health, productivity, academic performance, and their well-being in general. These elements are crucial for their educational management in order to cope with the situation, along with performance in online-based classes. To determine the effect of the COVID-19 on the students\' academic performance, this study is being carried out during the COVID-19 pandemic period. Therefore, the students are indeed gravely affected by the said virus, namely the COVID-19. The informants experienced numerous extreme difficulties in managing their time with balancing their academic performance and at the same time, their personal lives as well.\r\nKeywords: academic initiatives, efficient alternatives, purposive sampling, correlation, educational sector, mental health, productivity, well-being, academic performance, educational management, online-based classes, pandemic, COVID-19\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'Bairan, Aireen Grace T. | Cruz, Franklin Angelo D. | Junsay, Anne Franchezca DC. | Viri, Carlo R. | Vister, Angela S.'),
(38, 3, 'BSTM', ' INFLUENCE OF DIGITAL MARKETING OF TOURISM SERVICES AS PERCEIVED BY THE BS TOURISM MANAGEMENT STUDENTSOF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY', ' This study aims to know the influence of digital marketing in the purchasing decision of 3 and 4th year Tourism Management students of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus. The goal of the research is to know the significant relationship between the influence on the intention of respondents and tourism services in digital\r\nmarketing. The study showed that most of the students are between 20-30 years old, and most of the respondents are female. With their level of interest in tourism services being offered online, it shows that they strongly agree with these services such as attractions,\r\naccommodation, food and beverage, and package tours. On the other hand, the usage of digital media in purchasing these tourism services also had a result of strong agreement, including perceived ease of use, price, reviews, and promotions. Based on Pearson Correlation, the decision is to reject the null hypothesis, and accept the alternative hypothesis. Through the findings briefly discussed, this study led the researchers to conclude that there is a significant relationship between the influence on the intention of respondents and tourism services in digital marketing.\r\n', 2022, 'CALAYAG, ALFRED| DELA CRUZ, JELINE ELJAY  |  DELOS SANTOS, KYLA NICOLETTE  | LOPEZ, HERBIELYN PAYONGAYONG, | JEMUEL VELIZARIO, JELLIAH M.'),
(39, 6, 'BSTM', 'IMPACT OF ONLINE LEARNING TO THE MENTALHEALTH OF TOURISM STUDENT', 'The impact of online learning on the mental health of third-year tourism students\' results in difficulties as they are tired and unable to concentrate due to a variety of issues such as task, time, and expenses. Previous research has relied primarily on systematic screening to identify students who may require support. However, they are unaware of the significant impact that this has on students\' mental health. The researchers describe the population\'s characteristics using descriptive data. The researchers collected the data using a questionnaire form to learn about the circumstances affecting students during online classes and the differences between them and face-to-face classes. It will be useful to understand how the university and students adjust to and resolve such mental health issues in online classes. As a result, the researchers discover that the extent of the effect of online classes to the mental health of students in the following factor - Exhaustion has the highest weighted mean 3.28% among the other factors, indicating that they do feel drained while doing their school works. On the other hand, the researchers concluded that that time, task, and expenses had no significant impact during face-to-face classes.\r\n', 2022, 'CHAN, Ma. Katrina Annie P. | CONSTANTINO, Alliah Jazmine L. | CRISOSTOMO, Aileen M. | DEL ROSARIO, Aira Mae L. | MALAGSIC, Jhescile Marie S. | ONG, Daniel B.'),
(40, 13, 'BSTM', 'THE PERCEPTION OF DELIVERY RIDERS TOWARD THE ACCURACY OF TRANSPORTATION MOBILE APPLICATIONS', ' In today\'s modernizing world, the pervasive use of mobile technology has a significant impact on transportation; mobile applications have become one of the most important tools we use on a daily basis, both in our personal and professional lives. Mobile applications are commonly referred to as \"apps\" or \"mobile apps.\" Several crucial applications in today\'s society, including those related to communication, education, business, entertainment, travel, and social interaction, are made possible by these apps. For drivers who regularly experience traffic congestion, smartphone navigation apps like Waze and Google Maps have emerged as a favored option. Google Maps has remained the leading option ever since GPS turn-by-turn navigation was made available in 2008. (Samson, B.P. 2018). The purpose of this study is to ascertain how delivery riders feel about the reliability of smartphone applications for transportation, including those for navigating routes, traffic, destination services, weather updates, and accident-prone areas.\r\nUsing a survey questionnaire, this quantitative study evaluated the accuracy or otherwise of transportation mobile application perceptions by delivery riders from the Calumpit and Hagonoy locations. The majority of delivery riders who took part in the survey have a favorable opinion on how accurate transportation mobile apps are. The suggested strategy calls for at least twice-yearly updates to mobile applications for transportation. Riders who solely rely on the information provided by the app would tremendously benefit from this.\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Teressa A. Ballebas | Jaycel Ann C. Cruz | Daisy Ann P. Dugos | Rosewelle G. Tolentino'),
(41, 0, '0', 'CONTACTLESS PAYMENT IN THE TOURISM SERVICES: BARRIERS ANDBENEFITS ', 'The present study aims to examine the dynamic developments in contactless payment systems within the tourism industry of the Philippines, with a specific focus on the city of Malolos, located in the province of Bulacan. This study aims to comprehensively explore the obstacles and advantages linked to digital transactions. It investigates the chronological progression of contactless payment adoption, analyzing its effects prior to, during, and subsequent to the pandemic. In addition, it employs a qualitative research approach and utilizes a survey questionnaire to investigate the prevalence of Gash as a prominent payment method in the tourism industry. Specifically, the study encompasses both tourists and staff working in tourism services. Despite the presence of issues associated with internet access, the study reveals Gashs dominance in the payment landscape. The results underscore the advantages of expeditious transactions and heightened security, as seen by the offered strategies that underscore the necessity for increased offline functionalities and improved communication protocols during maintenance intervals. The findings of this study indicate that the resolution of recognized obstacles is of utmost importance for ensuring the long-term effectiveness of contactless payment implementation within the tourism industry in the Philippines.\r\nKeywords: contactless payments, Philippine tourism, Gash, digital transactions, technology adoption, pandemic impact, internet connectivity, user experiences\r\n', 2022, ' Innah Isabella D.C Faustino | Ivan Kurt M. Labysig | Gladys Ken T. Marcelino | Rheggie Ace T. Nocum'),
(42, 0, '0', 'SOCIAL MEDIA AS A TOOL FOR PROMOTING TOURIST DESTINATIONS IN THE MUNICIPALITY OF SAN RAFAEL, BULACAN', 'his research study focused on assessing the relationship of Social Media as a Tool for Promoting Tourist Destination in the Municipality of San Rafael, Bulacan, Philippines. As one of the popular tourist destinations in the province of Bulacan during the pandemic, the massive used of social media brought people to make plans on the destination they want to visit by just using the platform. Incorporating evidence from quantitative method through survey questionnaires, a variety of working personnel and tourists from different tourist destinations in San Rafael Bulacan, was asked to participate. A total of 100 respondents went through the data gathering process. The results showed that Facebook was the most popular and effective social media platform in promoting tourist destination using video-based contents that always attracts tourists\' interest. As supported in the study by Tjoe (2022), in which 51% of millennials claim that Facebook interactions have impacted or inspired their travel selections, this generation is equally open to social media. In addition, according to him, when you take into account how much individuals like sharing and recounting their travel experiences online, the significance of social media in the tourism business becomes abundantly evident. Overall, different social media platform helps promotes tourist destinations. In San Rafael, Bulacan. Keywords: social media, tourist destination, descriptive correlation, tourism, tourism promotion\r\n', 2022, 'Jefferson Manansala | Balingit, Aleli Joy G. | Mendiola, Ivy R.Ramos, | Allyssandra B.'),
(43, 0, '0', 'GREEN PRACTICES OF ACCOMMODATION AND LODGINGESTABLISHMENTS IN MALOLOS BULACAN:BASIS FOR SUSTAINABLE MANAGEMENT', 'The Hospitality-Tourism Industry is a sector that primarily served a large population and was one of the fastest-growing industries with a significant environmental impact. Green practices strive for a lush green environment; it was an excellent way to avoid environmental problems and encouraged guests to protect and care for nature while also improving the performance of the accommodation and lodging industry. Green\r\npractices strive to prevent adverse ecological effects by implementing waste reduction strategies and employing sustainable products and resources (Myung et al., 2012). This study aims to determine the green practices of Malolos, Bulacan\'s accommodation, and lodging establishments. This mixed-method study evaluated green practices in ten establishments used a surveyed questionnaire and interviews with the owners. This involves conserving water and energy, waste management, waste recycling, and supplying clean air. The ten businesses surveyed in Malolos, Bulacan, were actively engaged in green practices. It demonstrates that the respondent is willing to participate in our proposed plan and support environmentally friendly practices. The proposed plan was the Green Sustainable Management Plan. It encourages them to pursue sustainable practices while also providing resources to assist them in doing so. The Green Sustainable Plan aims to establish long-term goals and strategies for maintaining programs, activities, and collaborations in a way that does not deplete the resources of future generations.\r\nKeywords: Green Practices, Accommodation, Tourism, Environmental, Sustainable\r\n', 2022, 'Acebo, Precious Keye G. | Andres, Christine Joy DC. | Mata, Cyrell B.| Mercado, Ghinila S.'),
(44, 7, 'BSTM', 'A REVIEW IN THE ISSUES IN THE RAPID GROWTH OF DELIVERY SERVICES IN MALOLOS BULACAN', ' Business is one of the most important parts of the economy as the Covid-19 started, some businesses went bankrupt and everything goes online even the essential needs of the community is depending on online delivery especially when the community quarantine started. The government launched an emergency subsidy program with massive public spending to support disrupted households and businesses. Six months after the March lockdown, the Philippine economy has moved to the recovery stage, but micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises. \"Food Delivery on the Rise Due to COVID-19 Lockdown\" according to business wire with more people that are stuck at home during the Covid-19 outbreak most likely get to order food essentials and home supplies that they might need since people are unable to get outside.\r\nSocial Distancing is a must that\'s why people are not allowed to gather to prevent the spreading of the disease, you can\'t attend any birthday party, reunion, holy mass, and even enjoy by going to the mall. Dine-ins are not allowed during the lockdown. If you want to order food you\'ll be needing a delivery service in order to satisfy and enjoy yourself eating delicious foods.\r\nThe number of restaurants that do online delivery is increasing as the demand of the customer gets higher. Groceries are now opening into online grocery platforms and riders can able to support their families with it. Though some riders are scared to get infected by the disease they need to do it for their family is able to survive.\r\n', 2022, 'Alvarez, Jackyline P. | Cabrera, Erika Mariz V. | Cruz, Roselle R. | Dela Cruz, Pamela L. | Del Monte, Irene P. | Pagsanghan, Ritchelle'),
(45, 0, '0', ' EVALUATION OF THE DOÑA REMEDIOS TRINIDAD ECOTOURISM SITES:INPUT FOR SUSTAINABLE MANAGEMENT', 'The study aims to convey the significance of this study so that we know that in the beauty of this area, we must know what concerns need to be solved. To preserve the natural beauty of Doña Remedios Trinidad. Tourists come from all over the archipelago to see the natural beauty of the Doña Remedios Trinidad ecotourism destination. The 93,000 hectares of land were underdeveloped at the time, with little to no infrastructure and highways connecting to neighboring towns, forcing locals to work in an industry that kills trees for profit. Communities take waste management seriously, and littering is a serious environmental threat, but the DRT is concerned with more than just trash. Five suspected illegal loggers were recently apprehended in a barangay in neighboring Camachin in a joint operation by local police, the DENR municipality\'s Department of Environment and Natural Resources, Baliwag, and NPC-Awat. Furthermore, climate change is a looming issue that can have an impact on communities. As a result, they have taken steps to ensure biodiversity protection. Pollution is also a constant issue, and tour guides are responsible for taking action when rules are broken. The Environmental Awareness Act, Republic Act 9512, was enacted by the government to promote environmental awareness through environmental education and other purposes.', 2022, ' Manalo, Mary Ann N. | Quitain, Remileen Joy  lS'),
(46, 5, 'BSTM', 'PROJECT PLANNING FOR BICYCLE TOURISM IN DOÑA REMEDIOS TRINIDAD, BULACAN', 'The study looked into the viability of bicycle tourism in Doña Remedios Trinidad, province of Bulacan. The majority of people have immediately embraced cycling as an\r\nalternate mode of transportation. For this study, the researcher used a mixed method to gather data.\r\nThe researcher distributed survey questionnaires, consisting of two Likert tables and an open-ended question, to 50 locals and 50 cyclists using random\r\nsampling. The data gathered was then analyzed by finding the mean. The study discovered that Doña Remedios Trinidad, Bulacan, is a\r\nfavorable location for planning of bicycle tourism in the region, but it lacks\r\nthe necessary infrastructure to facilitate its implementation. The researchers\r\ntherefore suggested that the government allocate money for project planning that will enable innovation in Doña Remedios Trinidad. Additionally, this\r\nwill help develop a variety of tourist-oriented activities that will benefit the\r\nlocals by giving them a reliable source of income for their daily needs. Doña\r\nRemedios Trinidad will become well-known among both domestic and\r\ninternational visitors, particularly those who enjoy cycling for recreation and\r\ntravel. If those facilities, infrastructure, or businesses are developed in particular locations, this study may create an opportunity and have an economic impact.\r\nKeywords: Bicycle Tourism, Economic Impact, Government, Planning, Infrastructure.\r\n', 2022, 'Balmedina, Zean Khyle E. | Matic, Melanie C. | Reyes, Mart Andrea M. | Santos, Lovely Rose E.'),
(47, 2, 'BSTM', 'THE READINESS OF COLLEGE STUDENTS WITH REGARDS TO UPCOMINGFACE TO FACE CLASSES IN THE MIDST OF COVID-19 PANDEMIC', 'The Readiness of College Students with Regards to Upcoming Face To Face Classes in the Midst of Covid-19 Pandemic was conducted in Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus. The goal of this study is to know and understand the perception of every college student for the upcoming face-to-face classes. This research was able to gather information to reach its goal and determine if there\'s a significant relationship between the factors that affect the academic readiness of college students and the level of the college student\'s Social Readiness, in the matter of factors affecting their academic readiness such as financial, self-directed learning, learning interest and classroom environment. and their level of Social Readiness which includes Physical Health, Motivation, Self-Competence, and Preparedness. The study showed that most of the students are between 20-23 years old and most of the respondents are female. The researcher found out that 49 out of 50 respondents are fully vaccinated. To collect all this information, the researcher utilized Google Forms with a series of questions. All the data that the researcher has gathered will be used to determine the readiness of college students.\r\n', 2022, 'Dela Cruz, Jean Michelle| Dionisio, Juvelle Galvez, Elenila| Magtira, Lowel Maldo, Mica Merl Maracha, Alyssa Mae | Vinuya, Joyce'),
(48, 12, 'BSTM', 'RISK ASSESSMENT OF HAGONOY, BULACAN: INPUT FOR SUSTAINABLE TOURISM PROGRAMS', 'An overview of the Risk assessment of Hagonoy, Bulacan, and its potential contribution to sustainable tourism programs are provided in this abstract. Hagonoy, Bulacan, a town in the Philippines\' central Luzon province, is well-known for its historical sites, rich cultural history, and scenic features. An extensive investigation of the town\'s physical, social, economic, and cultural aspects that have an impact on the tourism business was part of the environmental scanning process. According to the findings, Hagonoy is home to a variety of pristine beaches, mangrove forests, and bird sanctuaries, all of which can be used to create sustainable tourist initiatives.\r\n\r\nThe community must urgently address a number of environmental issues, including deforestation, soil erosion, and water contamination. According to the report, initiatives for creating sustainable tourism can be created by combining environmental protection with the preservation of cultural assets and local economies. Policymakers, tourist planners, and other stakeholders can benefit greatly from the study\'s findings when creating sustainable tourism initiatives that support the town\'s economy and environment while conserving its cultural history\r\n', 2022, 'Castro, Alwyn S. | Amoroso, Alliyah Nicole M. | Lasam, Allysa Shane S.'),
(49, 0, '0', 'POST COVID 19: BEST PRACTICES IN HOTEL OPERATION IN SELECTED RESORT HOTELS IN BULACAN, PHILIPPINES', ' COVID-19, caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus, has significantly impacted the tourism and hospitality industry, leading to strict sanitary standards, preventative measures, and social distancing measures. The goal of the study is to identify the best practices that were implemented by a selected resort hotel in Bulacan, Philippines during the pandemic and maintained until post-pandemic.\r\n\r\nThe researchers applied a quantitative method that included collecting measurable data for statistical analysis of a population sample. A survey questionnaire was personally distributed by the researcher to chosen Resort Hotel establishments in Bulacan, Philippines. Part I of the questionnaire contains personal information from selected Resort Hotels, Parts II, III, and IV contain the quantitative element of the questionnaire. A 4-point Likert scale questionnaire will be used by the researcher to collect information regarding the best practices and obstacles faced by chosen hotels in the following years of the COVID-19 outbreak. A Likert scale, according to (Nikolopoulou, 2022), is a rating system used to assess beliefs, attitudes, or behaviors. In the study, respondents\' responses were recorded for accuracy. The researchers conclude that most of the respondents have been operating for 8-11 years which means they encountered different types of circumstances, and they experienced the pandemic era, which qualified them to answer the survey. When the pandemic hit, there were major issues with COVID-19 and the \"new normal\" protocols, which were extremely challenging due to the increase in competitors. The researchers would like to recommend to the owners to have a brainstorming or open conversation with the employees always especially when having challenges that are tough to face.\r\n\r\nKeywords: COVID-19 pandemic, resort hotels, best practices, new normal,challenges\r\n', 2022, '  Gaspar, Maila M.| Domingo, Mary Angeline V.| Ocmar, Jay Zell P.| Santos, Kirsten Owen N.'),
(50, 19, 'BSTM', 'THE IMPACT OF DIGITAL TECHNOLOGY IN TRAVEL DESTINATIONS IN MALOLOS AND HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'Digital technology has already changed the way of doing business. Technology has aided not only businesses but also society and the ability to grow as individuals. Technological advancements, the emergence of social networks, and the expanding convenience with which services can be purchased have all contributed to enterprises becoming more versatile. It should also be emphasized that a service provider\'s primary success factor is customer satisfaction. As a result, any service provider should strive to provide high-quality services while maintaining a high level of customer satisfaction Adesina and Chinoso (2015). This research will focus on how Digital Technology Impacts Travel Destinations in the area of Malolos and Hagonoy Bulacan. This mixed-method study evaluated the impact of Digital Technology in Travel Destinations in ten establishments using a survey questionnaire and interviews with the owners. This involves the digital technologies being utilized by tourist in choosing travel destination, the positive and negative impacts of digital technologies on travel destinations, the online platforms most commonly used in travel destinations, most effective and convenient for tourists and if there is an impact of digital technology towards travel destination. The ten businesses surveyed in Malolos and Hagonoy Bulacan, were actively engaged in digital technologies. The studies propose that digital technologies have a significant impact on the travel destinations of any businesses, that is why focus more on what specific digital technology is commonly used and useful in the travel industry.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Digital Technology, Travel Destinations, Tourism, Impact, Tourist\r\n', 2023, 'CATAJAN, Jam Meryll C. | HERNANDEZ, Ailene N. | LICUP, Rochelle Y. | LOPEZ, Angelica Mae DC'),
(51, 8, 'BSTM', 'CHOOSY SKY: FACTORS INFLUENCING THE BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY MAIN AND HAGONOY CAMPUS 4TH YEAR TOURISM STUDENTS\' DECISION TO WORK FOR AN AIRLINE', 'The role of the factors that are affecting the 4th year tourism students of Bulacan State University Main and Hagonoy Campus. The aim of this study was to determine which is the most important factor which may affect the; (1) Demographic profile, (2) Benefits, (3) Extent Benefits.\r\n\r\nThis was a descriptive and quantitative research, and the population was gathered by quota sampling, just because the focus of this study was the students of 4th year students in the Main Campus and Hagonoy Campus. The factors include: age, gender, civil status, and their campus. It also includes: compensation, working environment, benefits and the development opportunities.\r\n\r\nEighty five students were given the survey questionnaire through their Facebook Messenger which proceeded directly to the factors and the influences which may affect their decisions in choosing the airline that they want to work with. As a results of the survey, by getting the mean and the standard deviation it shows that students of Bulacan State University Malolos Campus and also the students of Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus, influences the factors by choosing their airline to work which means the; (a) Compensation, (b) Working Environment, (c) Benefits, and (d) Development Opportunities was very much agree.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Employability, Labor-market, Airline\r\n', 2022, ' FLORES, Rhonie Joy | GUEVARRA, King Samuel | LIBAO, Marilyn Joie | MENDIOLA, Edwin | PASCUAL, Hannah Mica | POSUGAC, Micaella | SAN JOSE, Arriza Miccaela'),
(52, 4, 'BSTM', 'COPING MECHANISM OF SELECTED LODGING ESTABLISHMENT IN BULACAN AMIDST OF PANDEMIC', ' A study of coping mechanism of selected lodging establishment in Bulacan was conducted in order to find out where the lodging establishments are located in order to gain information such as their demographic profiles, the flow of operations, and the strategie plan they have adopted to cope during a crisis, as well as to determine if there are any significant issues relationship between the profile of the respondents. The study implied the use of quantitative research method which aids the objective of the study. In addition, the study found that in the midst of the pandemic, hotel businesses are confronting various challenges, but the study also indicated that lodging establishments have implied an adopted strategical plan to survive and continue their operations even during the pandemic. The aim of the study is to assess the coping mechanism of selected lodging establishments in Bulacan amidst the pandemic and make an intervention based on the findings of the study. The ability of lodging establishments to operate in times of crisis would be improved by addressing their coping strategies in the factors that impact their working environment. It can be differentiated in a consistent manner depending on the significant facets of a coping strategies such as the employment of strategical plans. The study makes use of a descriptive type of research to obtain the needed data from the 50 respondents, who are employees and managers. Through use of Google forms as an electronic questionnaire is used to collect data. The questionnaire is divided into five sections based on the demographic profile of the lodging establishments, demographic profile of the respondents, the effect of pandemic to the flow of operations, the relationship between the profile of the lodging establishment and the strategical plans adopted during the pandemic, and the relationship between the strategical plans adopted during the pandemic.\r\n', 2022, 'Cruz, Johnrehj Yuuka G. |  Espiritu, Glaidel G. |  Halili, Mikee G. |  Hernandez, Angelika Raine  G. |  Maclang, Aira Mace G. |  Tolentino, Angelica L.'),
(53, 14, 'BSTM', 'TOURISM STUDENT’S TRAVEL DECISIONS AS INFLUENCED BY SOCIAL MEDIA ', 'The paragraph highlights the many facets of travel as well as the pervasive influence of social media on tourism decisions. It underlines how travel is more than just discovery; it is also an enriching experience that exposes people to various cultures and ideas. With platforms affecting ideas, judgments, and perceptions of destinations, social media has become a dominant force impacting travel choices.\r\nIt emphasizes social media\'s significant role in the tourism sector, altering perceptions and influencing decisions through user-generated content and reviews. The essay investigates the overwhelming global presence of social media users, emphasizing its impact on many parts of life such as leisure, education, and travel.\r\nFurthermore, it recognizes the negative consequences of unfavorable evaluations and opinions on places, which can have a considerable influence on tourism and local economies. Social networking website became a primary means of communication and entertainment when the COVID-19 pandemic made travel restrictions more severe.\r\nThe study\'s goal is to learn how social media influences tourism students\' travel planning decisions. It aims to find the most influential social media channels and key aspects influencing their travel decisions. Finally, the project aims to equip tourism students with the knowledge they need to make informed judgments about vacation planning by utilizing the power of social media.\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Agustin, Rose Camille D. | Bartolome, Maelah M. | Casao, Gunesa M. | Francisco, Jaymillou'),
(54, 0, '0', 'THE BREAKING DAWN OF THE FOOD ESTABLISHMENTS INMALOLOS, BULACAN', 'The pandemic had a significant impact on the global industry. When it comes to the food supply chain, there\'s a serious concern about food production, handling, distribution, transport, limited work opportunities, and demand due to the COVID-19 crisis.\r\nWith that, the study\'s objective is to gather information about the resiliency to recover food businesses despite the pandemic\'s rapid outbreak and to determine how\r\nMalolos and Bulacan food enterprises deal with and engage with the new normal.\r\nThis study was conducted at Malolos, Bulacan. Q questions are focused on how\r\nrestaurants can deal with resilience. The respondents are the managers and crew members of the abovementioned food establishment in Malolos, Bulacan.\r\nAccording to the study\'s findings, food outlets in Malolos, Bulacan has adapted to the covid-19 new normal. They already provide certain ways to help them survive and grow their business. Despite the difficulties, they continue to run their food establishment and\r\nadapt to the new standards. Most owners/ managers/ crew owners are aware of the new normal and are actively planning measures and tactics to maintain their company in line\r\nwith the new paradigm.\r\nThe correlation between the type of food facility and the tactics utilized during a pandemic was investigated using a chi-square test of independence. The connection between the variables is not significant since the chi-square value of 18.08 is less than the crucial chi-square value of 31.41. Meaning, the sorts of institutions are unaffected by the strategies utilized. Depending on their preferences, individual establishments may employ a variety of strategies.\r\nResiliency is the capability of an organization to survive an accustomed crisis and grow vigorously in a world that is full of uncertainties. It is a system that identifies the\r\nthreats coming and moving forward to combat the battle of the crisis. To help the restaurant organization in pandemic times, this study entitled \"Breaking Dawn of Food Establishment in Malolos, Bulacan\" was conducted. This study proposed a resiliency framework for establishment focusing on the resiliency after the pandemic crisis. The future study aimed to look at the recent changes that businesses have implemented to protect their employees and customers from this infectious virus.\r\nResearchers recommend that food establishment owners/managers have backup plans, especially in terms of changing their practices in times of a pandemic. They should engage\r\nin maintaining the protocols to ensure the safety of their customers as well as their employees. And during the pandemic, food establishment businesses should consider raising advertising to stimulate recovery and as a way of informative communication with\r\ncustomers, providing important security instructions.', 2022, 'APOSTOL, KATHLEEN ANGELA MARIE P. | BAUTISTA, DANICA Q. | DELA CRUZ, JAZLYN M. | MANLA, RIA RAY ROMELA G. | NICOLAS, ANJILLIAN A. | SUMAWAY, JHURY D.'),
(55, 0, '0', 'HANDLING OF PPE\'S: THE CASE OF HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'The focus of this descriptive quantitative study was to examine the effects of personal protective equipment (PPE) waste disposal on the ecosystem of Hagonoy, Bulacan. In particular, it focused on the handling of PPE in terms of disposing and recycling. According to a recent study of Svennevig (2021), individuals use PPE and dispose of an estimated 129 billion per month, the most of which are disposables made of microfiber plastic, which is regarded as a major danger to our environment.\r\n\r\nHagonoy, Bulacan is bordered by several bodies of water; high tides and floods are typical in the community, and results revealed that there was no particular procedure communicated to locals regarding the proper PPE disposal. The locals disposed of the PPE by throwing it in just about anywhere, where it is carried by the tides and swept into lakes and rivers. It also adds to sewage stagnation, resulting in severe floods. Thus, the researchers believed that it is detrimental to bodies of water and the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nIn terms of recycling, the majority of respondents do not recycle because they lack sufficient information on how to securely recycle used PPE. The results suggest that there is a lack of information dissemination on how to properly dispose and recycle PPE. It is urged that the local government, private institutions, foundations, or advocates of environmental protection organize seminars, training, or programs to inform, educate, and guide residents on how to properly dispose and recycle PPE.\r\n', 2022, 'Alberto, Ericka Rose | Delos Santos, Hannah | Laderas, Candido | Lopez, Sheryl | Santos, Josielyn | Sebastian, Ronnel | Villarías, Renz'),
(56, 34, 'BSHM', 'SALARY AND JOB PERFORMANCE OF EMPLOYEES IN SELECTED RESORTS IN BULACAN', 'The researchers conducted the study to assess how salary affects the job performance of resort employees in selected resorts in Bulacan. This study was conducted as well to determine what are the possible effects of salary to the job motivation and employee retention of employees in hospitality industry specifically the employees of selected resorts in Bulacan.\r\nThe effect of salary to the job performance, employee retention and job motivation were determined by using purposive sampling technique to answer the research problems given throughout data collection. By using questionnaires as research instrument, the result showed that most of the respondents of the research strongly agreed that salary has an effect on job performance, job motivation and employee retention of employees.\r\nBased on these results, the researchers recommend for resort owners to pay attention to the level of\r\nsalary they provide to employees as this can affect the job performance of employees as well as their intention to stay in their job and their motivation to work.\r\n', 2024, ' ABADILLA, DEXTER JOHN S. | CANTONA, MONICA JANE L. | PACULBA, NECY Y.  | SANTOS, REZ GABRIEL DL.');
INSERT INTO `thesisbooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(57, 38, 'BSHM', 'IMPORTANT FACTORS AFFECTING GENERATION ZCHOICE OF RESTAURANT', 'The Important Factors Affecting Generation Z Choice of Restaurant was conducted in Bulacan State University - Hagony Campus. The goal of this study is to know and understand the factors that affect Generation Z choice of restaurant in Hagonoy, Bulacan in terms of services, food menu items, environment, and experience. This study was able to gather information to reach its goal.\r\nThe researchers conducted a survey through simple random sampling that validated a questionnaire by their adviser to gather all the quantitative data. The outcome of the study may benefit several people Generation Z, students, restaurant staff.\r\nThis study determined the consumer behavior of Generation Z when it comes in choice of restaurant. The study showed that most of the Gen Z respondents are the Generation Is aged 15 to 25 years old. All the data that the researcher gathered will be used to determine the factors that can affect the choice of restaurant of the Generation Z.\r\nTo collect all this information, the researcher utilized a survey questionnaire. All\r\nthe data that the researcher gathered will be used to determine the factors of Generation Z in the choice of a restaurant.\r\nThe researcher believes that the study may benefit from several people.\r\nBenefiting the several people of gen Z in various sectors as: Hospitality Management Students, Restaurant Staff, Entrepreneurs, Market Development and the Researchers.\r\nThis study may help the Gen Z level of understanding in logical thinking in line with consumer behavior and their decision-making.\r\nThe study may help the future researchers to broaden their knowledge about Gen Z customer behavior and decision-making in Choice of Restaurant. It may also serve as ideas for them in the future.\r\nKeywords: factors affecting generation z, selecting restaurant, menu items, decision making, consumer behavior, environment, experience, services\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'AGUINALDO, RUTH L. | EUSEBIO, LESLIE ANNE B. | SANTOS, ANA MARHIA FEI A. | SANTOS, MARY JOY M.'),
(58, 42, 'BSHM', 'EXPLORING SUSTAINABLE MARKETING APPROACHES ADAPTED BY THE FOOD SERVICE INDUSTRY DURING COVID-19 PANDEMIC', 'Sustainability issues are becoming increasingly important in the hospitality sector during crisis times such as COVID-19 and post-pandemic. In order to synthesize the literature on sustainable practices in hospitality, the researchers developed a systematic literature to illustrate the dominant sustainable practices in hospitality. The COVID-19 pandemic significantly affects the advancement of Business entertainers should track down the right technique to make due. One of the procedures during the pandemic is computerized showcasing, which permits business entertainers to advertise their items without being compelled by arrangements during the pandemic. Research on advanced promoting techniques for business entertainers to contend in\r\nthis pandemic time utilizes subjective strategies with a logical distinct methodology.\r\nDuring the Covid-19 outbreak, researchers investigated marketing techniques and industry trends in a sample of restaurants in Hagonoy, Bulacan. Furthermore, The researchers targets to attract ages 20-40 below for the restaurants in Hagonoy Bulacan. As a result, there is often a gap between sustainable marketing efforts and consumer demands. Those demands can be unrealistic in terms of the cost of compliance and the time required to after production processes.\r\nSustainable marketing makes sense only as part of a strategy that will guide all of the actions of a business, not just product development, sales, and marketing. Since governments are slow to take up the challenge the future of the planet depends on the actions taken by companies to protect the environment and create a better society.\r\n', 2024, 'Bernardino, Princess M.| De Belen, Jenifer P. | Sacdalan, Roby Jeanger | Tarona, Lyca DB.'),
(59, 43, 'BSHM', 'AN ANALYSIS OF THE EFFECTIVENESS AND EFFICIENCY OF USING GREEN PRACTICES AMONG THE SELECTED RESTAURANTS IN MALOLOS', 'The present study evaluates the advantages and disadvantages of implementing environmentally friendly practices. It also seeks the specific and intuitive methods by which the selected restaurants employ these procedures. The researchers identified the key green practices that influence the perceptions of a restaurant\'s image among customers and restaurant personnel, but only among environmentally conscious people. These practices include the use of recyclable take-out containers, proper waste management (reduce, reuse, recycle), basic sanitation, especially in light of the pandemic, and minor modifications like energy-efficient lighting and water\r\nconservation.\r\nThis study aims to measure the challenges and benefits of implementing green practices among the restaurants. Shedding light on how these practices contribute to environmental\r\nconservation, it aims to analyze implementation and impact of green practices in hospitality industry especially in the restaurants.\r\n', 2024, 'Caraan, Raphael Mari F. | Flores, Angela Joyce C. | Javier, Kristine Anne R. | Manahan, Chrizelle Jie S.'),
(60, 37, 'BSHM', 'DIGITAL MARKETING TECHNIQUES: POSSIBILITIES FOR THE NEW NORMAL', 'The primary objective of this literature review is to examine the digital marketing techniques used by selected restaurants in Malolos, Bulacan amidst the COVID-19 pandemic. In this case, effective marketing enables the collection of data to understand more about the targeted consumers, allowing advertising and other strategies to be more directed\r\nIn addition, this was initiated to learn and find the importance of digital marketing techniques\r\nof restaurants work. Based on the literature review, the researchers identified the following themes: search engine optimization (SEO), search engine marketing (SEM), social media marketing (SMM), content marketing (CM), affiliate marketing (AM), native advertising (NA), marketing automation (MA), pay-per-click (PPC), and email marketing (EM).\r\nIn conclusion, digital marketing has surpassed traditional marketing. The consumer are looking\r\nand searching more on internet to. In this study, we acknowledged that restaurants can really benefit from Digital Marketing such as search engine optimization (SEO), search engine\r\nmarketing (SEM), social media marketing (SMM), content marketing (CM), affiliate marketing\r\n(AM), native advertising (NA), marketing automation (MA), pay-per-click (PPC), and email marketing (EM), e-books, optical disks and games and are becoming more and more common in our advancing technology. It is demonstrated that we all are connected through whatsapp and facebook and the increasing use of social media is creating new opportunities for digital marketers to attract the customers through digital platform. Awareness of consumer\'s motives is important\r\nbecause it provides a deeper understanding of what influences users to create content about a brand or store. Digital marketing is cost effective and having a great commercial impact on the restaurants. Based on this study, it can further be argued that knowing which social media sites a company\'s target market utilizes is another key factor in guaranteeing that restaurants marketing will be successful. The effectiveness of Internet marketing with respect to different business can be analyzed. The study can further be extended to compare the digital marketing techniques with\r\nspecific to various businesses.\r\n', 2024, 'Carlos, Andrea Mae D. | Dela Cruz, Piel Rona A. | Magaling, Raymart M.| Velasquez, Aljon M.'),
(61, 2, 'BEED', 'THE INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCES OF PRE-SERVICE TEACHERS AND THEIR PURSUIT OF FUTURE CAREER IN TEACHING', 'This research study explored the internship experiences of Pre-Service Teachers (PSTs) and their pursuit in teaching careers. The study aimed to explore the PSTs profile, their internship experiences and factors influencing their teaching career decisions to proposed an action plan to support PSTs teaching careers. This quantitative study utilized descriptive research design and data were collected using stratified random sampling among 133 PSTs-respondents through a three-part survey questionnaire. The research Instrument includes questions for profiling, rating scale on internship experiences, career motivations for pursuing teaching and their level of interest in pursuing teaching career as their future career. The Internship experiences with cooperating teachers and learning experiences were strongly agreed by the PSTs. The factors influencing the PSTs teaching pursuit includes personal motivations and their interests towards teaching and their perceived benefits of teaching as a profession. The PSTs strongly agreed to pursue their teaching career. An action plan was proposed by the researchers which will target mentorship for effective teaching, portfolio development, and job fair. Active participation of PSTs in professional development activities conducted by the university, strengthening university career guidance, and annual tracer studies were recommended in the study. Keywords: Pre-Service Teachers, Internship Experiences, Motivation, Teaching Career\r\n', 2024, 'Baje, Karla B. | Clemente Lara C. | Dayandayan Joana Joy S. | Embuscado Danica Chenny G. | Guevarra Jhona M. | Lim, Ayhizza Jhoy D.'),
(62, 7, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'BREAKING THROUGH THE DISTANCE: INTEGRATING INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATION TECHNOLOGY TOOLS IN REINFORCING WRITING SKILLS ', 'The use of Information and Communications Technology in the arena of modern language learning is no longer a choice but a necessity that gives life to the different vistas of how the English language is effectively taught and learned outside the four-walled room.\r\nIn language learning, having exposure to ICT tools such as word processors and word enhancement is indeed an impactful experience in breaking the distance given by virtual classrooms today— most especially in reinforcing writing skills. Therefore, the study was particularly zoomed in Bulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus, with quota sampling of 150 students from three departments namely, the Hospitality and Tourism Management, the Information Communication and Technology Program, and the Teacher Education Program during the Academic Year 2021-2022. A descriptive survey questionnaire was utilized to examine the measurable relationship between the variables accurately. And as the data heavily suggested, respondents in the 4th-year level dominated the number of responses. Microsoft Word and Grammarly were the most used ICT tools to improve their writing, particularly on writing essays, as the respondents enjoyed its features, such as bulleted and numbered lists that help them organize their ideas in a document and checks their misspelled and confused words. Gaining the full awareness of the different word processing and word enhancement tools and their features has been interpreted, as they habitually used them to write academic papers, particularly essays, but least on composting e-mails. Hence, the possibility that the interruption of the use of these ICT tools might result in the discontinuance of practicing writing skills compared to traditional pen-and-\r\npaper writing.\r\nkeywords: Information and Communication Technology (ICT tools), language learning, word processing tools, word enhancement tools, writing, academic papers\r\n', 2022, 'ABANTE, ANA KARINA S. | BALTAZAR, REAH MHEY S. | BAUTISTA, JANELA MARIE L. | MERCADO, NICOLE ALLIAH M. | SALAMAT, CARESH B. | SANTOS, DANNIEL T.'),
(63, 5, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'SECONDARY ENGLISH TEACHERS PERCEPTIONSON MEMES AS A STRATEGY IN TEACHING GRAMMAR AND LITERATURE', 'his study focuses on the perceptions of the Secondary English teachers on Memes as a strategy in teaching Grammar and Literature. In order to know the perceptions of teachers in the proposed study, the researchers sought the following statement of the problem; (1) how may the profile of respondents be described in terms of: age, gender, educational attainment and number of years in teaching? (2) How may the perceptions of the teachers in using memes as strategy in teaching Literature be describe in terms of:\r\nLanguage of memes, Word Construction Methods, Abbreviation, Contraction, Grammatical Structures, Capitalization, Use of punctuation, Rhetorical Pattern, Text and Image. (3) To what extent is the level of acceptability of memes to the secondary English Teachers as a strategy in teaching Grammar and Literature? (4) What are the intervention\r\nprograms that can be crafted from the study? This study signifies the following; students, teachers, and future researchers in many ways. The researchers used legitimately made survey questionnaire and interview guide questions for the respondents so that the researchers will know their perceptions in the proposed study. To sum up the findings of the study, Memes are acceptable to use as a strategy in teaching Grammar and Literature.\r\nFurthermore, the proposed study will be recommended to the English teachers for them to know its effectivity inside the classroom, next will be, the future researchers for them to use this study as their reference in enhancing this academic research paper.\r\nKeywords: Memes, Strategy, Literature, Grammar and Perceptions\r\n', 2019, 'Karen R. Cruz | Marilou B. Cruz | Eloisa Marielle E. Garcelis | Rhiena Mae M. Mercado | Glomer P. Sebastian | Jasmin B. Sierte | Janine Erica DC. Terrado'),
(64, 4, 'BEED', 'CHALLENGES IN EDUCATION DETERMINING THE HOME - BASEDPRACTICES OF PARENTS, TEACHERS AND PUPILS', 'The turn towards home-based learning has made it imperative to have a clear idea regarding the practices adopted by teachers, pupils, and parents outside the classroom. This research was meant to understand the different challenges related to such practices and especially the increased reliance on remote learning of course, due to unwarranted circumstances like the COVID-19 pandemic.\r\nThrough quantitative means, data was obtained through surveys, interviews, and studies of participants from rural school in Hagonoy, Bulacan.\r\nThe primary aim is to identify challenges in post-pandemic home-based educational practices and evaluate the demographic profiles, practices, frequency, and specific challenges faced by parents, teachers, and pupils. The study also seeks to develop pedagogical recommendations based on these insights.\r\nThis study employs Descriptive Research Design. The respondents in this quantitative study consist of four teachers, grade 3 pupils, and parents of the grade 3 pupils for the school year 2023-2024. Non-probability sampling is employed to select specific respondents with an interest in the studys topic. These questionnaires utilized to gather information from the respondents at Teodora Cruz Elementary School in the Municipality of Hagonoy, Bulacan. The survey questionnaires contain 4 parts the respondents will be given a different set of questions. Keywords: Home-Based, Challenges, COVID-19, post-pandemic, practices\r\n', 2024, 'Enriquez, Trina B. | Galman, John Isidro G. | Javier, Reigne Ashly D. | Pablo, Aliczzandra C. | Velasco, Ma. Carmella L. | Villanueva, Pamfilo Jr '),
(65, 18, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'LANGUAGE USAGE IN RELIGIOUS SPACE: A LINGUISTIC LANDSCAPE STUDY OF OUR LADY OF MT. CARMEN PARISH - BARASOAIN CHURCH', ' This study describes the linguistic landscape (LL) of Our Lady of Mount Carmel Parish - Barasoain Church, one of the historical religious buildings in The Philippines. The study was conducted to learn the present languages in Barasain Church that correlate to the following elements: language used, types of signs, orthographic features, material choice, placement within the area, and communicative functions categorized by Mary Funicchiaro & Brumfit, (1983, pp. 65-66). Mixed data were made to identify the said elements. Finally, the results revealed based on the language use and material choice that the signages in the church of Barasoain do not adhere to the National Building Code of The Philippines Presidential Decree 1096, Section 5 of Administrative Order No. 160, Chapter 20, Philippine Rules and Regulations on Signs and Linguistic Landscaping and the 2007\r\nAdditional Rules and Regulations in Presidential Decree 1096.\r\nThe researchers recommended the following; Firstly, add more elements to linguistic landscape such as grammar, and dimension of the signages. Secondly, the researchers advised the future researchers who will conduct this study to comeback to\r\nBarasoain Church, and analyze if the said Church make some changes or if they finally adhere to the Presidential Decree 1096, Lastly, the researchers suggested ways and tactics to further inform the people and the public about the Presidential Decree 1096.\r\n', 2024, 'De Leon, Christelle Joyce L. | Dela Cruz, Cristine T. | Magaling, Rica Joy P. | Salguet, Johnaflor T. | Santos, Marlon C '),
(66, 21, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'VOCABULARY BUILDING IN EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION THROUGH YOUTUBE KIDS VIDEOS', 'The growing reliance on digital media platforms in the 21st century calls for a more efficient and effective usage of YouTube Kids videos. The primary objective of this study was to describe the effects of utilizing YouTube Kids videos on vocabulary building among early childhood learners at Bulihan Day Care Center in the City of Malolos, Bulacan. The study used a mixed method research design to describe the effects of using YouTube Kids videos on the vocabulary building of early childhood learners. It helped in describing the effects of YouTube Kids videos on early childhood learners. The researchers used observation notes to gather qualitative data and quantitative data. This research revealed that vocabulary building indeed occurs through various key elements, namely repetition of words, paralanguage, asking questions, and creating sentences. Repetition of words is one of the undeniably evident occurrences among the respondents. The early childhood learners showed significant vocabulary building when it comes to repetition of words, which all the learners did repeat different content words. Vocabulary building through paralanguage, the same with repetition of words, is highly evident among the students, showing almost all of the learners performed paralanguage related to the word. When it comes to asking questions, three-quarters of the learners asked questions using or about the words. Lastly, creating sentences is also as evident as repetition of words, showing that all learners created sentences using the words from the videos they watched. Based on these, both repetition of words and creating sentences are considered as significant elements in vocabulary building, while both paralanguage and asking questions are also valuable elements of vocabulary building. The findings highlighted the potential of digital media as an essential material for supplementing vocabulary instruction in early childhood education. Keywords: vocabulary building, YouTube Kids videos, digital media platforms, language education\r\n', 2024, 'Castillo, Pauline Lie Andrei O. | Felipe, Ronnel L. | Galicia, John Carlo A.| Lopez, Marielle Liezel E. | Reyes, Kyla S.'),
(67, 6, 'BEED', 'A JOURNEY TO MINIMALIST CLASSROOM: TEACHER PRACTICES ON THE IMPLEMENTATION OF DEPED ORDER NO. 21 S. 2023', 'This study explores the implementation of minimalist classroom practices in select schools in Hagonoy, Bulacan, in response to the Department of Education (DepEd) Order No. 21, Series of 2023, also known as the Brigada Eskwela Guidelines.\r\nThe order aims to promote student concentration and participation by removing excessive decorations in classrooms. This study explores teachers\' practices and views of minimalist classroom designs, focusing on design and décor components, and assesses the implied efficacy of these activities.\r\nUsing a mixed-methods approach, data were collected through surveys and interviews with elementary school teachers from kindergarten to grade 6. The findings reveal that minimalist classroom practices, characterized by simplicity and functional design, positively influence student focus and reduce distractions. Teachers reported that a well-organized, clutter-free environment enhances learning outcomes by fostering a more conducive atmosphere for student engagement.\r\nData were acquired using a mixed-methods approach, including surveys and interviews with primary school instructors from kindergarten to sixth grade. The findings show that minimalist classroom methods, defined by simplicity and utilitarian design, improve student focus and eliminate distractions. Teachers noted that having a well-organized, clutter-free workplace improves learning outcomes by creating a more conducive environment for student involvement.\r\nThe study suggests the benefits of using minimalist principles in classroom design and makes recommendations to educational officials and practitioners. The report proposes an action plan that includes seminars and workshops to help teachers effectively implement and sustain minimalist classroom practices. The findings of this study contribute to the current discussion about optimizing classroom surroundings to improve educational experiences for primary school students. Keywords: Implementation, Guidelines, Minimalist Classroom, DepEd Order\r\n', 2024, 'Calion, Juvelle R. | Dela Cruz, Jewel Mae Y. | Delos Angeles, Jennifer DR. | Francisco, Ira Trisha I. | Gaspar, Maica M '),
(68, 0, '0', 'EFFECTS OF THE COVID-19 PANDEMIC ON GRADES STUDENTS\' READINGPROFICIENCY AT SAN MARCOS ELEMENTARY SCHOOL', 'The COVID-19 pandemic has caused an uncommon disturbance in students\' educational achievement. The Covid-19 pandemic\'s effect on the reading proficiency levels of San Marcos Elementary School specifically in Grade 5 were the main subject of this investigation. This study aims to identify the reading proficiency level of Grade 5 students during post-pandemic and how it differs on the proficiency level during pre- VBGPandemic. To pursue the objective of this research, the researchers utilized the experimental research design and applied the quantitative approach. Pre- and post-pandemic respondents\' reading proficiency levels were distinguished using percentages, frequencies, weighted means, pre-test, and post-test data. Using random sampling, a total of 20 pre-pandemic and 20 post-pandemic respondents were selected. According to the study, Covid-19 circumstances had a significant effect on Grade 5 children\' reading proficiency.\r\nInternal and External factors also impact the reading performance of the students.\r\nIt demonstrates that pre-pandemic respondents had an increased level of reading proficiency than post-pandemic respondents.\r\nThe results suggest that Grade 5 students in particular are vulnerable to reading\r\nchallenges and will need specialist attention. To increase students\' reading proficiency\r\nover time and reduce the reading gap caused by the epidemic, educators must enhance the reading programs that they provide for students who struggle with reading.\r\nKeywords: Covid-19 Pandemic, Pre-pandemic, Post-pandemic, Reading Proficiency.\r\n', 2023, ' Gordo, Marian S. | Jumaquio, Christine Joy J. | Tambiga, Carmela M.| Velasco, Kristen Joy C '),
(69, 0, '0', 'EXPLORING THE UNIQUE LINGUISTIC FEATURES OF TAGALOG BULACAN', 'This study is conducted to explore and determine the unique linguistic features of Tagalog Bulacan, specifically in phonology and semantics. A wordlist with the phonological and semantic characteristics of terminologies from Tagalog Bulacan has been created, with different domains, namely kinship terms, objects and their attributes, human characteristics, actions, and foods. In addition, this study used a Likert scale to determine the mutual intelligibility of Tagalog Manila and Tagalog Bulacan. Additionally, it is important to understand the unique linguistic characteristics of the terminologies used by\r\nnative Tagalog Bulacan speakers in terms of phonology (pronunciation and syllabication) and semantics (equivalent meaning), as well as the mutual intelligibility of Tagalog Manila with native Tagalog Bulacan. This research used a mixed-methods research design\r\nconsisting of an interview and a survey questionnaire. The qualitative method is used in the interview with the Tagalog Bulacan speakers and in analyzing the terminologies\r\nincluded in the wordlist. The quantitative method was used in analyzing the data from the survey and to identify the mutual intelligibility of native Tagalog Manila speakers with the list of terminologies elicited in Bulacan. In conclusion, Tagalog Bulacan has a unique linguistic feature. In phonological aspects, Tagalog Bulacan terminologies stress the last syllable and use the tuldik (accent mark) pahilis to determine its pronunciation. In the semantics aspect, there are peculiar terms that Tagalog Bulacan speakers use to describe or call someone or something. Lastly, Tagalog Bulacan and Tagalog Manila are mutually intelligible.\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'De Guzman, Richell S. | Fajardo, Nicole Anne L. | Gonzalo, Alicia | Matic, Leslie Ann B. | Pulido, Edison M.'),
(70, 16, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'PSYCHOLOGICAL WELL-BEING FACTORS INFLUENCINGCOMMUNICATIVE COMPETENCE AMONG UNDERGRADUATE STUDENTS OF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'This research paper was a Quantitative Research Design that aimed to investigate the psychological well-being of students, which had become a crucial issue in society due\r\nto the various challenges they faced, such as academic pressure, social dynamics, and stressors of contemporary life. To combat this increasing concern, state universities and colleges have become more committed to promoting the mental health of their students.\r\nAcross the nation, state universities and colleges had acknowledged the significance of\r\nmental health and had implemented measures to prioritize the well-being of the students.\r\nThrough the use of a Quantitative study, the researchers investigated the influence between the psychological well-being factors of Ryff and Keyes and communicative competence among undergraduate students at a University in Bulacan. The study explored whether factors of Ryff and Keyes, Psychological well-being in communicative competence was influenced by various factors, including autonomy, mastery of the environment, personal growth, positive interpersonal relationships, a sense of purpose in life, and self-acceptance.\r\nThese elements acted as mediators in the relationship. The primary objective of this study\r\nwas to examine how communicative competence and psychological well-being are interconnected, with the aim of enhancing communicative competence among university students. The data collection focused on a specific group of 230 undergraduate students from a university in Bulacan, chosen as a representative sample of the larger population.\r\nKeywords: Autonomy, Quantitative, Self-Acceptance, Communicative Competence,\r\nPsychological\r\n', 2023, 'Corigal, Sophia G. | Dela Cruz, Angelu H. | Delos Santos, Patricia Paola T.| Delsol, Alyssa Neña O. | Dy Pangco, Mark Joseph C.'),
(71, 0, '0', 'LEVEL OF PERCEPTION OF PARENTS AND TEACHERS INLEARNERS READING COMPREHENSION AT HAGONOY WEST CENTRALSCHOOL', 'The current study of teachers and parents\' perceptions shows that reading habits, environment, and reading materials affect the comprehension of learners. Reading habit affects the reading comprehension in terms of teachers\' follow up questions and reading over the context stimulate learners\' reading comprehension, while writing difficult terms and looking up their meanings are not as effective. The results from the study show that cold and fresh home environments have a significant impact on learners\' comprehension.\r\nAdditionally, the availability of a place where the learner can read on their own can also affect their comprehension. Classroom environment also affect the reading comprehension of learners. In the result of the study, reading comprehension of the learners highly affected also when they use furniture and designated areas for reading in school, many learners are able to study better because of a well - organized classroom and many types of relevant, purposeful, resources and technology that will help him/her to study. The study also shows that reading materials affect the reading comprehension. Reading materials can help to increase reading comprehension by providing a variety of reading materials and tasks, allowing students to learn and comprehend better.\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Bartolome, April C. | Capili, Michelle A. | Cruz, Dyan J. | De Guzman, Jennifer R. | Evangelista, Jobelle DG.'),
(72, 14, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'TONAL VARIATION ANALYSIS OF TAGALOG DIALECT IN HAGONOY AND MALOLOS BULACAN', 'This study aimed to develop understanding and analyzed the tonal variation differences of\r\nTagalog dialect in Hagonoy and Malolos Bulacan. Snowball sampling was used which included (20) selected individuals residing in Hagonoy, Bulacan, and (20) selected individuals residing in Malolos, Bulacan. This study utilized a pure qualitative through interviews and the use of a validated interview questionnaire. To gather data, the researchers used semi-structured questionnaires which allowed respondents to express their views in their own words. This research aims to set out the methodological approach to discover the tonal variation of Tagalog dialect in Hagonoy and Malolos Bulacan. The\r\nstudy used a grounded theory approach where the data is systematically collected and analyzed. The researcher personally traveled to Malolos and Hagonoy, Bulacan, to\r\ninterview the respondents with Tagalog Bulacan dialect. The researcher will search for\r\nlocals who have lived there for at fifteen years and, if possible, have not settled elsewhere.\r\nThere is no tonal structure difference between the two dialects of Tagalog, according to the study\'s research of the tonal structure of Tagalog speakers from Tagalog Hagonoy, Bulacan, and Tagalog Malolos, Bulacan. Researchers discovered that speakers from both towns have a 2-1-2 tonal structure pattern. It\'s important to keep in mind that the study was only conducted at the local level while speaking of it. As a result, the data only provide a limited understanding of the linguistic diversity among Tagalog-speaking populations.\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Aquino, Jona P. | Calanoc, Ghwynette D.| Camero, Joana Iva A.| Del Rosario, Arlene C. | Enriquez, Erica E. | Roque, Jerwin T.'),
(73, 15, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'THE EFFECTS OF ENGLISH-ONLY POLICY TO GRADE-10 STUDENTS\' CLASS PARTICIPATION', 'ABSTRACT: This study determines the effects of the English-Only Policy on Grade 10\r\nstudents\' participation on their performance, confidence, and motivation for the academic year 2022- 2023. It is also intended to investigate how effective the English-only policy is when put into classroom practice. The study wanted to fill a gap on what the effects of the English only policy are on students who are currently enrolled in private schools. Validated A researcher-made questionnaire was disseminated to ninety-one respondents at the chosen school of the researcher, who has used the English-Only Policy for years. The study used a quantitative research design, and the sampling technique used was probability sampling\r\nwith stratified random sampling. The findings of this study show that the effects of the English-Only Policy on students\' performance inside the classroom are effective, with a\r\nweighted mean of 1.85, which is regarded as agreeable. The effects of the English-Only Policy on students when it comes to their self-confidence are the lowest among all domains, with a 2.30 weighted mean, which is also regarded as agreeable. The English-Only Policy is effective when it comes to students\' confidence. In the motivation of students to use the\r\nEnglish-Only Policy in the classroom, a 1.96 weighted mean was regarded as agreeing.\r\nLastly, how effective is the English-Only Policy for students when put into classroom practice? The 2.11 weighted mean agrees. The study shows that implementing the English-Only Policy for students currently enrolled in private schools is effective and has positive effects on their performance, confidence, and motivation. It is also effective to use as classroom practice.\r\n', 2023, 'AGUINALDO, Rocel G. | AMOR, Melissa L. | CRUZ, Joben Mc Lean L. | DORMIDO, Mary Joy P. | LIMPONG, Ma. Florelyn N. | RELLORES, Jerilyn C.'),
(74, 45, 'BSHM', 'VIEWPOINT OF THE RESIDENT OF HAGONOY, BULACAN TOWARDS THE USE OF ECO-BAGS AS A REPLACEMENT TO PLASTIC BAG', ' Plastic bags are one of the major contributors of plastic waste pollution. Despite the fact that the overwhelming use of plastic bags harms the environment, people are still using them. The study conducted in the Municipality of Hagonoy Bulacan, Philippines was focused on the Viewpoint of the residents of Hagonoy Bulacan towards the use of Eco-bags as a replacement for plastic bags. The researchers aim to know the participants perception and willingness to use eco-bags as a replacement for plastic bags, also it aims to determine if the use of eco-bags influences environmental sustainability. This quantitative research study used the descriptive and correlation design. The questions on the survey questionnaire were made by the researchers guided by the statement of the problem, The total of 100 residents were selected through convenience sampling. The study was essential especially to the LGUs and National Government. The deeper understanding of the perception of people regarding this matter will play a crucial role in planning, promoting and implementation of the use of eco-bags to replace plastic bags as one of the steps to suppress the plastic waste pollution. The majority of the participants believe that eco-bags are environment friendly and can be used to replace plastic bags, also most of the participants strongly agreed that eco-bags have a big impact on environmental sustainability. As a conclusion, the use of eco-bags influences environmental sustainability. According to Pearsons r data analysis, there is a strong positive correlation between the use of eco-bags and environmental sustainability.\r\nKeywords: Plastic waste pollution, Viewpoint, eco-bags, convenient sampling, replacement, LGUs, Environmental Sustainability.\r\n', 2024, ' Buenaventura, Roann M. | Carating, Sophia Nicole C. | Cruz, Jhuliane Arvie DC. | Felipe, Francheska Elaine R.'),
(75, 44, 'BSHM', 'ASSESSMENT ON THE IMPLEMENTATION OF GREEN PRACTICEIN SELECTED COFFEE SHOPS IN THE CITY OF MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'Environment conservation is becoming increasingly prevalent, and environmental issues are continuously being widely recognized. Challenges arise with the connection to\r\nsustainability that affects the lives of people globally. The purpose of the study is to assess the various implementations of green practices in selected coffee shops in Malolos, Bulacan, in accordance with the growing awareness of the global environment. A descriptive study was conducted to examine the current practices that focus on waste\r\nmanagement and eco-friendly packaging in select coffee shops. Utilizing a survey questionnaire, a purposive sampling technique was employed for the selected 100 participants, who are customers and managers or staff. The questionnaire was divided into\r\nthree sections: business profile, implementation of green practices, and level of quality in\r\nthe implementation of sustainable green practices. The research revealed that the majority of coffee shops have implemented encouraging trends toward environmentally friendly and sustainable development, mainly when it comes to packaging and waste management.\r\nMost of the coffee shops primarily serve Generation Z, which serves as the main target customer, and have been in operation for two to five years. The research also showed that coffee shops commonly integrate waste reduction techniques and eco-friendly packaging made with biodegradable materials. In addition, the use of local and organic produce was widely agreed upon by managers, staff, and customers. The study also shows that the adoption of green practices and the quality of sustainability measures did not significantly correlate. The results suggest that in order to protect the environment, future research should concentrate on promoting fair-trade practices, recycling packaging, and putting in\r\nplace efficient waste management systems in coffee shops.\r\n', 2024, 'Pagdanganan, Catherine D. | Reyes, Melanie A. | Pajarillaga, Patricia B. |  Caligan, Mariz Joy DG.'),
(76, 0, '0', 'WORKPLACE ENVIRONMENT AND JOB PERFORMANCE OF EMPLOYEES IN SELECTED FAST FOOD IN MALOLOS, BULACAN', 'Workplace Environment and Job Performance of Employees in Selected fast food in Malolos, Bulacan was conducted to know the factor of job performance of the employees based on their workplace environment. In these studies, it discussed three parts of condition in workplace environment namely: mental condition, ergonomic condition and indoor condition. many things can discover to the employees who was working in the fast food.\r\nAnd all the problem that we had given to the worker was answering in the good way and honestly. And the result of this study will help to other researcher, and they will help too in the employees who was working in the fast food and how workplace environment can simply affect their job performance. Even our theory they help in our research, because they determine all the data or gathering a information. According to O\'Neill & Davis, 2011, This high turnover is attributed to a lack of job satisfaction, and it is thought that the hospitality industry\'s explosive growth has resulted in stress and work overload\r\nKeywords: Workplace, Job Performance, Fast food\r\n', 2022, 'Crisostomo, Ceazar lan O. | Deimos, Mariel | Perez, Jerico | Perez, Joyce| Pineda, Renz | Santos, Dana Clarisse'),
(77, 10, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'STRUGGLES AND ASPIRATIONS OF 4TH YEAR EDUCATION STUDENTSWHO WORK FULL-TIME WHILE STUDYING', 'This research sought to discover the struggles and aspirations of 4th year educationstudents who work full-time while studying. The respondents consisted of twenty-two (22) 4th year full-time workers from Education Program of Bulacan State university - Hagonoy Campus. The researchers used a virtual interview to gather the qualitative data and an online form utilizing a likert scale method for the quantitative data. Both methods were through Microsoft Teams. The gathered qualitative data were analyzed using thematic analysis by inductive approach. On the other hand, the quantitative data were computed using the Mean formula, and after coming up with the mean, the interval were interpreted. According to the results, students who work full-time while studying ranges from twenty-one (21) years old to forty-three (43) years old who has dissimilar work profile form one another. In addition, the students stated that their reasons of working while studying are due to their financial status and gain experiences. Furthermore, the results showed that students were struggling financially, managing their time, social life, extra-curricular activities, deadlines, health, safety, and motivations. Lastly, the respondents aspire to develop themselves personally and professionally.\r\n', 2022, ' Cruz, Lara Joyce S. | Dela Cruz, Micaella T. | Lalata, Angelika R. | Manahan, Marinel C. | Tubig, Esperanza DR.'),
(78, 13, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'INTRALINGUAL ERRORS IN COLLEGE ESSAYS: BASIS FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL ENGLISH CURRICULUM', 'The study investigated the Intralingual Errors that were committed by first-year\r\nstudents in their essays. The sources of data were 64 freshmen students who were pursuing the Bachelor of Secondary Education Major in English, Bachelor of Secondary Education Major in Mathematics, and Bachelor of Elementary Education at Bulacan State University\r\n- Hagonoy Campus. The data were collected from original essays and analyzed using Error Analysis. Students then reviewed their essays, identified errors, and made revisions. The\r\nresearchers collected both the original and revised essays for validation of errors.\r\nIntralingual Errors were classified into four categories which are Overgeneralization,\r\nIgnorance of Rule Restrictions, Incomplete Application of Rules, and False Concept Hypothesized. As indicated in the data, it was revealed that students were most prone to errors due to Ignorance of Rule Restrictions, accounting for 58.14% of all errors, followed by Incomplete Rule Application (19.84%), Overgeneralization (12.24%), and False Concept Hypothesized (9.78%). As shown in the research findings, the students\' poor grasp of grammar and syntax, as well as a lack of vocabulary, had impacted their writing ability, making it challenging for them to write and structure their ideas. Consequently, the researchers recommended that the Senior High School curriculum give priority to\r\nstrengthening students\' writing skills, including grammatical, semantics, syntax, lexical, and mechanics exposing them to different writing styles to prepare them for the diverse writing demands in college.\r\n', 2023, 'Azotes, Alaysa Marie A. | Cruz, Nazarene D. | Dizon, Rhona L. | Santos, Keiziah Arielle P.'),
(79, 0, '0', 'EVALUATION OF LANGUAGE GENDER-SENSITIVE USE IN ENGLISHLEARNING MODULES', 'This study is to evaluate the frequency of gender stereotypes in learning modules\r\nused by grade 7 in Iba national High School. Language gender stereotyping has become a controversial topic of research in different fields such as: sociology, psychology, ang\r\nlinguistics. Gender discrimination in language specifically gender stereotyping is said to be ubiquitous.\r\nThis research uses a tool kit for gender-sensitive communication to determine the\r\noccurrence of gender stereotypes: common gender noun, personal gender pronoun,\r\ndiscriminatory and gender neutral in the module. Researchers used a quantitative and qualitative mix method in which they evaluate the frequencies of gender stereotype words\r\nin learning modules\r\nAfter evaluating grade 7 modules the occurrence of gender stereotyping in learning modules words are found. With these result the study concludes that gender stereotyping\r\nis ineludible.\r\nKeywords: Gender, Gender stereotype, ubiquitous, gender discrimination, gender common noun, gender personal pronoun, gender discriminatory, gender neutral\r\n', 2023, 'Buenavista, Rein Errica P. | Del Rosario, Lara Jane E. | Dela Cruz, Maecel T. | Matawaran, Jenny Mae C. | Santiago, Alriane Gabrille S.'),
(80, 17, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'READING HABITS OF GRADE 7 STUDENTS: BASIS FOR REMEDIAL PROGRAM', 'This study aims to discover the reading habits of the students. Having the ability to comprehend written texts is an essential skill that is critical to success in various aspects of life. Therefore, this investigation is focused on studying the reading habits of 7th-grade students who have difficulties comprehending written materials. The study will explore several factors that could impact reading habits, including the availability of reading materials, personal preferences, the school environment, and technology usage. Data collection will involve survey questionnaires, and the researchers will use descriptive methods to analyze the collected information. The study aims to identify potential strategies that can improve their reading skills. The primary goal of this study is to understand the causes of frustration in the reading habits of 7th graders. The research team will examine how the accessibility of reading materials,\r\nboth at school and at home, can\r\naffect students\' reading habits. They will also explore how personal interests and the school environment can influence reading habits. For instance, students who have access to diverse reading materials and study in an environment that fosters reading are more likely to develop good reading habits than those who lack such resources. Another significant aspect that the study will investigate is technology use. With the increasing popularity of digital media, students are spending more time online and less time reading physical books. Therefore, the research will examine whether technology usage affects students\' reading habits and whether digital resources can be used to improve reading skills.\r\nAdditionally, the research will examine the relationship between reading comprehension and students\' interest in learning English. By understanding what motivates students to participate in English classes, the researchers can identify ways to enhance participation and learning outcomes. In summary, this research aims to provide a comprehensive understanding of the reading habits of 7th graders and the factors that impact their reading comprehension. By identifying the causes of frustration in reading habits and exploring potential remedies, the study can contribute to the development of effective interventions that can improve students\' reading skills.\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Francisco, Angeline H. | Gabriel, Kristine Mhae D.C Perez, Dhaptine Marie E.| Santos, Ma. Luisa R.'),
(81, 22, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'EXAMINING READING STRATEGY UTILIZATION ACROSS GENDERS AMONG COLLEGE STUDENTS AT BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY -HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'This research explores reading strategy utilization across genders among college students at Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus. The study investigates demographic profiles, reading strategies, comprehension scores, and relationships between strategies and scores.\r\nFindings indicate diverse strategy usage across genders. Male, female, and LGBTQ+ students of Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus usually utilized cognitive strategies such as comprehending, memory and retrieval strategies, and metacognitive strategies such as planning, monitoring, and evaluating strategies as their reading strategies. While male students displayed unsatisfactory comprehension, females demonstrated satisfactory levels, and LGBTQ+ students showed a need for improvement.\r\nSignificant differences in comprehension scores by gender were found. Relationships between strategies and scores varied: while males showed no significant correlation,\r\nfemales exhibited relationships with comprehending and memory strategies, and LGBTQ+ students with memory and planning strategies. Recommendations include tailored instructional strategies, curriculum integration of reading tactics, student self-assessment, and further research into contributing factors to comprehension differences.\r\n', 2024, 'Castro, Carla Mariz G. | Diama, Mark Anthony C. | Lazaro, Bianca Joy C. | Santos, Aerol Daniel L. | Tolentino, Michelle D.'),
(82, 0, '0', 'CORRELATIONAL ANALYSIS BETWEEN THE ATTENTION SPAN AND ONLINE GAMING BEHAVIOR AMONG THE INFORMATION AND TECHNOLOGY STUDENTS', 'Investigating the connection between online gaming and cognitive attention is the goal of this study. The Attention Network Test (ANT) and a self-report questionnaire on their online gaming behaviors were given to 50 randomly chosen individuals. The results of the study show a favorable correlation between attentional ability as measured by the Attentional Network Test (ANT) and both high and low online gaming behaviors. These results emphasize the potential advantages of online gaming for enhancing attention span. The Attention Network Test (ANT) scores used in the study to gauge levels of attention revealed a statistically significant positive link between high behavioral gaming scores and high levels of attention. The Pearson correlation coefficient was used in the correlation analysis, which showed a high positive link between behavioral gaming scores and attention levels of 0.69. Based on their behavioral gaming scores, the respondents were split into two groups: those with high behavioral gaming scores and those with low behavioral gaming scores. According to the analysis, the group with the high behavioral gaming score paid more attention than the group with the low behavioral gaming score. In contrast to the low behavioral gaming score group, which had a mean ANT score of 56.27, the high behavioral\r\ngaming score group had a mean ANT score of 77.44.\r\n', 2023, 'ABAGA, Melrose L. | CRISOSTOMO, Glian * | FELICIANO, Arabella Q. | JULIANO, Eddrian T. | LOPEZ, Humperdinck C. | PEREZ, Matthew R.'),
(83, 0, '0', 'THE LEVEL OF DIFFICULTIES IN FUNDAMENTAL OPERATIONSMATHEMATICAL AND BASIC INTERVENTION', 'This study aimed to investigate the difficulties in fundamental operation mathematical basic of intervention program. A survey was created containing basic questions about four fundamental operation and what basic intervention program. A total of 30 students from carillo elementary school were surveyed. It was determined that no\r\nsignificance was found between the participants who havedifficulties in fundamental operation and the participants who did not have difficulties in fundamental operation. The results suggest the need for further research to investigate other contributing level of difficulties in fundamental operation mathematical\r\n', 2023, 'Alba, Zaira Mae P. | Alejo, Lovely Michaella B. | Bacergo, Alexis Joyce L. | Balatbat, Ma Angelica Capulong, Rochelle R. | Gamotea, Lourdes C.| Magaling, Julie Ann M.');
INSERT INTO `thesisbooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(84, 7, 'BEED', 'BIG BOOK AS AN READING STRATEGY TO IMPROVE PHONEMIC AWARENESS OF GRADE 1 STUDENT AT EUGENIO G. SY-TAMCOELEMENTARY SCHOOL', 'This experimental study aims to determine the effectiveness of using Big Books as a reading strategy to improve the phonemic awareness skills of Grade 1 students at Eugenio\r\nG. Sy-Tamco Elementary School during the academic year of 2023-2024. This study main purpose is to improve the phonemic awareness of grade 1 student using big book as a reading strategy at Eugenio G. Sy-Tamco Elementary School. The research problem investigated in this study includes: how may the evaluation of the controlled and experimental group be described; is there a significant difference between the evaluation of the controlled and experimental group be described; how may the achievement test result of the controlled and experimental group be described; is there a significant difference between the achievement test results of the controlled and experimental group; is there a\r\nsignificant difference between the evaluation and achievement test result of the controlled group and is there a significant difference between the evaluation and achievement test result of the experimental group. The One-way Experimental Research Design is a wise decision when examining the effectiveness of using Big Books as a teaching approach to improve the phonemic awareness skills of Grade 1 pupils at Eugenio G. Sy-Tamco\r\nElementary School. This method makes it easier to carefully review real-time scenarios and provides a more detailed knowledge of the effects of different actions. The study found that big books, a reading strategy, significantly improved phonemic awareness skills in Grade 1 students. Both traditional methods and big books showed improvement, but the big book group consistently scored higher on final assessments. This suggests that big books may provide a richer learning environment, fostering phonemic awareness more effectively than traditional methods. The study suggests further research into the specific elements of big books and how educators can maximize their impact on phonemic awareness development in the classroom.\r\n', 2024, 'Dionisio, Dyannel B. | Garcia, Bernadette S. | Lopez, Marites T. | Martin, Shairmae E. | Raymundo, Ella Elaine DC. | Santos, Rogeline S.'),
(85, 9, 'BTLED HE', 'DEVELOPMENT OF BANANA BLOSSOM AND BANGUS MEAT INTO A ROLL', 'The study, titled \"DEVELOPMENT OF BANANA BLOSSOM AND BANGUS MEAT INTO A ROLL,\" the goal of this study is to develop a new recipe and offer banana blossom rolls as a healthier and less expensive dish. In place of the meat in rolls, the researchers would like to utilize banana blossoms, or as puso ng saging as they are more popularly known and milk fish or bangus.\r\nThis research study was done among 60 people of Bulacan State University and Barangay Abulalas Hagonoy, Bulacan who are student, entreprenuer and parents in order to serve as the foundation for banana blossom and bangus meat into a roll development\r\nrecommendations. The developmental research method was adopted. A questionnaire\r\nwas utilized to collect quantitative and qualitative data on sensory quality and other research parameters. Following a review of all of the data supplied in the research, the\r\nfollowing conclusions were reached, and the following suggestions were made;\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'Wallem Jude A. Bigornia | Maria Angelu F. De Leon | Lesslie Jane P. Galvez | Mark Joshua M. Santiago | Rhea Lyn C. Sta Cruz | Mayette Mondejar'),
(86, 12, 'BTLED HE', 'ENHANCING COOKIES BY ADDING MINT ESSENCE AS FLAVORING AGENT', 'This study, conducted at Bulacan State University Hagonoy - Campus, explores the incorporation of mint essence as a flavoring agent in cookies. It aims to assess its impact on sensory attributes and propose a marketing plan for promotion.\r\nUsing a quantitative approach, demographic profiles of respondents (students and parents) were analyzed alongside the steps in preparing mint-flavored cookies.\r\nSensory evaluations revealed that the cookies were generally accepted in terms of texture, appearance, aroma, taste, and aftertaste. A marketing plan was proposed involving social media, flyers, and food tasting events. Recommendations for future research include expanding demographic profiles, exploring alternative preparation methods, and experimenting with additional flavor enhancements. Overall, the study highlights the potential of mint essence in enhancing the sensory experience of cookies and offers insights for marketing strategies in promoting such products.\r\n', 2024, 'Danganan, Faith G. | Dayao, Clarisse Ann V. | Dela Cruz, Missy Anne A. | Haduca, Angel M. | Santos, Joseph Jucons C.'),
(87, 7, 'BTLED HE', 'COMMERCIALIZATION OF NIPA PALM ICE CREAM WITH CASHEW NUTS', 'The commercialization of nipa palm ice cream is illustrated in this paper. The study primarily focused on one of the third-class municipalities in Bulacan which is Paombong since it has a vast land of nipa palm or \"sukang sasa\" and most of its residents source of income comes from the nipa palm. The study uses a survey, a descriptive type of research design, with a sample of 50 individuals divided equally from both the Education Department of the Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus and vinegar sellers in selected barangays in Paombong. The survey employed a hedonic scale to assess the products acceptability in terms of the four descriptors — texture, appearance, taste, and sweetness. In addition, the rating system that solicits opinions on the flavor profile of the product was utilized. It is observed in this study that the overall weighted mean of both the influence of a product in terms of marketing and its launching is very acceptable for verbal interpretation. Also, it highlighted the feasibility of nipa palms first extraction in the unique flavor of ice cream and its capability to be commercialized. As a conclusion, nipa palm ice\r\ncream with cashew nuts will serve as a promising product that will enhance Paombongs\r\n', 2024, 'Amar, Sunny M. | Benitez, Ma. Maricris B. | Clemente, Raisa Joy S.'),
(88, 13, 'BTLED HE', 'UNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF MUNG BEAN INNOVATING PROTEIN PACKED COOKIES FOR SUSTAINABLE AND DELICIOUS SNACK', ' This study aims to explore the untapped potential of Mung Bean as a key ingredient in the creation of sustainable, protein-rich snacking. This research will investigate the formulation, sensory attributes, and market potential of these cookies, ultimately contributing to the diversification of plant-based protein sources in the snack industry. The study employed an\r\nExplanatory quantitative research method to systematically examine the comparison of a Mung bean Flour Cookies and an Ordinary Flour Cookie. Additionally, it will investigate various methods for processing Mung beans flour to enhance its sensory properties, making it an attractive ingredient for snack development. Furthermore, sustainability assessments will be conducted to\r\nevaluate the environmental impact of MUNG Bean-based snacks compared to conventional snack\r\nproducts. This study will assist in innovating a mung bean flour as an alternative or even a replacement ingredient in baking according to this research. It will also assist in developing a protein-packed cookie that is safe, all-natural, and will also provide consumers with a sense of comfort and relaxation without endangering their health.\r\n', 2024, ' Clarino, Raizen Emanúel DP. | Faustino, Thea Marie V.| Ignacio, Carmela | Paguio, Rhamboy B. | Pasco, Sofia Marie T.'),
(89, 3, 'BTLED HE', 'TRANSFORMING SABA BANANA INTO CRISPY DELIGHT: A STUDY IN THEPRODUCTION AND QUALITY OF THE SABA BANANA CHIPS', 'The study of the production of Saba banana delights is an exploration of the process involved in creating a delectable and popular snack made from raw Saba bananas. The study aims to investigate various aspects of Saba banana delight production, including enhancing production efficiency, ensuring product quality, and exploring potential variations in flavor. Additionally, the purpose of this study is to determine how citizens of Aurora Province can produce quality Saba Banana Chips in a traditional way to establish\r\na basic source of income.\r\nThis research is experimental since it provides and describes the production and\r\nquality of Saba banana chips. This research employs a Mixed Method Study approach, necessitating the formulation of questions for a survey questionnaire to gather data.\r\nResearchers will utilize a printed survey questionnaire containing predefined questions and\r\nrating scales as the primary instrument for data collection. Once the questionnaires are\r\ndistributed and completed by respondents, their answers will be evaluated. The researchers\r\nwill then categorize the responses provided by the participants for analysis and interpretation, using mean, median, and mode as statistical tools.\r\nThe sensory attributes of the Saba banana chips were evaluated, and four criteria determined the results of the evaluation. Saba Banana Chips are prepared by frying sliced Saba bananas and coating them with a mixture of glucose syrup, calamansi, sugar, salt, and water. Careful sanitation and handling of materials ensure quality. Sensory evaluation among 100 respondents showed high scores for taste (3.53), aroma (3.76), texture, and appearance (3.43), with an overall acceptability rating of 3.57, indicating widespread appreciation for the product across all sensory attributes.\r\n', 2023, ' Agulto, Jamaica S. | De Guzman, Anjela Kaye I. | Eugenio, Bernalyn C. | Robles, Robelyn V. | Solis, Michaela P.'),
(90, 8, 'BTLED HE', 'REDEFINING HEALTH SNACK: NUTRITIONAL ENHANCING STRATEGIES FOR CARROT BAR', 'The Philippines is well-known for its various culture and diverse culinary traditions - and\r\nlove for pastries is one of it. This trend underlines a challenging investigation why Filipinos are very attached to pastries. Furthermore, the country\'s distinct culture was able to establish bond between the people and the treat for pastries. Studying why Filipinos love to eat pastries is crucial in identifying its psychological, historical, and social factors that can impacted their culinary preferences. Finally, determining the underlying factor that formally accept the carrot bar is important. Using a mixed research design that included both qualitative and quantitative methodologies, this thesis aimed to provide a comprehensive understanding of the impact of carrot inclusion on brownie innovation. Lastly, the innovation of pastry using carrots presents a promising avenue for culinary exploration, blending tradition with creativity and catering to evolving consumer demands for flavor diversity and health-conscious options. This mixed research\r\ndesign has provided a well-rounded perspective, paving the way for further studies in innovative culinary creations. The study\'s findings are specific to Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus students and may not apply to other campuses or universities. The preferences and acceptability of carrot bars may differ among student populations. The study is limited to bread and carrots as the primary ingredients. While these are common pastry ingredients, including additional ingredients\r\nis beyond the scope of this study.\r\n', 2024, ' Angelia M. Baltazar | John Louie M. Reyes'),
(91, 9, 'BSED MATH', 'RELATIONSHIP OF COOPERATIVE LEARNING TECHNIQUES IN TEACHING AND LEARNING MATHEMATICS', 'The study aimed to investigate the cooperative learning techniques used in teaching and learning mathematics at Iba National High School. It is also intended to investigate the correlation between the teacher\'s cooperative teaching techniques and the students cooperative learning techniques, which are measured by the following indicators: (a) think-pair-share, (b) differentiated learning, (c) explicit learning. Two sets of survey questionnaires were disseminated to the respondents: first, to the grade 7 Tulip students of Iba National High School in the school year 2022-2023; and second, to two mathematics grade 7 teachers in the school year 2022-2023. The findings of this study show that the perception of Iba National High School students using cooperative learning techniques has a mean of 3.67 on the think-pair-share, 3.73 on the differentiated learning, and lastly, 3.74 on the explicit learning. For the teacher\'s cooperative teaching techniques, the mean is 4.7 on the think-pair-share, 4.6 on the differentiated learning, and 4.1 on the explicit learning.\r\nLastly, in correlating two variables using Pearson\'s r correlation coefficient, the result indicates that the cooperative learning techniques in teaching and learning mathematics have a perfectly positive correlation (r= 1.0), meaning the two variables move in the same direction. The obtained critical value of 2.015, which was found significant at 0.05 alpha, indicates that the cooperative learning techniques are effective in teaching and learning mathematics at Iba National High School. Hence, the researchers accepted the hypothesis. Therefore, Iba National High School students and teachers would have an initiative regarding the students who encounter cooperative teaching techniques that improve their learning in mathematics and the teachers who apply cooperative teaching techniques that enhance their performance.\r\n', 2023, 'Dela Rosa, Lyka Mae N. | Guanlao, Ann Rio D. | Pascual, Jocelyn R.| Serrano, Judy Ann S. | Velasco, Melissa G.'),
(92, 0, '0', 'ASSESSMENT OF THE ACCEPTABILITY OF PANDESAL DE GUYAPAN', 'The researcher will carry out this study to an ascertain the acceptability of Pandesal De Guyapan made with Guyabano and Pandan leaves since in contrast to other varieties of Pandesal, they have various benefits for individuals. The purpose of the research was to evaluate the acceptability of \"Pandesal De Guyapan\" which sparked the researcher\'s curiosity.\r\nThe researcher\'s aim to utilize guyabano and pandan leaves in the bread production. Pandesal De Guyapan provides different health benefits like lowering cholesterol, preventing urinary tract infections, improving sleep duration, boosting our immune system, and helping weight loss. It contains different kinds of vitamins minerals, and antioxidants known to support good health. It is also an important ingredient for eye benefit of pandan leaves. It is a natural technique to relieve dizziness and can help prevent stroke. Pandan leaves are an effective cure for pains and cramps, and can be used by making a liniment and massaging it into\r\nthe affected area. This is also beneficial in the treatment of arthritis pain.\r\nWhile, Guyabano is high in vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients.\r\nGuyabano includes vitamins A, C, E, K, Choline, Folate, Thiamin, Niacin, Pyridoxine, Pantothenic acid, and Riboflavin. Guyabano also contains Omega 3 fatty acids, Omega 6 fatty acids, dietary fiber, salt, and potassium, all of which have significant health benefits. \r\n\r\nThe ingredients used in making \"Pandesal De Guyapan\" were all-purpose\r\nflour, sugar, eggs, yeast, salt and guyabano and pandan extracts. By combining fresh guyabano and pandan leaves \"Pandesal De Guyapan\" produced a more delicious yet healthy flavored pandesal.', 2023, 'REGIO, Vernardita M. | BAUTISTA, John Sequiel C. | REYES, Lenewniel F. | FLORES, Rosemarie S. | DELA CRUZ, Jean S.'),
(93, 8, 'BSED MATH', 'PUBLIC SCHOOL MATHEMATICS TEACHER\'S TIME-USE ANALYSIS', 'This study was conducted to analyze the impact of Time-Use in the professional life of Mathematics Public School Teachers and to interpret the data for male and female teachers, on how they use their time in their routinary activities. In these connections, the study\'s sample was made up of 23 math teachers in public schools. In order to gather information regarding teachers\' time management, questionnaires that were developed by the instructors themselves were given to the mathematics teachers in public schools. Data from the sample were gathered using a quantitative research approach. In general, the time use of mathematics teachers has a positive impact on how they balance their time and use it to the extent of the work was found. The study also inferred that Male Mathematics Teachers does their work during workdays oftenly at Friday unlike in the Female Mathematics teacher who does their work during weekends specifically on Saturdays where they have the most of their time at home. It is recommended that time management skills be included in teaching training programs, in order to enhance the managerial and administrative activities of teachers. Keyword: Time-use; mathematics public school teachers; teachers\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Bautista, Ghericka A. | Bauto, Dezy Rei C | Delo Santos, Andronico| Fajardo, Christian Jerome B. | Ibañez, Lealyn M. | Singson, Jenmark G'),
(94, 0, '0', 'CODE-SWITCHING PRACTICES IN THE MATHEMATICS SUBJECT OF SELECTED SCHOOL IN BULACAN AND PAMPANGA', 'This study examined the code-switching practices of teachers and students in mathematics subject at two high schools in the Philippines - Iba National High School\r\n(INHS) and Sta. Ana National High School (SANHS). The researchers employed a mixed-methods approach, utilizing classroom observations and survey questionnaires to\r\ngather data on the types and factors influencing code-switching.\r\nThe findings revealed distinct patterns in the code-switching practices between the two schools. INHS teachers primarily used intra-sentential code-switching (53%), while SANHS teachers relied more on intra-sentential (59%) and inter-sentential (28%)\r\nswitching. Students in both schools exhibited lower rates of code-switching compared to their teachers. The survey data identified several key factors driving code-switching, including improving student comprehension, addressing language proficiency gaps, and negotiating social contexts. The study highlights the important role that code-switching can play in supporting mathematics learning, especially in multilingual classrooms. The results suggest that strategic use of code-switching, particularly intra-sentential switching, can enhance instructional effectiveness and student engagement. These insights can\r\ninform professional development and pedagogical approaches to leverage the benefits of code-switching in mathematics education.\r\n', 2024, 'Coronel, Anne Kristine S.|| Dayson, Manilyn M.| Galang, Jhannachiel G.| Mercado, Carmi Belen P.| Rivera, Mary Ann S.| Vasquez, Shane C.'),
(95, 0, '0', 'CORRELATION BETWEEN STUDENTS\' DEMOGRAPHIC PROFILE AND MATHEMATICAL ACHIEVEMENT', ' The study was designed to determine if the students\' demographic profile and mathematical achievement have a significant relationship. It sought to describe the personal profile of the participants in terms of age, sex, senior high school strand, household members, number of siblings in the family, and work description. And mathematical achievement is their grade in the general mathematics subject. This study also determines if there is a significant relationship between competencies and scores in the three topics under the said subject. In line with that, it also looked to see if there was a significant relationship between demographic profile, scores and mathematical achievement, as well as the suggested programs to enhance the students\' mathematical achievement.\r\nThe participants of the study are the 107 senior high school learners through purposive sampling from the 442 total population of learners from Ramona S. Trillana High School in the first semester of the academic school year 2023-2024. The study involved self-made survey questionnaires and diagnostic tests for the participants. The data gathered were tabulated using the descriptive method in problems one to three, Chi Square for number four, and multiple regression in number five.\r\nThe result shows that the working competencies has no significant relationship with their diagnostic score test under function and their graph, basic business math, or logic.\r\nFurthermore, among the demographic profiles, only sex has a significant relation to the mathematical achievement of the participants, and among the three topics in general mathematics, only the function and their graph have a significant relation to the mathematical achievement. Lastly, the following result suggests implementing future programs that enhance the students\' development, especially in mathematical achievement or academically despite of their demographic profile.\r\nKeywords: demographic profile, diagnostic scores, mathematical achievement, general mathematics subject\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'Acuña, Criselda Nicole J. | Atienza, Edna Lyn R. | Garcia, Jhulie Anne M.| Sunga, Paula Mae B.| Tolentino, Antonette T.'),
(96, 13, 'BSED MATH', 'MASTERING THE BASICS: A BLUE RED GREEN YELLOW (BRGY)APPROACH IN TEACHING ORDER OF OPERATION', ' Mathematics is a fundamental part of the curriculum, requiring students to master basic operations-addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division— and understand their interrelationships. A key component in this learning process is PEMDAS, which dictates the order of operations. A common error is that students often perform division before\r\nmultiplication when both operations appear together in an expression. Researchers have developed the BRGY approach to teach this order using colors: blue for parentheses, red for exponents, green for multiplication and division (left to right), and yellow for addition and subtraction (left to right).\r\nThis research study aims to investigate the effectiveness of the BRGY method on\r\nGrade 7 students in evaluating order of operation. An experimental study with 43 Grade 7 learners at Sta. Monica National High School tested this approach. Over three days, pre-and post-test scores showed significant improvement, indicating that color-coded system helped reduce misconceptions and clarified the sequence of steps. BRGY Approach can be an auxiliary to the traditional way of teaching order of operation, as it helps ultimately improving their mathematical skills.\r\nResearchers recommend the BRGY approach for primary and secondary teachers,\r\neducators, homeschooling parents, and tutors. This method can be an effective supplementary tool to the traditional approach. Future researchers might develop applications or games to automate color-coding equations, making it easier for teachers.\r\nAdditionally, future studies could expand to include more complex operations, such as roots, to further validate the BRGY method\'s efficacy.\r\nKeywords: order of operation, PEMDAS, BRGY, colors\r\n', 2024, ' Bartolome, Rommalie I. de Guzman, Rioline P. | Libiran, Clarissa P. | Salalac, Jenny Rose A. |Tamargo, Marjorie G.'),
(97, 11, 'BTLED HE', 'LEMGUNDI INFUSION: BLENDING LEMON ZEST AND LAGUNDILEAVES FOR FRAGRANT BREW ', ' Common respiratory disorders affect millions of people globally. Asthma is the\r\nmost common chronic respiratory disorder, even in adults, and most children suffer many respiratory infections during their childhood. This research study was done among 50 people of Iba o este, Calumpit, and Barangay Iba, Hagonoy Bulacan. The focus was on the health benefits for older individuals and the promotion of herbal tea among those aged 20 and above. The Study will have used a quantitative research design with survey-style data collection for the survey. The results are through the survey form of the respondents that\r\nthe researchers have chosen to use. They made questionnaires to analyze the satisfaction\r\nof the target respondents in making the best beneficial tea for health.\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'Austria, Roma C. | Faderugao, Chona A.| Gutierrez, Mickaella B.| Lizarondo, Kristel T. | Mariano, Mezra Mae F.'),
(98, 0, '0', 'GRADUATE TRACER SYSTEM WITH DIGITAL COMMUNICATION FORBULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY ALUMNI OFFICE', 'The purpose of the study is to develop a Graduate Tracer System with Digital Communication for Bulacan State University Alumni Office. It was developed and designed to provide a comprehensive software solution for the Alumni Relations Office not just to help to improve the processes and transactions of the Alumni Relations Office but also to provide the latest news or information about the Alumni Relations Office or The University.\r\nThe researchers will utilize Agile Methodology in developing the system which will provide user satisfaction by embracing the customer\'s concept in the system\'s implementation. It allows the developer to guarantee that the system is actually the user\'s demand by keeping the customer in the circle by making improvements based on their feedback.\r\nIn conducting User Acceptance Testing. The researcher used an online sample size calculator to determine the sample size we need in UAT and used a 10% of margin of error, 10% of Population Proportion, 95% of Confidence Level, and expected population size of more than 100,000 Graduates, A total of 35 Graduates participated and 1 Alumni Relations Officers for the test.\r\nBased on the findings of the User Acceptance Testing for Graduate Students\r\nand\r\nAlumni Office Admins, the Graduate Tracer System with Digital Communication for Bulacan State University Alumni Office gets a majority marked for \"Passed\" in terms of functionality, this means that the actual result matched the stated expected result. While other responses stated that there were issues encountered as they used the system.\r\nConsidering the findings of the study, the following recommendations are made. First is Upgrading the Live Chat Facility of the developed system to be a medium of communication between alumni to contact one another, may be especially useful for those old alumni who have forgotten their batchmates\' names.\r\nSecond is the future researcher may consider the restriction of Graduate Tracer Respondents and the last is recommended to add another feature that the alumni will have a community window wherein they can share ideas with one another.\r\n', 2022, 'Bolina, Alfredo Jr., B. | Jose, Lalorence, C.| Lopez, Ronan Angelo| Santos, Marc Nathaniel'),
(99, 0, '0', 'UTILIZATION OF CARROTS INTO COMMERCIALIZED PASTILLAS DECAROTA', 'The study entitled\" Utilization of Carrot into commercialized Pastillas de Carota\r\naims to determine the acceptability of Pastillas de Carota in the market \r\n\r\nThe researchers used an experimental method in conducting the study. The experimental method was used to determine the cause and effect of two given variables.\r\nThe research was conducted in San Miguel Hagonoy Bulacan. It has an overall total of 100 respondents who are divided into 2 main categories the Producers (20 Entrepreneurs,\r\n30 selected students in BulSU Hagonoy Bulacan) and Consumers (30 Parents and 20\r\nChildren). The data gathered in this study was through the Likert scale with 5 main criteria (Appearance, Aroma, Taste, Texture, and Sweetness) The researchers tally the\r\nresults of the survey to analyze and interpret the weighted mean of the study.\r\n\r\n1, Base on the level of acceptability on the sensory of Pastillas de Carota in Appearance was 4.64, in aroma 4.79, in taste 4.91 in texture 4.55 and in sweetness 4.75which means very acceptable in verbal interpretation. Therefore, the respondents accept the sensory evaluation of the product.\r\n\r\n2. Base on the significance difference on the respondents in the acceptability of\r\ncommercialized Pastillas de Carota; In appearance the T-Value was 1.5561, in aroma was 0.4479, in taste was 0.1536, in texture was 0.3378 and in sweetness was 0.7210.\r\nTherefore, the verbal interpretation was No significance, and the decision was accepted.\r\n\r\n3. Also based on the study the respondents like the taste of Carrot Pastillas that the researchers made. According to respondents the taste of Carrot Pastillas is just the same as traditional Pastillas but more nutritious because of the carrot. Another thing that makes the Researchers\' Carrot Pastillas stand out from the traditional ones is the portion\r\nnutrition value and can be eaten by children without noticing its containing vegetable per piece. The researchers use Carrot as the main ingredient to add flavor, balance the\r\nsweetness, and make the Pastillas have a portion of nutrients per piece than the traditional Pastillas.\r\n', 2022, 'Enerson D. Cabantog| Alfredo D. Lagan | Raniel A. Perona| Mark Edron E. Dela Cruz | Clarisse C. Sta Cruz | Desserie S. Estomaguio| Mara S. Cervantes'),
(100, 0, '0', 'EFFECTS OF MODULAR LEARNING TO THE STUDY HABITS OF ELEMENTARY PUPILS AT LONGOS ELEMENTARY SCHOOL', 'Modular learning is one of the COVID-19 pandemic brought extraordinary\r\nchallenges to the stakeholders, teachers, parents, and students. The printed modular distance learning modal is used to continuously to provide excellent and relevant education in the face of the epidemic. Modular learning is one of the so-called modes of learning along with synchronous and asynchronous learning.\r\nModular learning is one of the methods implemented by the department of\r\neducation to continue students\'\r\ngovernment\'s conceivable ways to keep students away\r\nfrom the pandemic we are experiencing. Modular learning consists of worksheets,\r\nworkbooks, and other supporting material the administration can provide. It is implemented for the welfare and safety of the students and the faculty. The researcher\r\nbelieved that there is an advantages and disadvantages effect of the teaching-learning\r\nprocess in new normal education on students\' performance, most significantly using a\r\nmodular type of learning in each subject.\r\nThe advantages that the pupils might encounter during modular learning: (I) the pupils learn to be more flexible in managing their modules amidst pandemic; (2) Parents tend to realize they have a role in their child\'s education; (3) this is the point at which parents understand that teaching is never easy. They tend to absorb the idea that they are the teachers now that the pandemic has spread. These are some advantages that the pupils may encounter. Contrary, among the advantages, there is a downfall such as the majority of pupils is not taking their modules seriously. There is no guarantee that the pupils are learning through printed modules because some students tend to copy the answer after reading the modules. The harsh reality may be disappointing, but it is also the truth. The current situation can be tricky in motivating the pupils to reach their goals.\r\n', 2022, 'Pintor, Christine Joy DR. | Faustino, Eulagine C. | Albino, Lorraine'),
(101, 9, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'INTERGENERATIONAL LANGUAGE TRANSMISSION: ANALYSIS OF LEXICAL BORROWINGS FROM TAGALOGLANGUAGE', 'This study is based on the Intergenerational Language Transmission: Analysis ofLexical Borrowings from Tagalog Language. The researchers want to know where is the gap in intergenerational language transmission in Nigui, Masantol Pampanga among the Kapampangan speakers. Therefore the present study aims to help the community in knowing the gaps among Kapampangan speakers\' lexical borrowings from Tagalog language.\r\nMixed method of research was used in this study. Thirty (30) respondents from the\r\ninitial population of the community of Nigui, Masantol Pampanga that is randomly selected were asked to answer the questionnaires and interview questions. On the other hand, the researchers also conducted interview to some educators and advocates of the Kapampangan\r\nlanguage. The questionnaire was used as primary guide in the realization of the intergenerational language transmission of the Kapampangan speaker\'s lexical borrowings from Tagalog words. The following steps were followed in analyzing the results: (1)\r\nObserving the respondents\' answers (2) Computing the results (3) Building some ideas that we\'ve got from the respondents (4) Describing the results (5) Evaluating the results.\r\nResults show that among the first generation, they are all speaking in\r\nKapampangan, they know most of the words in Kapampangan, and their preference of words are Kapampangan. On the other hand, second generation respondents selectively\r\nknow the Kapampangan words, they are speaking in Kapampangan in some people for example the elders, while they speak Tagalog when they are talking to their children or to the youth. Basically, for them this is the easiest way to communicate to the next generation.\r\nLastly, the third generation draw away the results although they are Kapampangan because they live in Pampanga. They are not familiar with some Kapampangan words. The basic words obviously they are familiar, however, they are not familiar with the native Kapampangan words. Third generation are much familiar with the Tagalog words. They prefer to use Tagalog in household, school, in peers, social media and television. The third generation, choose to speak in Tagalog despite of being Kapampangan.\r\nThe study submits the recommendation as follows: (1) The community might encourage their people to practice Kapampangan language as a means of communication inside their house. (2) The school supports more Kapampangan Language programs to\r\nenhance and develop the use of Kapampangan language in their community. (3) The teacher and parents must cooperate and help the school to practice and maximize the significance of the language in their community. (4) The government should encourage the parents to practice their children to use the Kapampangan language to maintain the existence of the Kapampangan language through generations. (5) That prospective\r\nresearchers should develop the study for it to become more reliable and to add more\r\nrecommendations that will really improve the intergenerational language transmission.\r\n', 2022, 'Dela Cruz, Alexa C. | Garcia, Beatriz Anne R. | Lacap, Roxette Ann | Reyes, Rusty Jordan L. | Villafuerte, Aaron Joseph C.'),
(102, 3, 'BSED MATH', 'CORRELATION OF TEACHER\'S INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATION TECHNOLOGY SKILL LEVEL AND STUDENT ACADEMIC ENGAGEMENTTOWARDS MATHEMATICS', 'The study aimed to investigate the levels (Basic ICT skills, Advanced ICT skills, Internet application for information access, and Internet application for communication purposes) of Mathematics instructors of Bulacan State University-Hagonoy campus\' ICT skills. It also intended to investigate the correlation between the teachers\' ICT skills and the students\' academic engagement which are measured by the indicators: (a) Class Participation, (b) Attendance/Promptness, (c) Examination, and (d) Submission of requirements. Two sets of questionnaires were disseminated to the respondents first, to all the Mathematics Instructors of Bulacan State University-Hagonoy campus in the second semester of A.Y 2021-2022 (Teacher A, Teacher B, and Teacher C), and second, to the sample population of students from the BSED Mathematics course with Mathematics subject/s in the second semester of A.Y 2021-2022 (BSED Math 1A, BSED Math 2A, and BSED Math 3A). The findings of this study show that the level of ICT skills of Mathematics instructors of Bulacan State University-Hagonoy campus vary with Teacher A being highly skilled with a total mean of 4.53, Teacher B having average ICT skills with a total mean of 2.9, and Teacher C having moderately high ICT skills with a total mean of 4.20. In addition, it was discovered that the area of ICT skill in which the teacher respondents have the lowest level is on Advanced ICT skills (Teacher A=4.17, Teacher B=2.5, Teacher C=3.5) For the academic engagement of students, Class A which evaluated their academic engagement with regards to Teacher A\'s ICT skill level, their total academic engagement mean is 4.393 which means they have moderately high academic engagement. Class B in relation to Teacher B\'s ICT skill level has a total academic engagement mean of 4.067 or moderately high academic engagement. Lastly, Class C\'s total academic engagement mean with regards to Teacher C\'s ICT skill level is 4.692 or high academic engagement. Lastly, in correlating the two variables, using the Pearson\'s r correlation coefficient, the result indicate that teacher\'s ICT skill level and the students\' academic engagement have a strong positive correlation (F= 0. meaning the two variables move in the same direction. The obtained critical value of .643 which was found significant at .05 alpha indicates that teachers\' ICT skill level form a significant effect on the students\' academic engagement at Bulacan State University-Hagonoy campus. Hence, the researchers accept the hypothesis. Therefore, Bulacan State University-Hagonoy campus and its Mathematics instructors should have an initiative regarding the acquisition and development of ICT skills which in return will impact their students\' academic engagement towards Mathematics, positively.\r\nKeywords: Teacher\'s ICT skill level, Academic engagement, Mathematics\r\n', 2022, 'ESTRELLA, John Dominique | GARCIA, Joanna Marie | PANGANIBAN, Ciara Joy | SAN DIEGO, Colleen Mae | SIMBULAN, Nyca'),
(103, 7, 'BSED MATH', 'EDUCATIONAL SUPPORT THROUGH DIGITAL MEDIA IN LEARNINGMATHEMATICS', 'Digital media has a wide variety of platforms and site that use as an educational tool. This study will evaluate the used of digital media in assisting student\'s learning in Mathematics.\r\nThe BSED Math student from first year to fourth year level of Bulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus are the respondent that take way in this study. The total population of 119 BSED Math student participate to evaluate the significance of using digital media in Mathematics. This quantitative research used a survey questionnaire that include the statements for the digital media and the skills develop by the students in learning Mathematics. The frequency, percentage, and weighted mean was the statistical treatment apply in the data gathered. The findings of the study shows that social media has the mean of 3.98, video tutorial has the mean of 4.15, mobile applications has the mean of 3.74, and website has the mean of 4.11 are the digital media serve as an educational tools, and it has the total weighted mean of 3.99 interpret as agree. On the other hand, the develop skills of the students in learning Mathematics are interpersonal skill with mean of 3.85, advance skills of using different apps has the mean of 3.86, Problem-solving skills has the mean of 3.74, active participation has the mean of 3.69, and the test taking skills has the mean of 3.93. The total weighted mean is 3.81 interpret as agree. This study concludes that the alternative hypothesis was accepted indicates the support of using digital media has a significant influence in assisting student\'s learning in Mathematics. Keywords: Digital Media, Assisting Student\'s Learning, Mathematics\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'De Guzman, Danica R. | Geronga, Jewell S. | Joson, Paula Angela M.| Magbitang, Bernadette M. | Tamargo, Marisol G'),
(104, 0, '0', 'PRODUCTION OF SMOKED FISH UTILIZING HERRINGS/SARDINELLAFIMBRIATA (SILINYASI)', 'Aquaculture is one of the biggest income generating business in Bulacan.\r\nAccording to the Fisheries Statistics of the Philippines from year 2013-2015, Bulacan was included in the top 10 provinces that produced brackish water sea foods. Hagonoy is one of the municipalities in Bulacan that has numerous amounts of brackish water fishpond\r\noperators and consignacions which is why it is called the \"Aquaculture Capital of Bulacan\". With the abundant water resources, majority of the population is dependent on fishing industry. Aside from fishing industry, Hagoeño also processed their sea foods as one of their major products.\r\nThe general problem of the study is: May the Sardinella Fimbriata be utilize into smoked fish? The study also seeks to answer sensory evaluation in terms of color, aroma,\r\nflavor, and texture. The researcher will cover only the community of Bulacan State\r\nUniversity- Hagonoy Campus with a total number of 100 to evaluate the project. The primary objective of the study is the production of smoked fish utilizing Sardinella Fimbriata, the researcher adopted the IPO model, which stands for input, process, and output. This model serves as a guide in developing, constructing and assessing the projects\'s acceptability.\r\nThis researcher\'s objective is conducting this study to determine how smoked fish works if it is made of sardinella fimbriata or what we called \"silinyasi\". The study used the descriptive type of research in which the researchers aimed to gain information through making smoked fish and through surveys. This is also a qualitative type because the researchers do not have a control on the participant of the study. The research is inferentially in approach because of the aim to gather information on the selected sample of the population.\r\nIn acquiring data, the researchers visited some market places near the area referred to thesis available to gain information. Online researches were also made to have insights\r\nabout the topic internationally.\r\nWith the result on the data analysis, the community of Bulacan State University\r\nstrongly agreed that Silinyasi fish does and can be utilize into smoked fish.\r\nSalting is the best way to remove or reduced the number of bacteria of the fish and prevents the multiplication. Salting also prolong the life span of the fish. That is why the salt is the main ingredients in smoked fish. Smoking drains the moist in the fish resulting,\r\nit preserves fish by drying, and when the fish are near the source of heat.\r\n', 2019, 'Dela Cruz, Nicole Elijah V.| Dela Peña, Trixia V.| Luna, Arvie C.| Ramos, Angelica E. | Santiago, Ronell C.| Sarmiento, Ron Paolo N.'),
(105, 0, '0', 'MUSIC AS AN INSTRUMENT TO ASSESS LISTENING COMPREHENSION', 'This study was conceptualized to explore the idea that music can be use as an instrument to asess the listening comprehension of the students. Specifically it sought answers to the following questions: (1) To what extent is the level of performance of the students with music? (2) To what extent is the level of performance of the students without music? And, (3) Is there a significant difference between the performance of students in listening comprehension with music and without music?\r\nThe study used the experimental method of research to measure the significant difference between students\' performance in listening comprehension of the control group and experimental group. The researchers discussed samples of Literature and distributed comprehension questions. These comprehension questions were used to measure each participant\'s listening comprehension skill.\r\nIn the light of the findings of the study, the level of performance of the students with music was good based on the overall mean of the first, second, and third trial which is 3.97 interpreted as good, the level of performance of the students without music is good based on the overall mean of the first, second, and third trial which is 3.58 interpreted as good, and there is a significant difference between teaching literature with background music and teaching literature without background music when it comes to students\' listening comprehension. Therefore, teachers can use this technique to further improve students listening comprehension. Further studies can be conducted to\r\ninvestigate the listening comprehension of the students in an enclosed room where in the students could focus their attention in the discussion with the help of music.\r\n\r\n', 2018, 'Danica G. Bordamonte | Ranellee R. Coronado | Janella Anne M. Diamante| Nerissa U. Nicolas | Mariel O. Ruaya | Mary Kryss DG. Sangle'),
(106, 1, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'EFFICACY IN TEACHING ENGLISH AS A SECOND LANGUAGE (ESL) INTERVENTION: A CASE OF HARVESTERS\' MISSIONS INTERNATIONAL SCHOOL', 'The study focuses on the \" Efficacy in Teaching English as Second Language ( ESL)\r\nIntervention A Case of : Harvesters Missions International School. \" The followings are the\r\ngeneral problem of the study: (1) what is the demographic profile of the respondents in terms of:\r\nName, Age, Gender, Educational Attainment and Years in Service. (2) What are the level of self-efficacy in terms of : English Language Confidence, Teaching Confidence, Motivating Students, and Classroom Management. (3) What is the level of teacher\'s efficacy according to Elite Korean Students in terms of: English Language Confidence, Teaching Confidence, Motivating\r\nStudents, and Classroom Management.\r\nThe researcher used descriptive research method because it gives the respondents the opportunity to answer the questions subjectively. According to Garcia (2005) it gives a better and deeper understanding of phenomena through the use of an in-depth study which provides basis\r\ndecision making. The researcher conducted a survey questionnaire for 8 teachers and 21 Elite\r\nKorean students from Harvesters\' Missions International School. The purpose of the study is to\r\nevaluate the teacher\'s efficacy in teaching English as Second Language (ESL) Intervention to the elite Korean students. After gathering and interpreting the data, the researcher found out that the ESL teachers are confidentwith their English Language skills but their confidence weren\'t really so high, and also teachers know that they are confident in teaching the language but they believe that they still need something to improve. Moreover, researchers found out that ESL Teacher is truly exerting their effort to motivate their students in their class but they are not strict when it comes to the classroom rules and regulation. However, Elite Korean Students believe that their ESL teachers are confident enough and knowledgeable in teaching English Language.\r\n', 2017, 'Abegail V. Calonzo | Ma. Corazon C. Caralde | Mira May R. Sabino'),
(107, 0, '0', 'EPEKTO NG KAGAMITAN SA PAGTUTURO NG KWENTONG BAYAN SA HAGONOY, BULACAN', ' Ang pag-aaral na ito ay buong sikap na sinuri ang mga epekto ng kagamitang panturo sa layuning ituro ang kuwentong bayan na nagmula sa Hagonoy, Bulacan sa mga mag-aaral na nasa elementarya.\r\nAng mga guro na naninirahan at nagtuturo sa mga paaralang elementarya ng\r\nHagonoy, Bulacan at maging mga mag-aaral na nasa baitang anim na mula rin dito ay mga respondante sa pananaliksik na ito. Ang pag-aaral na ito ay gumamit ng \'interview method\' para sa mga guro sa mga mababang paralan at gumamit din ng deskriptibong sarbey na pamamaraan para sa mga estudyante sa elementarya. Ang talatanungan sa interbyu para sa mga guro na isinagawa ay naglalaman ng open-ended questions; ang mga nakalap na datos mula rito ay sinuri nang mabuti at ginamitan ng thematicalcode analysis upang maisaayos ang mga nakuhang datos sa layong matukoy ang mga magkakaparehong sagot ng mga respondante hinggil sa kuwentong bayan, at mairanggo ito pagkatapos. Ang mga talatanungan naman sa pagsasagawa ng sarbey ay five-point Likert scale kung saan sa pamamagitan ito ay inalam ang mga epekto ng ginawa at ginamit na kagamitan ng mananaliksik para sa pagtuturo ng naturang paksa. Sa pananaliksik na ito natuklasan ang pinakaepektibong gamiting kagamitan ayon sa mga respondente para sa pagtuturo ng kwentong bayan na nagsilbi ring gabay sa pagbuo nito. Ang lumabas sa resulta ay ang kagamitan sa pagtuturo na \"story book\". Mula sa tatlumpu\'t lima (35) na mga respondante na mga guro, dalawampu\'t anim (26) o 74% sa kanila ang nagsabi nito. Ayon sa nakalap na datos, natuklasan din naang kuwentong bayan ang pinakamainam na ituro upang subukin ang epekto ng nasabing kagamitan para dito. Ang kuwentong bayan na ito ay ang tungkol sa \"sirena\", lumabas sa resulta na labing-isa (11) mula sa tatlumpu\'t lima (35) na respondente o 31% ang nagsabing ito ang pinakamainam na ituro. Ang pinakamalaking epekto na nakita sa paggamit ng binuong kagamitan sa pagtuturo ng kuwentong bayan sa mga respondente na mag-aaral sa elementarya ay nagkaroon ng kalidad at kaangkupan nagamitin ito sa pagtuturo ng isang aralin lalo nat higit kung patungkol sa literatura. Sa ibang salita, naiugnay ito nang wasto sa isang aralin para sa mabisang pagkatuto ng mga bata at maiwasan ang kalituhan sa nilalayong matutunan. Ang ikalawa sa nakitang epekto ay naging daan ito upang ang mga mag-aaral ay magokus, manabik at magkaroon ng kamalayan sa paksang aralin pati na rin sa mga binigay na halimbawa hanggang sa huling bahagi ng talakayan patungo sa mahusay nilang pagkatuto. Ang ikatlo sa naging epekto ay naging mabisa itong paraan upang magkaroon ng kaalaman ang iba sa mga mag-aaral at ang iba ay dagdag kaalaman tungkol sa mga kuwentong bayan na sumasalamin sa kultura at paniniwala ng kanilang bayan na kinabibilangan. Namalas na ang mga kuwentong bayan sa Hagonoy katulad ng kwento sa \"Sirenasa Bahay Kastila\" ay hindi naging dominante ang takot sa mga mag-aaral batay sa mga reaksyon nila habang nakikinig o pagkatapos nila itong mapakinggan kundi ang mas nangingibabaw ang saya na dulot nito at nagbigay rin ng aral at inspirasyon sa kanila. Samakatuwid, ang kagamitang panturo ay may malaking epekto sa pagkatuto ng mga mag-aaral tungkol sa mga kuwentong bayan. Ang story booknaman na isa sa kagamitang panturo ay masasabing epektibong gamitin lalo na pagdating sa pagtuturo ng mga kuwentong bayan sa mga mag-aaral.\r\n', 2022, 'Abila, Rhonarhisa Marie L. | Capili, Mary Joy D. | Marigsa, Esnie Ana Jane P. | Royo, John Rhey T');
INSERT INTO `thesisbooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(108, 3, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'LEVEL OF EFFECTUALITY OF WATCHING ENGLISH CAPTIONED MOVIES TO THE VOCABULARY ENHANCEMENT OF THE STUDENTS', 'This study was conducted to identify the effect of captioned movies to the vocabulary enhancement of the students. This study sought to answer the following questions: (a) How may a movie affect the vocabulary level of the participants in terms of pre-test scores and post-test scores? (b) Is there any significant difference between the pre- test and post-test to enhance the vocabulary of the students? (c) What intervention program may be crafted after conducting the study? The participants were thirty (30) first year English major students who were enrolled at Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus in the academic year 2018-2019; six (6) male and twenty-four (24) female. The instruments used in order to gather data needed for the research were pre-test and post-test and the results were described using a rating scale.\r\nThe results showed that there is a significant difference between pre-test and post-test. Table 2 shows that the mean of pre-test is 10.09 with the rating of satisfactory while table 4 shows that the mean of post-test is 8.88 with the rating of good. Based on the findings, on the first and second trial of conducting the process of watching movies and administering the exams, the pre-test scores were higher compared to the post- tests Scores. Therefore, it can be concluded that there is no enhancement of vocabulary through watching movies. It can be assumed that there are possibilities that this happened because the participants focused on the sequence of events of the story rather than the unfamiliar words that were flashed on the screen.\r\n', 2022, 'Rhea R. Capulong | Joshua V. De Lumen | Daniel DC. Jumaquio| Merejean C. Laceda | Margine M. Santos | Ria A. Santiago | Mary Joy S. Sunga| Jobelle C. Tolentino'),
(109, 0, '0', 'HANDLING OF PPE\'S: THE CASE OF HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'The focus of this descriptive quantitative study was to examine the effects of personal protective equipment (PPE) waste disposal on the ecosystem of Hagonoy, Bulacan. In particular, it focused on the handling of PPE in terms of disposing and recycling. According to a recent study of Svennevig (2021), individuals use PPE and dispose of an estimated 129 billion per month, the most of which are disposables made of microfiber plastic, which is regarded as a major danger to our environment.\r\n\r\nHagonoy, Bulacan is bordered by several bodies of water; high tides and floods are typical in the community, and results revealed that there was no particular procedure communicated to locals regarding the proper PPE disposal. The locals disposed of the PPE by throwing it in just about anywhere, where it is carried by the tides and swept into lakes and rivers. It also adds to sewage stagnation, resulting in severe floods. Thus, the researchers believed that it is detrimental to bodies of water and the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nIn terms of recycling, the majority of respondents do not recycle because they lack sufficient information on how to securely recycle used PPE. The results suggest that there is a lack of information dissemination on how to properly dispose and recycle PPE. It is urged that the local government, private institutions, foundations, or advocates of environmental protection organize seminars, training, or programs to inform, educate, and guide residents on how to properly dispose and recycle PPE.\r\n', 2022, 'Alberto, Ericka Rose | Delos Santos, Hannah| Laderas, Candido| Lopez, Sheryl | Santos, Josielyn | Sebastian, Ronnel | Villarías, Renz'),
(110, 12, 'BSED ENGLISH', ' PICTURE-WORD AS PHRASEOLOGY TEACHING-LEARNING APPROACH IN VOCABULARY', 'Vocabulary is the foundation for comprehension. Children with poor knowledge in vocabulary are at risk of reading comprehension and writing difficulties, which will impact their educational performances and achievements. This quasi-experimental study aimed to determine the effectiveness of using pictures as a vocabulary-learning approach in an intervention.\r\n\r\nThere was a total of 70 Grade 7 students who took the pretest and posttest examination: 35 students received treatment of strategic vocabulary intervention (experimental group) while the other 35 students were remained conventional teaching method (controlled group). The results from the pretest showed that there was a 0.66 mean score difference; the controlled group\'s scores (14.29) are slightly higher than the experimental group (13.3) in which indicates that pretest scores had no significant difference. Results also revealed that the posttest mean score of the experimental group (17.03) is significantly higher than the controlled group\'s (14.09). Comparing the pretest and posttest scores of the controlled group; it had no significant difference due to its retained average. While the comparison of both tests\' scores in experimental group indicated that the experimental group performed better after 5 days of intervention. Therefore, the picture-word as a vocabulary learning approach is effective- evidently implying its significant improvement in student\'s performance throughout the experiment.\r\n\r\nKeywords: vocabulary building, picture-word, teaching strategy, learning approach\r\n', 2023, 'CALONZO, Blessie I. | MARTIN, Jasmine R. | SANTOS, Cherrie Mae A. | SANTOS, Maricris V. | SUMBILLO, Sheena Mae C. | VERGARA, Joshua G.'),
(111, 4, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'A CORRELATIONAL STUDY BETWEEN THE FACTORS THAT AFFECT LANGUAGE CREATIVITY IN PLAYING MOBILE LEGENDS: BANG BANG', 'This study was conducted to find out the correlation and the factors that may affect the language creativity in playing Mobile Legends: Bang Bang of the First year Education Students in Bulacan State University Hagonoy - Campus. The researchers identified the factors affecting the language creativity in playing Mobile Legends such as: demographic profile, duration, game ranking, word-formation processes, and the vocabulary of the players.\r\nThe researchers focused only on the different factors existent in the Language creativity shown in playing Mobile Legends: Bang Bang. The study did not do an in-depth analysis of morphological pattern and syntactic pattern, it only focused on the word-formation processes such as coinage and abbreviation.\r\nThe study was only limited to 1st year Education students, Bachelor of Secondary Education, English, Mathematics and Science) Bachelor of Technology and Livelihood Education and Bachelor of Elementary Education who are players of Mobile Legends in Bulacan State University Hagonoy-Campus School Year 2018-2019. Bachelor of Secondary Education English has the highest percentage of Mobile Legends player\'s within the total population of 98 respondents while Bachelor of Technology and Livelihood Education has the lowest percentage, fifty five respondents are male and forty three\r\nrespondents are female. Majority of the respondents have reached the maximum time duration in playing and male has the highest percentage of game exposure and 60% of them provided the Abbreviation word category: 22% Female and 36% Male. The other 40% of the respondents preferred Word Coinage with 17% female and 23% male. This study used qualitative, quantitative and inductive approach. Pearson R correlations of linear regression was considered in analyzing the data, as the researchers wanted to determine the significance of relationship between the given independent and dependent variable. SPSS version 22.0 program was the statistical treatment used to calculate analytical data gathered and compute for significance of data. Each data analyzed created an impact on the result of the study. The findings presented in this paper clearly illustrated that there is significant relationship between each factor which affects the language creativity in playing Mobile Legends: Bang Bang\r\n', 2019, 'John Michael G. Arellano | Mary Rose S. Lapaz | Mary Joy C. Magsakay| Sandra Polintan | Judy Ann T. Sacdalan | Ma. Angela DC. Sta. Cruz | Eunice Anne P. Sytamco'),
(112, 0, '0', 'THE PHRASES USED IN ONLINE SELLING IN THE PROCESS OF PERSUASION: AN ASSESSMENT ', 'The study focuses on the \"Phrases used in Online Selling in the Process of Persuasion: An Assessment\". The general problem of the study is, \"How are the phrases used by the online sellers persuade consumers?\" In addition, the specific problems are: (1) what is the demographic profile of the respondents in terms of; age, gender and location. (2) What are the common phrases do online sellers use? (3) What is the level of familiarity of the consumers to the phrases used by the online sellers? (4) Are the phrases effective to persuade consumer? Moreover, the researchers used the mixed method which gathers quantitative and qualitative data. The researchers administered survey questionnaires to 100 consumers around Hagonoy Bulacan.\r\nInside the survey questionnaires are the common phrases used in online selling like pta, rfs, hm, organic, authentic and more, aligned with tick boxes measuring the consumer\'s familiarity and their reason for using the phrase. After gathering and interpreting the data, the researchers found out that most of the consumers are familiar with the common phrases used in online selling. Though there are synonymous words for the given common phrases, they still choose to use those common phrases in the context of their online purchasing.\r\n\r\n', 2019, 'Angel Claire B. De Belen | Cheska Grace C. Perez | Elleiza S. Munez | Genber DG. Angeles | Kristella R. Dolosa | Leslie G. Lim | Mylene Joy E. Reyes| Sarah F. Vino'),
(113, 0, '0', 'ENHANCEMENT OF COOKIES USING SQUASH WITH COCONUT STRIPS', 'The study focuses on the \"Phrases used in Online Selling in the Process of Persuasion: An Assessment\". The general problem of the study is, \"How are the phrases used by the online sellers persuade consumers?\" In addition, the specific problems are: (1) what is the demographic profile of the respondents in terms of; age, gender and location. (2) What are the common phrases do online sellers use? (3) What is the level of familiarity of the consumers to the phrases used by the online sellers? (4) Are the phrases effective to persuade consumer? Moreover, the researchers used the mixed method which gathers quantitative and qualitative data. The researchers administered survey questionnaires to 100 consumers around Hagonoy Bulacan.\r\nInside the survey questionnaires are the common phrases used in online selling like pta, rfs, hm, organic, authentic and more, aligned with tick boxes measuring the consumer\'s familiarity and their reason for using the phrase. After gathering and interpreting the data, the researchers found out that most of the consumers are familiar with the common phrases used in online selling. Though there are synonymous words for the given common phrases, they still choose to use those common phrases in the context of their online purchasing.\r\n', 2022, 'Dela Cruz, Hanna Kariz DR | Royo, Alexa Jane Clemente, | Jolina Mae Garcia, |  Godwin Perez, |  Lenard Sevilla, |  Bryan Jasper Arellano, | Jayson Andrei'),
(114, 0, '0', 'UTILIZATION OF BYCATCH FISH MEAT AS HOMEMADE PATTIES', ' \"Bycatch\" is the unwanted fish and other marine creatures caught during\r\ncommercial fishing. The term \"bycatch\" was first originated in British Guiana during 1950\'s due to the large numbers of discarded catfishes caught by the local fishermen using their fish nets and abandoned as unmarketable. For instance, in the Municipality of In The Hagony Province of Bulacan the fish named \"Don Pilas\" is a kind of fish that serves as a discarded fish and unwanted catch or bycatch. It is also known for its scientific name \"Thryssa Setirostris\" and was considered as Indian Sardines and most abundant marine species in Batangas Bay. Moreover, the waters or nearby seas of Hagonoy, Bulacan are also rich in don pilas during month of August until December.\r\nMeanwhile, the word \"Patties\" was derived from the French word \"Pâté\" since 17th century and generally it was served in round and flattened shaped mostly made of ground pork meat. As part of food innovation rather than accepting regular pork meat as major burger patties the researchers in this study utilize the use of bycatch fish meat specifically don pilas as homemade bycatch fish patties.\r\nThe general problem of the study is how bycatch fish utilized into homemade patties. The main purpose or importance of the study is to introduce the good implications of using bycatch fish meat as substitute for burger patties.\r\nThe ingredients used in the preparation of homemade bycatch fish patties are fresh bycatch fish meat, all-purpose flour, breadcrumbs, eggs, onions, carrot, celery, salt, pepper and paprika. The tested sample of homemade bycatch fish patties had passed all the microbiological qualities. Homemade Bycatch Fish Patties go through sensory evaluation to evaluate its acceptability when it comes to appearance, aroma, taste, and texture. The overall acceptability of the product got scored 4.46 which means acceptable in all sensory attributes and the respondents accepted the product very well. The given results are based on the evaluation conducted among one hundred (100) respondents held during month of January - March 2022. Therefore, the researchers concluded that the Homemade Bycatch Fish Patties can be use as substitute burger patties in the market.\r\n', 2022, 'Eruel E. Tolentino | John Carlo J. Jacla | Melvin Jheff N. Carpio| Anna Luisa E. Anicete | Kristel C. Bautista | Janina Kyla S. Ofliar'),
(116, 0, '0', 'INFESTATION OF WATER HYACINTH AS A PREDICAMENT TO THE LOCALS OF BARANGAY IBA-IBAYO HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'Water hyacinth (Eichhornia Crassipes) is an obnoxious floating weed that deteriorates the enswathed ecosystem where it is present. It is one of the most invasive species of aquatic plants (Carlini et al., 2018). Native to South America, this plant grows on the surface of lakes, rivers, and canals in tropical and subtropical climates such as the Philippines. Water hyacinths have become a prevalent invading macrophyte in a rich body of water due to the human transport and fast growth rate, which has caused negative effects on the quality of the water (Pin et al., 2021). The river of barangay Iba-Ibayo Hagonoy, Bulacan, is enswathed by Water Hyacinth and mainly a dilemma to the locals living in the said vicinity. In this study, the researchers\' main goal is to identify the problem caused by the said obnoxious weed. The researchers used mixed-method as a research methodology and used standardized survey and interviews with guide questions to assess the dilemma brought by water hyacinth. With the interpreted gather\r\ned outcome, the river is simply unable to give aquatic resources and the chance of water transport and fishing exercises decreases. In the concern of wellbeing, the smell brought about by the rotting water hyacinth has an effect on the breathing of a person. It causes an imbalance in the ecosystem; because of the matting of the water hyacinth, the propagation of biotic species such as snakes and bayawak is profound. The proposed action plan is to turn it into a fertilizer and other products proposed by the locals through the said interview.\r\n', 2022, 'Gaspar, Edroline M.| Geronimo, Jhoana Mae C. | Guevarra, Fort Gian Piolo A. | Torres, Ralph S'),
(117, 0, '0', 'DEVELOPMENT OF LAGUNBAY (Lagundi and Bayabas)INTO HERBAL TEA', 'The study, titled \"DEVELOPMENT OF LAGUNBAY (LAGUNDI AND BAYABAS) INTO HERBAL TEA,\" intends to use Lagundi and Bayabas as the key components to create an herbal tea that may have health-promoting properties, especially during current Pandemic.\r\nThis research study was done among 100 people of Abulalas, Hagonoy, Bulacan who are consumers and entrepreneurs in order to serve as the foundation for Lagunbay herbal tea development recommendations. The developmental research method was adopted. A questionnaire was utilized to collect quantitative and qualitative data on sensory quality and other research parameters. Following a review of all of the data supplied in the research, the following conclusions were reached, and the following suggestions were made;\r\n1. The researchers created the \"Lagunbay\" herbal tea after three rounds of trial and error. The sensory quality of Lagunbay herbal tea is greatly influenced by the correct drying of the leaves.\r\n2. Research interest focused on various medicinal plant like; Guava (Psidium\r\nguajava L.) leaf extract as a functional ingredient for immunostimulant and Lagundi (Vitex negundo) leaf extract as the decoction to treat cough, fever, and other respiratory diseases. Lagundi is used to treat a variety of ailments, including coughing, asthma, phlegm secretion, and fever caused by colds or flu. While Guava is a traditional remedy for a number of ailments and symptoms, including menstrual cramps, diarrhea, the flu, type 2 diabetes, and cancer.\r\n3. Since the plants are commonly found in the Philippines, the capsules and syrups are available with a range of P8.00 to P200.00 from over-the-counter products.\r\nNow with the development of the Lagunbay (Lagundi and Bayabas) into herbal tea, each tea bag would be available with a range of P 3.50 to P 5.00. The ability of Lagundi and Bayabas leaf extract on the treatment of various diseases has been proven scientifically, but the mechanism hasn\'t been fully explained. Staying healthy requires a robust immune system. As a result, the ability of natural compounds to enhance the immune system has long been studied.\r\n4. As a result, Lagunbay herbal tea, with its diverse medicinal properties, requires further development for broader application. Future research should focus on the\r\ndevelopment and separation of novel chemical components for the creation of specialized items. The researchers also advise future researchers to perform study on upgrading the research product, such as adding certain substances for added\r\ntaste without compromising the product\'s quality. Keywords: Guava, Psidium guajava L., Lagundi, Vitex negundo, Pandemic, medicinal properties, herbal tea, leaf extract\r\n', 2022, ' Aguilar, Qeen N. | Castro, Amelia A. | De Guzman, Rose Ann D.| Mallari, John Patrick B. | Perez, Angelito J. | Sacando, Bernadete C.| Salamat, Brael Emer P.'),
(118, 0, '0', 'CHALLENGES IN ONLINE LEARNING EDUCATION TO GRADE 5 STUDENTS OF HANGGA ELEMENTARY SCHOOL', 'The study focuses on the challenges faced in the Online Learning of Grade 5 students in Hangga Elementary School as a result of the pandemic in the country. It also states the hindrance experienced by using the internet or google to have enough information and whether to match the researched data from the students. The researcher used a quantitative and qualitative mixed-method, conducted through an online survey through a random sample technique. The questionnaire is a five-point Likert scale composed of three parts. The first part is the challenges they faced during the Online Learning, and the second part includes the possible effects of the difficulties they faced in Online Class. The last part includes the possible solution they did to cope with the challenges they encountered. It was used with a sample of 41 respondents to gather valid and reliable information about challenges in Online Learning of Grade 5 pupils of Hangga Elementary School.\r\nThe pupils experiencing certain challenges in online learning, there are factors in different kinds of levels that they are dealing with. The interviewers gathered respondent\'s data registered 2.32, which implies \"seldom\" hindrances they faced for many reasons. The respondents are not affected by these challenges because it is registered as 1.44. The data shows that the respondents have already adjusted in the new way of the learning process. Students are attempting to overcome challenges they faced in the New Normal Education to avoid negative consequences such as downgrading, loss of concentration and motivation, and poor academic achievement. This research will serve as a guide for educators, students and researchers in online distance learning.\r\n\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Cuartero, Vincent Peter L. | Manahan, Joshua Louie A.| Perez, Erwin John DC | Pineda, Mark Daniel S'),
(119, 0, '0', 'SENTENTIAL AND MORPHOLOGICAL PROCESS SWITCHING: AN ANALYSIS OF THREE TYPES OF CODE-SWITCHING PATTERNS AMONG KAPAMPANGAN SPEAKERS', ' The analysis of code-switching practices in the Kapampangan community is the main objective of this study. The ability to switch and alternate in a conversation with a bilingual or multilingual can be identified as code-switching. Code-switching in Kapampangan culture is a common practice, according to research findings, that is used to express emotions, demonstrate respect, and communicate better with whom they are speaking. Inter-sentential, Intra- sentential, and Tag switching are the several types of code-switching that have been identified. This study stresses the significance of comprehending language use in multilingual communities and offers insights into the code-switching patterns in the Kapampangan community, particularly in the City of San Fernando. The findings of this research show that Kapampangan speakers most frequently used Intra-sentential code-switching. They used intra- sentential code-switching to express certain ideas or concepts that were better conveyed in another language, to add emphasis or emotion to their speech, and to demonstrate their linguistic ability. This study also analyzes the affixation used by the Kapampangan through the transcriptions of their responses. Based on the data gathered, the informants commonly used prefixes among other affixes. Their choices of affixation were influenced by the context of the situation or the intended meaning or the effect of the word. In short, they used affixes when they were trying to switch from their second language to their first language but ended up not, which is why they tend to use the Kapampangan word with Tagalog affixes in it.\r\n\r\nOverall, this study sheds light on the Kapampangan community code-switching customs and emphasizes the significance of comprehending language use in multilingual settings. The findings of this research have significance for language instruction and policy, highlighting the need for more knowledge of multilingualism and the function of code- switching in promoting communication and social cohesion in diverse communities.\r\n\r\nKey words: Code-switching, Kapampangan community, Intra-sentential, Inter-sentential, Tag switching, Multilingualism\r\n', 2023, 'Calivo, Jewelle Mae E. | Fajardo, Fatima S. |  Olicia, Elisha Ann Aubrey D. | Ong, Alyanna Loise P. | Romero, Arjay S.'),
(120, 23, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'EXPOSURE OF DIGITAL TECHNOLOGY ON ACADEMIC WRITING: AN ANALYSIS IN MECHANICAL ERRORS OF GRADE 9 STUDENTS', 'The study focused on exposure of digital technology on academic writing: an analysis in mechanical errors of grade 9 students. The researchers tried to find if exposure to digital technology for more than four had an impact on the frequency of mechanical errors in a student\'s academic writing. The respondents of the study are the ten Grade 9-Virgo students of San Roque National High School. The study used Pearson Moment Correlation as the statistical treatment in the study. The hypothesis formulated in this study is that exposure in digital technology for more than four hours has an impact on the frequency of mechanical errors in the academic writing of Grade 9- Virgo students at San Roque National High School. The salient findings in this study are the following: (1) Overall impact of digital technology exposure on mechanical errors in grade 9 learners\' academic writing. The results show that the Grade 9-Virgo from San Roque National High School is moderately associated with an increase in mechanical errors, particularly in punctuation, capitalization, and spelling, within their academic writing. (2) Impact of digital technology exposure on mechanical errors in terms of punctuation in Grade 9 learners\' academic writing. The study revealed that exposure to digital technology for more than four hours significantly influences the frequency of mechanical errors in terms of punctuation among grade 9 students. (3) Impact of digital technology exposure on mechanical errors in terms of capitalization in grade 9 learners\' academic writing. The results revealed that the exposure to digital technology exceeding four hours significantly affects the frequency of capitalization errors among Grade 9 students. (4) Impact of digital technology exposure on mechanical errors in terms of spelling in grade 9 learners\' academic writing. The results implies that as students\' exposure to digital technology increases for more than four hours, there is a moderate tendency for spelling errors to also increase in their writing. The study revealed a significant positive correlation between exposure to digital technology and mechanical errors in Grade 9-Virgo students\' academic writing. Lastly, based on the conclusion drawn, the researchers recommended the Future researchers to employ qualitative methods, such as discourse analysis, to understand potential connections between variables and formulate interpretations based on contextual knowledge and content specifics and to consider developing remediation programs in order to reduce the frequency of mechanical errors among student.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Mechanical Errors, Digital Technology, Error Analysis, Punctuation, Capitalization, Spelling, Academic Writing\r\n', 2024, ' Eugenio, Feliciti Anne DL. |  Estanislao, Arjon Eurielle G. |  Galgo, Roshane Jean W. | Magtira, Princess Ann C. |  Tolentino, Tricia A.'),
(121, 0, '0', 'GAME-BASED ACTIVITIES AS LEARNING RETENTION STRATEGY INSTATISTICAL PROCEDURE IN MATHEMATICS', 'The Program for International Student Assessment (PISA) of the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development has stated that the exam taken by the students in the Philippines caused the country to rank second to last in 2018 among the other 79 participating countries. In the years 2019 and 2020, the test scores were still decreasing. The research of Heibert (2023) stated that formal teaching is the learning style in the Philippines that lets students passively participate in class.\r\n\r\nWe conducted this study to find a way to determine whether game-based learning activities can affect the stimulation of students\' academic performance. Also, to know if using game-based activities impacts the performance of respondents. Our respondents in this research are in two sections. The first section is section A, where they are the Experimental group, while the second section is section B, where they are the Control Group. We conducted our research on the Experimental and Control group by giving them a pre-test and post-test.\r\n\r\nBefore the discussion begins, the pre-test is distributed to determine if each other has an idea about the lesson. The researchers used a traditional teaching style in the controlled group and a game-based learning activity in the experimental group. After the discussion, the post-test will be handed out to test if anything has changed. The difference between the experimental and control groups is that the Experimental uses game-based activities in the discussion, while the control group uses traditional learning.\r\n\r\nThis study\'s findings show the respondents\' performance level in the post-test. Both sections had an improvement in post-test performance. But the improvement in the performance of the Experimental Group, which is Section A was more excellent. The scores are satisfactory, with a total mean of 29. While Section B is slightly satisfactory, with a total mean of 23.302\r\nIn this study, the decision is accepted when the T-value is less than 2.000 at a 0.05 level of significance. Still, if its Greater than 2.000 at a 0.05 level of significance, the decision is rejected. Since the T value of Section A and Section B are greater than 2.000, the decision is to reject the null hypothesis. This study affects the student\'s performance using game-based activities.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, game-based activities are effective mathematics performance stimuli. The researchers\' recommendation for the teachers is to use this approach for a better outcome in stimulating students\' mathematics performance.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Game-Based, Game-Based Activities, Performance Stimuli, Traditional Teaching Method, Learning Retention Strategy\r\n\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Castro, Mylene DJ. | Galman, Mary Grace L. |  Mangahas, Mary Jem D. | Sacdalan, Pauline Ann DC. | Sarmiento, Elaine M. |  Sunga, John Irish B.'),
(122, 0, '0', 'AN UNDERGRADUATE RESEARCH PRESENTED TO THE FACULTY OF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'This study focused to determine the effects of an online learning environment on the academic engagement of students enrolled in the Bachelor of Secondary Education in Mathematics program at the Bulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus during the academic year 2021-2022. The method of random sampling was used to pick at least 75% of the entire population of students major in mathematics.\r\n\r\nThe study utilized a quantitative research methodology, and the percentage, mean, correlation test, and linear regression test were utilized to examine the effects that an online learning environment had on the academic engagement of college students.\r\n\r\nAccording to the findings of the study, there is a statistically significant effect between the use of online learning environments and the level of academic engagement proven by students majoring in mathematics at BulSU-Hagonoy Campus. Therefore, there is a high possibility of increasing students\' level of academic engagement if there is a great online learning environment for the students to utilize.\r\n', 2024, 'Calibuso, Aaron John R. | Dela Cruz, Roy C. |  Dionisio, Mark Angelo U. |  Geronimo, Jose Roy Jr. A.'),
(123, 0, '0', ' PARENTAL SUPPORT AND LEARNING INTEREST: EFFECTS ON STUDENTS\' ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE IN MODULAR AND FACE-TO- FACE LEARNING MODALITIES', 'COVID-19 brings changes on the academic system in the Philippines. Just to continue the school year that time, different modalities and platform are employed. This study seeks to differentiate the Effects of Parental Support and Learning Interest that students received in Modular Learning in school year 2021-2022 and Face to Face learning in today set-up. Quantitative was applied in this study using Frequency and Mean to measure frequency of occurrence of a specific score in a given set of data, T-Test, to see if there is a significant difference between the level of parental support that students received and the level of learning interest that students demonstrated during modular and face-to- face learning, and Pearson (r) to assess linear correlation, which also quantifies the connection between two variables to determine if parental support and learning interest have a significant effect on students\' academic achievement during modular and face-to- face learning. Researchers used survey to find out the effects of this study on the 28 students of Grade 6-Makabayan in Abulalas Elementary School.\r\n\r\nThe study revealed that parental support and learning interest has no significant effects on students\' academic performance. performance. It demonstrates that parental support has a moderate correlation with students\' academic performance in both modalities. As a result, parental support has a major impact on a child\'s academic progress. This allows parents to be aware of their child\'s development, which helps them perform better in school. While learning interest has no substantial effect on students\' academic achievement. Teachers, on the other hand, must raise students\' drive to study in order to improve their academic performance. The findings of this study will assist teachers reflect on their present teaching practices and improve learning outcomes. Future researchers who will conduct research related to Parental Support and Learning Interest: Effect on students Academic Performance in Modular Distance Learning and Face to Face Learning may also consider the findings of this study in drafting their related concepts.\r\n', 2023, 'ADRIANO, Jhovi Rose M. | AGUSTIN, Judy Ann L. |  BULAONG, Joyce Anne A. | BULAONG,  Kristel C. |  HALILI, Irish Beneath A. |  SANTOS, Zenaida'),
(124, 3, 'BEED', 'DEVELOPING BIG BOOK USING LOCALIZED CONTEXT', 'The research entitled \"Developing Big Book Using Localized Context\" delves into the integration of local context in the development of instructional material, specifically focusing on a big book. The study aimed to incorporate the unique culture of the Municipality of Paombong in the Province of Bulacan into the development of a big book for primary grade students. he researcher used Mixed Method Research (MMR) approach explore social phenomena in depth, using methods like ethnography to understand the\r\n\"why\" behind human experiences. This approach, emphasizing local context, aligns with design-based research where researchers can identify and address knowledge gaps in instructional materials. In this example, researchers are creating materials to teach Sukang Paombong production, a local process. Through survey, the researchers uncovered essential insights into the local community, revealing that a significant portion of residents were young adults, with a majority over 21 years old and a substantial percentage born in Paombong. Notably, all participants recognized local symbols, with sukang sasa or sukang paombong and sasa emerging as the most familiar. Historical records solidify the enduring significance of sukang sasa, or sukang paombong, and sasa as cherished symbols of Paombong, Bulacan. This recognition goes beyond mere designation. A local fiesta, held in collaboration with local government unit (LGU), exemplifies the communitys deep connection to these symbolic elements. Building on this foundation, the study emphasized the importance of infusing elements of local identity into instructional material to enhance student learning experiences. Subsequently, a big book centered on Sukang Paombong was meticulously crafted, adhering to the guidelines set by the Department of Education. This educational resource was then evaluated by LRMDS coordinators to ensure its acceptability. This study recommends promoting local symbols like Sukang Paombong to preserve cultural heritage and create educational materials using these symbols. It also suggests using a pre-test and post-test design to measure the effectiveness of big books and conducting similar studies in other municipalities to understand Bulacans diverse cultural heritage\r\nKeyword: Big book, Localized context, Sukang Paombong/sasa, Integration\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'Carmona, Mareese | Concepcion, Kimberly B. | Salonga, Adrian M. |Santiago, Narold Ezekiel P. | Santos, Rachelle M. | Tolentino, John Patrick'),
(125, 0, '0', 'ENGLISH LANGUAGE ANXIETY AMONG PRE-SERVICE TEACHERS:BASIS FOR CAPACITY BUILDING PROBLEM', 'The study aimed to determine the possible causes of English language anxiety among Pre-Service Teachers with a bachelors degree in Elementary Education in terms of\r\na) lack of confidence, b) fear of judgment, c) social cultural differences, and d) peer pressure among students. It is also intended to determine the abilities and skills of the\r\nrespondents, which are measured by the indicators: a) speaking, b) writing, c) reading, d) listening. A self-made survey questionnaire was used as a tool in gathering the data and disseminating it to the respondents of Bulacan State University - Hagony Campus, in the second semester of A.Y. 2022-2023. The findings of this study show the cause of English language anxiety among the respondents. The outcome of the Pre-Service Teachers English language skills average mean is 2.60, which regard as sometimes; on the other hand, the causes of English language anxiety average mean is 2.62, which also translates as sometimes. This outcome is consistent with the findings of the survey questionnaire distributed to fourth-year Pre-Service Teachers under the Bachelor of Elementary Education department. The possible causes of English language anxiety among the respondents were cited as the sources of high anxiety, even though the English language skills of the respondents were explained as having a prime knowledge of using English\r\nlanguage. Therefore, the researchers proposed an action plan that the Pre-Service teacher can use to overcome their English language Anxiety.\r\nKeywords: English language skills, English language anxiety, Pre-service teachers\r\n\r\n', 2023, ' Bautista, Anton Butch M. | Clara, Ayessa Jovy R. | Crisostomo, Wilfred Marvic P. | De Belen, Christina R. | Magno, Keith Allyson M. | Perez, Kristine I.| Ramirez, Eunice N.'),
(126, 5, 'BSED MATH', 'AN INSIGHT STUDY ON THE LEVEL OF JOB SATISFACTION', ' The purpose of this study was to investigate relations of teachers level of job satisfactions in faculty teachers of Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus. Hence, it examined the teachers level of job satisfaction in terms of Extrinsic and Intrinsic factors. To accomplish this purpose, the study employed quantitative research design. A total of 30 individuals have participated in the study, 53 teachers were included through convenience sampling technique. Survey questionnaire was the main instruments of data collection. The analysis of the quantitative data was carried out by using percent, mean, and T-Test. As the mean teachers level of job satisfaction revealed that the extrinsic factors have more influence than intrinsic factors on teachers level of job satisfaction in the study area. The practices of extrinsic factors and intrinsic factors of the study area are satisfactory. Based on the findings, the assessment on Level of Job Satisfaction in terms of Extrinsic factors at Bulacan State University Philippines - Hagony Campus was found to be effective and they are very satisfied in terms of salary, information sharing, job security, empowerment, participation, leadership, number of schedule. The assessment on Level of Job Satisfaction in terms of Intrinsic factors at Bulacan State University Philippines - Hagony Campus was found to be effective and they are satisfied in terms of career goals, responsibilities, knowledge level, achievement and respect for employee. It is recommended that the campus administration should be aware to the job security of the faculty teachers for their secured future, they must consider the service year of each teachers that needs to give more benefits according to their working status. The campus administration should be aware to the job salary of the faculty teachers in terms of additional incentives for extra works and also to those who underpaid in relation to their efforts. The campus administration should give more activity to collaborate teacher to develop the relationship of their co teacher.\r\n', 2022, 'Coronel, Lovely Jane F. | Domingo, Rhealyn F.| Halili, Ma. Cristina DC.| Parole, Leo Robin G. | Tayson, Marleen C'),
(127, 5, 'BEED', 'EDUCATIONAL SUPPORT ON SUSTAINABLE COMMUNITY PROJECTS IN SELECTED BARANGAY IN HAGONOY, BULACAN', ' Initiating constructive changes in a communitys socioeconomic structure is the main objective of community initiatives. In addition to educational programs, a community must establish a solid educational support structure in a few chosen barangays to promote environmental stewardship and socioeconomic resilience in sustainable development projects. Consequently, sustainable community projects aim to provide long-lasting effects on the environment, livelihoods, and overall well-being. Hence, each and every local barangay needs to have and engage in different educational programs being implemented in their area. In line with this, this present proposed study is conducted to discover how sustainable community projects play a crucial role in educational support in two (2) barangays in Bulacan namely Barangay Abulalas and Barangay Iba-Ibayo. The researchers utilized a quantitative research method to gather responses from eighty (80) respondents (both beneficiaries and barangay officials). Forty (40) respondents were from Barangay Abulalas and Forty (40) respondents were from Barangay Iba-Ibayo. When it comes to the gathering of data, the researchers distributed a survey questionnaire checklist to the target respondents. As they came up with the results, it was revealed that both of the two (2) barangays only have one (1) educational program that is currently being implemented. In line with this, it was also revealed that both the beneficiaries and barangay officials are just quite satisfied with the said program. As the researchers came up with the recommendation, it was highly suggested that there is a need to explore and understand how their educational programs affect the lives of the residents of the different barangays not just in Bulacan, but in other different areas.\r\nKeywords: sustainable educational program, satisfaction, implementation, planning evaluation\r\n', 2024, 'Cabatana, Shine Angeline C. | Cruz, Ma Roxanne S. | Mancilla, Eula L. | Nieto, Shaira Abigail P. | Robles, Rhosmine R. | Santos, Patricia Anne M'),
(128, 0, '0', 'LEVEL OF PERCEPTION IN THE USE OF DIGITAL AND NON-DIGITAL TOOLS IN SCIENCE LESSON', 'The recent study of Level of Perception in the Use of digital and Non-Digital Tools in Science Lesson shows that the mostly use of digital and non-digital tools in classrooms are printed picture, PowerPoint, textbook, video and real objects. These may help the teaching and learning floe of the students and the teachers. Digital and non-digital tools as the support of the learning of grade 6 pupils in terms of remembering and understanding. Digital and non-digital tools as the support of the learning of grade 6 pupils in terms of remembering and understanding.\r\nBased on the findings of this study, the type of digital and non-digital tools used during the lesson in science are printed picture, PowerPoint, textbook, video and real objects. This research will able to show that digital and non-digital tools as the support of the learning of grade 6 pupils in terms of remembering and understanding.\r\n', 2023, 'BENIDICTO, Janella B. | CERVANTES, Alaine E. | DIONISIO, Chelsea J.LLOBRERA,Mylene M. | SARMIENTO, Ma. Loraine C. | VELASCO, Jecel R.'),
(129, 6, 'BSED MATH', 'ACCEPTABILITY OF THE PROGRAM OBJECTIVES AND AWARENESS OF THE VISION, MISSION, GOALS, AND PROGRAM OBJECTIVES OF THE BACHELOR OF SECONDARY EDUCATION STUDENTS IN BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'The vision, mission, goals, and program objectives are the backbone of the Bulacan State University. They serve as the blueprint for the students and teachers towards the attainment of the university goals, and the development of its people. More than just statements posted in every corner of the school, they are essential as they align the university towards the accomplishment of its objectives.\r\nThough the vision, mission, goals, and program objectives are being discussed to students every time the school year begins, it is not assured that students really understand and are aware of its essence and relevance to the university. The researchers believe that this study could be an aid to know the students responses in order to assess their awareness and acceptability of the VMGO.\r\nThe Descriptive Method of Research was utilized in this study. This type of research enabled the researchers to gather data which was used to determine the level of awareness and acceptability among BSED students of BulSU Hagonoy Campus on the VMGO. Frequency and Percentage Distribution was used for descriptive presentation of the data such as the age, sex, specialization, and year level and section. The Weighted Mean was utilized by the researchers as a measure of central tendency. The researchers also used the z-test to determine if there is a significant difference on the level of awareness and acceptability of BulSU Hagony Campus VMGO.\r\nThe results revealed that the BSEd students of BulSU Hagony Campus are fully aware and completely accept the vision, mission, goals, and program objectives of the University. Based on the findings of the study, the null hypothesis is rejected while the alternative hypothesis is accepted since there is a significant difference between the awareness and acceptability of vision, mission, goals, and BSEd program objectives among the BSEd students of BulSU Hagonoy Campus.\r\nIn light of the findings and conclusion of the study, it is recommended for the University Administrators to consistently extend the reach of dissemination of the VMGO inside the campus. In the Online Distance Learning Education where teachers and students utilize various media platforms, VMGO could be sent to students Google Mail every semester. It could be posted on the Official Facebook page of the Campus or in every organizations social media page/account. Moreover, the use of printed materials could also be helpful to raise their awareness and insights regarding the VMGO statements. It could be displayed in every classroom of the campus through bulletin boards or be included in student publication papers. It could also be printed in tarpaulin and placed at the entrance and exit gate of the campus. Emphasis in the discussion of the VMGO to students is also necessary for them to remember and understand its essence.\r\nKeywords: awareness, acceptability, vision, mission, goals, and program objectives (VMGO), online distance learning, dissemination.\r\n', 2022, ' Abueg, Reychelle Ann G. | Cruz, Gieselle L. | Dela Cruz, Charmaine C.| Sayago, Carlo | Tolentino, Marie Claire L'),
(130, 19, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'GRADUATES EMPLPYABILITY STATUS: A TRACER STUDY OF BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY-HAGONOY CAMPUS BACHELOR OF SECONDARY EDUCATION MAJOR IN ENGLISH GRADUATES', 'The transition from higher education to the professionai word can be a significant hurdle for graduates. This study aims to assess the current employment status of graduates, identify the types of jobs they have secured, evaluate the skills acquired during their education, and investigate the challenges faced by graduates from the Bachelor of Secondary Education English programme at Bulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus.\r\nThe study employs a tracer study method, tracking specific cohorts from 2016-2019 to 2021-2023. By employing a tracer study approach to explore graduates challenges during their transition to the workforce, data collection is conducted through surveys and interviews to gather comprehensive insights into the career trajectories and experiences of the graduates. The findings of the study reveal key aspects such as the post-graduation employment rate, diversity of job roles undertaken, and challenges encountered in securing employment. It is observed that graduates, in their work fields, have effectively utilized these competencies and skills acquired from the university, contributing significantly to their success in the professional world.\r\nIn conclusion, the study underscores the importance of aligning university programmes with industry demands to enhance graduates employability. It emphasizes the need for continuous improvement. Enhance career counseling services to provide\r\npersonalized support, foster strong partnerships with industries for internship and job placement opportunities, and incorporate essential soft skills into the curriculum; conduct regular reviews of educational programmes to meet industry demands; foster active alumni networks for mentorship and career advice; and organize workshops and seminars for ongoing professional development. hThese recommendations aim to equip graduates with the necessary skills, support systems, and opportunities to succeed in their careers and contribute effectively to the workforce.\r\n\r\n', 2024, 'Andes, Abigail P. | Balingata, Khrystynn Astrea G. | Cervantes, Sheila Marie F. | Cruz, Aldrin S. | Flores, Dea Mariz L. | Zafra, Andrea T.'),
(131, 0, '0', 'ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE OF GRADE 6 LEARNERS AND ITS LEVEL OF PERCEPTION', ' This research study aimed to investigate the academic performance and level of perception of fith grade learners during face-to-face classes in San Agustin Elementary School. The research utilized a quantitative research design and a Likert scale questionnaire to answer specific sub-questions on components of summative assessment, factors affecting academic performance in school and family environments, and intervention plans for improving academic performance. The study found that several components of summative assessment significantly affected the academic performance of students. Written works, quarterly assessments, and performance tasks were identified as crucial components for students academic success. Additionally, factors such as the classroom environment, teacher effectiveness, and peers eagerness to learn were found to significantly impact the academic performance of learners. Based on the findings of the study, the research team recommended that interventions such as teacher training and parent involvement be implemented to improve academic performance.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Academic performance, face to face classes, summative assessment, school environment, family environment\r\n', 2023, 'AGRAVANTE, Joy Ann R. | JOSON, Ma. Julia Fe P. | QUIJADO, Melita B. SEBASTIAN, | Louise Jhemaine DC. |  SINON, Elaica Jean A.');
INSERT INTO `thesisbooks` (`id`, `control_number`, `course`, `title`, `abstract`, `year`, `author`) VALUES
(132, 0, '0', 'SIPNAYAN OR MATHEMATICS: THE ATTAINMENT OF LOWER ORDER THINKING SKILLS LEARNING TARGETS THROUGH THE USE OF MOTHER TONGUE-BASED AND ENGLISH INSTRUCTIONS', 'The present shisty experimentally determines the atterement of the learning target for lower-onder thinking skills in mathematics through the use of mother tongue based (MTR) and English instruction for grade 1 pupils at fita. Monica Elementary School (Y 2032 2033) This shisty used a quantitative method that will provide objective facte represented through statistics and numbers utilising the raw score of grade 1 pupils as the result of the assessment of both MTB and Einglish as a medium of instruction. The researchers utilized Slovins formula in selecting the sample size from the total population of grade 1 pupils at SMES. The following statistical tools were utilized in the analysis of the data: frequency, percentage, and weighted mean. In this study, an assessment test 15 being given to grade 1 pupil at Sta. Monica Elementary School, and it is divided into 2 sets, the mother-tongue-based instruction and the English instruction. Each set has two parts: the demographic profile of the pupils in Part 1, and a tool to measure learning in mathematics through mother-tongue-based instruction in Part 2. Set 2 of the assessment is the translated version of Set 1, from MTB to English as the medium of instruction. The researchers used Blooms taxonomy as a guide in developing these assessments; however, the assessment only focused on lower order thinking skills (LOTS) and was validated by the Grade 1 adviser, particularly the translation. The findings of this study reveal that both mother-tongue-based and English instruction are effective mediums of instruction in teaching mathematics, with both receiving an adjectival rating of very satisfactory.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Implementation, Challenges, Medium of Instruction, Mother Tongue- Based Multilingual Education (MTB-MLE), Primary Grades, Mathematics\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'BISAGAS, John Carlos DR.  | LIZARONDO, Ann Szherine J. | MARUKOT, Rochelle D. |  TAPANG, Rachel Anne DJ. | VALERIO, Anna Marie DL.'),
(133, 2, 'BSED MATH', 'REINFORCEMENT ON ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE AMIDST THE PANDEMIC', 'Parents and teachers reinforcement is an integral part of education system. With COVID-19 pandemic situation, educational set up together with how parents and teachers engagement to academic performance of students altered differently. Research finding shows that there is significant relationship between parents and teachers reinforcement for academic performance of the Bachelor of Secondary Education major in Mathematics students at Bulacan State University- Hagonoy Campus base from collected and analysis of the data gathered. The researchers formulate survey questionnaire using Likert Scale with 4 as always, 3 as often, 2 as sometimes, and 1 as never, and out of 109 respondents, 100% of the sample size responded. With the statistical method used, the study rejected the expected null hypothesis.\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Bulaong, Ferdinand A. | De Guzman, Angelo F. | Mangali, Vincent Aaron D. | Ventura, Edward John I, | Victoria, Lemmuel F.'),
(134, 0, '0', 'ENHANCEMENT OF BANANA PEEL PATTIES', 'This study aims to utilize the Saba Banana Peel or (musa acuminata) into a homemade patties. Banana peel, also known by its scientific name, Musa sapientum, was discovered to have a number of vitamins and minerals. The banana peel was composed of 11.82 2.17% crude carbs, 5.93 0.13% crude fat, and 1.95 0.14% crude proteins. The elements phosphorus, iron, calcium, magnesium, and sodium were all present in banana peels. Incorporating the findings trial and error, review of related study and literature, and survey questionnaires is used. The Banana Peel can be alternatively used in making patties. The researchers concluded that the banana peel patties would be acceptable. And the cost of making banana peel patties is very affordable.\r\n\r\nKey words: Saba Banana Peel, Homemade Patties, Musa Sapientum, Musa Acuminata, Affordable.\r\n', 2023, 'John Michael Aguilar| Bautista, Jayson T.| Cabral, Erica Joyce A.| Enriquez, Melanie P.| Perez, Olivia Marie E.| Revilla, Rinalyn C.'),
(135, 1, 'BTLED HE', 'ORELEMON CANDLE: AN INNOVATIVE MOSQUITO REPELLANT FROM OREGANO AND LEMONGRASS', 'The purpose of this investigation was to develop an organic mosquito repellant that has an ingredient that is easy and accessible to find in the community; these ingredients are lemongrass and oregano. This study investigates the right procedure to formulate an effective mosquito-repellant candle using oregano and lemongrass. It was also intended to investigate the correlation between the different ratios and their effects in terms of duration and number of mosquitoes killed. This research uses a quasi-experimental method that utilizes trial and error, a survey questionnaire, and testing of the product for data gathering. The products ideal look, smell, and texture were created using the trial-and-error process. Survey questions assess the products sensory attributes. Additionally, an evaluation of the product was carried out to determine the impact of various ratios on the length of time and quantity of mosquitoes killed. The respondents assessment of sensory acceptance based on smell, texture, and appearance formed the basis for the studys conclusions. The findings indicate that participants gave fragrance the lowest grade, with a weighted mean of 3.3. While the respondents gave texture a rating of 3.5, which they found to be completely acceptable. The highest rating is 3.6, which is the appearance. Furthermore, the results of the effect of orelemon candles show that 2 teaspoons of orelemon extract can kill 10 mosquitoes in 90 minutes. For 3 teaspoons of orelemon extract, it kills 16 mosquitoes in 60 minutes. While 4 teaspoons of orelemon extract kill 21 mosquitoes in 45 minutes, the data shows that the different ratios of the orelemon extract can affect the number of mosquitoes killed and their duration.\r\nBased on the results of the Pearson correlation and p-value, it indicates that there is a non- significant, very small negative relationship between the duration and ratio. It demonstrates that the fewer extracts used, the longer it takes for the effect to be observed. However, the results showed that there is a significant and strong positive association between the two factors in terms of killed mosquitoes and ratios. It reveals that the candle may kill more mosquitoes the more extract is used in it. The percentage and quantity of mosquitoes destroyed generally vary greatly. Although the results of the experiment indicate that the performance of the orelemon candle based on the number of mosquitoes killed is not far from the performance of the mosquito coil, the coil used to kill mosquitoes is still far better than the orelemon candle based on the assessment. Hence, the researcher accepts the hypothesis therefore, the orelemon candle can be used as an alternative to the mosquito coil as a mosquito repellant\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Aguinaldo, Christine Joy S.| Cajida, Darlyn L. | Castro, Sheena May A. | Fajardo, Nicah Aileen L. | Reyes, Sarah Joy M.'),
(136, 0, '0', 'ASSESSMENT OF THE ACCEPTABILITY OF PANDESAL DE GUYAPAN', ' The researcher will carry out this study to an ascertain the acceptability of Pandesal De Guyapan made with Guyabano and Pandan leaves since in contrast to other varieties of Pandesal, they have various benefits for individuals. The purpose of the research was to evaluate the acceptability of \"Pandesal De Guyapan\" which sparked the researchers curiosity.\r\n\r\nThe researchers aim to utilize guyabano and pandan leaves in the bread production. Pandesal De Guyapan provides different health benefits like lowering cholesterol, preventing urinary tract infections, improving sleep duration, boosting our immune system, and helping weight loss. It contains different kinds of vitamins minerals, and antioxidants known to support good health. It is also an important ingredient for eye benefit of pandan leaves. It is a natural technique to relieve dizziness and can help prevent stroke. Pandan leaves are an effective cure for pains and cramps, and can be used by making a liniment and massaging it into the affected area. This is also beneficial in the treatment of arthritis pain.\r\n\r\nWhile, Guyabano is high in vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients. Guyabano includes vitamins A, C, E, K, Choline, Folate, Thiamin, Niacin, Pyridoxine, Pantothenic acid, and Riboflavin. Guyabano also contains Omega 3 fatty acids, Omega 6 fatty acids, dietary fiber, salt, and potassium, all of which have significant health benefits.\r\n\r\nThe ingredients used in making \"Pandesal De Guyapan\" were all-purpose flour, sugar, eggs, yeast, salt and guyabano and pandan extracts. By combining fresh guyabano and pandan leaves \"Pandesal De Guyapan\" produced a more delicious yet healthy flavored pandesal.\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'REGIO, Vernardita M.  | BAUTISTA, John Sequiel C. | REYES, Lenewniel F. | FLORES, Rosemarie S. | DELA CRUZ, Jean S.'),
(137, 11, 'BSED MATH', 'CORRELATION OF CODE-SWITCHING AS TEACHING PEDAGOGY AND STUDENTS ACADEMIC ENGAGEMENT IN MATHEMATICS', ' The study aimed to determine the relationship between the code-switching teaching strategy of the mathematics teachers at San Roque National High School and the students academic engagement. It is measured by the classroom learning phases as indicators: ( Preliminary, (b) Lesson Proper, and (c) Evaluation. Two sets of questionnaires were disseminated to the respondents, first, to all San Roque National High School Junior High Mathematics teachers, and second, to the selected student via convenience sampling from the Junior High School level in the academic year of 2022-2023. The findings of the study show that in every indicator, both group of respondents agrees that in every indicator, with the weighted mean range from 3.51 to 4.50, the students academic engagement is moderately high when the teacher uses code-switching teaching pedagogy. In correlating the two variables using Pearsons r correlation coefficient, the result indicate that teachers code-switching strategy and students academic engagement have a high positive correlation (-0.78) meaning, the two variables move in the same direction. However, the researchers accept the null hypothesis stating that the two variables have no significant relationship in one another due to the reason that the r-value is greater than the significance level, 0.05. Therefore, the researchers recommend to the future researchers to test more factors that have a significant relationship to the learning of students, not just academic engagement. The researchers also recommend for the administration to create a program that will enhance the knowledge of both students and teachers in different mathematical terminologies written and spoken in L1 and L2.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Code-Switching, Academic Engagement, Mathematics, Students, Teachers, Teaching, Pedagogy\r\n\r\n', 2023, 'Cabardo, Caryle Joy M. | Crisostomo, Katherine N.  | Tolentino, Patricia Mnemosyne F. |  Umali, Jericho C. | Vasquez, Jazel Mae T.'),
(138, 0, '0', 'MULTIPLE SKILLS DEVELOPMENT: A COMPARATIVE STUDY AMONG FACE-TO-FACE LEARNING AND ONLINE LEARNING', 'Considering the pandemic, a lot of establishments closed and many programs and activities were forced to continue over the internet including education specifically in tourism management where service and interaction is an important key to their learning The traditional way of leaming is vital for students success, due to the reason that it gives them the reality of what they can expect in the real world. The universities provide an experience that students can take away when they graduate from school. The matter of the relationship between traditional learning and online students has been undergoing studies for over decades. The purpose of this study is to understand the preparedness of tourism graduates with different mediums of learning such as traditional learning and distance learning. Thus, this study will know the multiple skills of tourism students that graduated with different mediums of learning. The findings of this study will reflect the benefit of aspiring students in tourism management.\r\n\r\nIn this study is the researcher wants to determine the comparison of Tourism students that graduated in a normal way of teaching and the Tourism students that graduated in online learning and to know if they are both prepared and ready for employment in the tourism industry. This research anticipates fulfilling the questions: What is the extent to which the BS Tourism Management program contributed to the development of the face-to-face graduates in terms of; Communication skills, Leadership skills, Problem-solving skills, and Human relation skills and What is the extent to which the BS Tourism Management program contributed to the development of the Online learning graduates in terms of; Communication skills Leadership skills, Problem-solving skills, and Human relation skills.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of this study is to understand the preparedness of tourism graduates with different mediums of learning such as traditional learning and distance learning. Thus, this study will know the multiple skills developed by tourism students that graduated with different mediums of learning. The findings of this study will reflect the benefit of aspiring students in tourism management that wanted to work in the industry of tourism and for the employers that wanted to hire competitive and well-enhanced graduate students to work in their company.\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'CRUZ, Mark lan HERNANDEZ, Gerrie Mae | DEL ROSARIO, Renz Adriel| MAGAHIS, Jane Claire | MOSTACISA, Kyle Joshua | SUNGA, Gerry'),
(139, 11, 'BSTM', 'A COMPARATIVE STUDY: THE EFFECTIVENESS BETWEEN DO-IT- YOURSELF BOOKING AND PACKAGE TOUR IN THE CITIZEN OF HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'Travel agents and package tour have been the main intermediaries in the tourism sector, contributing significantly to the evolution and development of destinations and tourism companies, acting as a bridge between consumer demand and the operators offer. (Huang, Goo, Nam, & Yoo, 2017; Sun, Cárdenas, & Harrill, 2016) Independent travel booking is another method or approach of making travel arrangements. Instead of depending on travel agents to arrange their accommodations and other needs. The purpose of this study is to know which of two booking arrangements they prefer and who is more effective when traveling. The researchers applied a mixed method that included data gathering and descriptive research. Respondents were given an open-ended survey form via Google forms. The T-test is required to determine whether there is a statistically significant difference between the two variables, the efficiency of DIY booking and package tours. All results are presented with the proper levels of confidence and significance using trusted statistical techniques, such as the correlation coefficient. The findings of the paper offer a useful source of data for evaluating the level of effectiveness between DIY Booking and Package Tour. This study did not find a difference between DIY Booking and Package Tour. Although there is a slight difference based on the percentage of respondent results, the overall result shows no significant difference between the package tour and DIY Booking as both respondents answers were all in agreement. This paper develops an argument that both DIY and Package Tour is effective in terms of tour itinerary and costing/rate since travelers can save more money, make the itinerary more enjoyable, and access their necessities more easily. Given that both ways of traveling. whether via a DIY tour or a package tour, have benefits that travelers can enjoy, both DIY and package tour could provide some suggestions and services for a comfortable journey.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Package Tour, DIY Booking, Travel Decision, Tour Itinerary, Individual Booking\r\n\r\n', 2022, ' Alvarado, Jasmin S. | Fabian, Ma. Joyce Anne E. | Matic, Angelica T. | Sulit, Kristine Jewel P.'),
(140, 0, '0', 'SWOT ANALYSIS OF HAGONOYΥ PASALUBONG CENTER', 'This research chapter encapsulates the core findings, conclusions, and strategic recommendations derived from an in-depth study conducted on Hagonoy Pasalubong Center, a prominent cultural heritage and souvenir establishment located in Hagonoy, Bulacan. The invesugation involved gathering insights from a diverse group of 50 respondents, comprising local residents, center personnel, and neighboring residents. The primary objective was to assess the current operational status of the center and propose comprehensive strategies for its sustained growth and development.\r\n\r\nThe summary of findings unveils significant insights into the inherent strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, and threats faced by Hagonoy Pasalubong Center. The results highlight notable concerns related to ambiance, product freshness, limited product variety, pricing strategies, and marketing efforts. Conversely, the research identifies encouraging aspects, such as the positive perception of staff knowledge and approachability, product taste, and product quality.\r\n\r\nBased on the discerned findings, a set of recommendations is put forth, addressing both Hagonoy Pasalubong Center and the broader Municipality of Hagonoy. These recommendations encompass a spectrum of improvements, encompassing enhancements to ambiance, product freshness, product taste, staff training, and customer engagement. Moreover, the proposed strategies aim to tackle the perceived limitations in product variety, concerns about location popularity, marketing deficiencies, packaging quality, and pricing competitiveness. These recommended actions collectively aim to bolster the centers competitive edge, elevate customer satisfaction levels, and contribute to the preservation of local cultural heritage.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the study underscores the preferences expressed by respondents regarding business growth strategies. It accentuates robust support for the adoption of an online store and the expansion of the product range to incorporate regional specialties. The research also emphasizes the significance of loyalty programs, social media marketing, and the prospect of collaborating with local tourism agencies.\r\n\r\n', 2022, ' Lhian Mae F. Cortez | Joshua Miguel C. Marcelo | Ann Meilany M. Martin'),
(141, 0, '0', 'AN ANALYSIS OF COMMON GRAMMATICAL ERRORS IN WRITTEN COMPOSITION TOWARDS ACHIEVING ACADEMIC WRITING ACCURACY', 'The study analyzed the common grammatical errors and identified the possible reasons of these errors in the written essays made by forty (40) students. The participants wente 3rd year English major students who are currently enrolled at Bulacan State University-Hagonoy Campus in the academic year 2017-2018; eight (8) male and thirty- avo (32) female. The instruments used in order to gather data needed for the research were the participants written essay and a modified checklist adapted from the study of Houtati in 2008. The results of the study showed that five (5) common grammatical errors committed by the participants were subject-verb agreement, run-on sentence or comma splices, verb form, spelling and punctuation, respectively. It has been found out that there are two major sources of grammatical errors. These were classified as intralingual and interlingual errors. These sources have something to do with language transfer involving the first language and second language. On the other hand, there were also several possible reasons that apply the difficulty in writing. These possible reasons were the contextual factor and behavioral factor. Based on the findings, it can be concluded that the most agreed reason in writing difficulty in terms of contextual factor lies in the incomprehensibility of grammar rules, while in the behavioral factor the difficulty lies in mother-tongue interference.\r\n\r\nKeywords: Grammatical errors, Error analysis, Essay, Writing\r\n', 2018, 'Jann Mark C. Marcelino | Kevin A. Montecalvo | Trizia Mae A. Reyes | Maria Teresa F. Rubio | Kimberly Anne P. Santos | Angelica C. Sta Cruz'),
(142, 2, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'WATTPAD READING: THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN READERS AND NON-READERS AMONG ENGLISH MAJORS IN BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY-HAGONOY CAMPUS', 'This research was done to know the difference between of readers and non-readers of Wattpad. The study aims to know the performance of these two types of respondents in terms of grades and reading skills. The researchers used the quantitative method to gather the data needed and a reading comprehension test to know the level of their reading skills. Results showed that there is a significant difference between their reading skills and the effect size was large based on the t-test result. Table 19 shows that out of 34 Wattpad Non-readers, 14 are under proficient level while out of 24 Wattpad readers, 20 are proficient. This shows that more Wattpad readers are proficient because aside from reading Wattpad, they had taken up literature subjects that require them to read poems and novels. In terms of Grades, there is no significant difference between the two that is why reading Wattpad will not negatively affect the academic performance.\r\n', 2017, 'Alissen Y. Bondoc | Nathalia R. Bondoc| Juddie Marrisse G. Bonifacio | Veronica F. Generalao'),
(143, 8, 'BSED ENGLISH', 'PROBLEMS ENCOUNTERED BY ENGLISH LANGUAGE LEARNERS IN ONLINE MODE OF LEARNING', 'The occurrence of CoVid 19 strengthened the use of ICT tools in education, and changed almost all of the systems that humans were accustomed to. For years, the coronavirus disease 19 (Covid-19) affected local and global economy and the educational system. Several countermeasures were implemented to cope with the situation and maintain learning despite the challenges using various learning modes which include online (synchronous); and modular (asynchronous), or blended learning systems. It has a direct impact to English language education. Because of its implementation, educators who are unfamiliar with the system encountered difficulties. Several questions arouse, with regards to its effect to the quality of education that students will receive using other approaches and how students will cope with it which brought difficulties in deciding which mode of learning is best suited to the learners.\r\n\r\nThe study used a quantitative method with a descriptive, non-experimental design. The quantitative method will deal with large sample sizes of participants who will be representative of the entire population. The population and sample of the study are the Bachelor of Secondary Education major in English program at Bulacan State University- Hagonoy Campus with 195 students enrolled. Using Slovins formula, this studys sample size is 131, with a margin of error of 0.05. The researchers used a research-made Likert scale questionnaire with descriptions as 5,4,3,2,1 where 5 was labeled Strongly agree, 4- Agree, 3 Neutral/Uncertain, 2 Disagree and 1-Strongly Disagree. The questionnaire will be done via an online survey which will be distrusted to the respondents.\r\n\r\nResults shows that majority of learners are technologically oriented and educated that enables them to fix technical problems; however, the common problems that learners are most likely to experience are struggles to study at home because of the background noise, housework, and duties which affects their motivation wherein it causes them to be isolated which results to have a lack of desire to learn online. It also indicates that students are in a state of confusion about the problems they encountered while learning online because the learners are disoriented about the online learning set up.\r\n\r\nThis study recommended the following: (1) To reduce the number of women who encountered problems classmates or teachers must help them by giving enough provision with their need like internet connection, use of device etc. (2) A whinar ondd implement to provide guidance and encouragement for a sense of inspiration to continue learning. (3) A remote learning for the students of English 24, who showed a great percentage who encountered problems in online class while for other year levels mary request a one-on-one meeting with a teacher or instructor to receive a personalized assistance. (4) To lessen the percentage of age from 20 to 22, they need to stick to a comfortable time schedule, making a list of tasks to complete, and asking teachers for help when they dont understand something. (6) Students must set up a study table in a convenient location around the house and to reduce background noise, use earphones with a built-in microphone. (7) There must be cooperation with barangay chairman to give students a place with a conducive environment provided with a strong internet connection. (8) There must be a collaborative opportunity, regular feedback, diverse content delivery, and engaging presentational style. (9) A webinar focusing on the use of technology. (10) An orientation should happen before the beginning of school year because a webinar will be a platform for students to be well-informed about the possible challenges that they may face in the online learning modality. (11) A proposed action plan is made to the university.\r\n', 2022, 'ANGCAJAS, ROBERT M. |  CASTILLO, CONCEPCION ISABEL B. | DIONISIO, RICHARD C. | ESTORNINOS, ARON PAUL T. |  MANUEL, LAILAH DIANNE M.|  REGALADO, ELLA MAE G'),
(144, 0, '0', 'PARTISIPASYON NG MGA MAMAMAYAN SA PAMAMAHALA NG MGA BASURA SA BARANGAY SAN AGUSTIN HAGONOY, BULACAN', 'Ang layunin ng pananaliksik na ito ay matukoy ang Partisipasyon ng mga mamamayan sa pamamahala ng mga basura sa Barangay San Agustin Hagonoy, Bulacan. Ang nasabing pananaliksik ay sumailalim sa kwalitatib at kwantitatib na pamamaraan at ginamitan ng Simple random sampling kung saan kumuha ng apat na raan (400) na respondente mula sa mamamayan ng Barangay San Agustin Hagonoy, Bulacan. Ang sarbey forms ang ginamit na instrumento sa pananaliksik upang makakuha ng mga datos na kinakailangan sa pag-aaral.\r\n\r\nBase sa ginawang pananaliksik, lumabas na ang residual waste ang pinakamaraming uri ng basura ang naipoprodyus ng mga mamamayan sa bawat purok ng Barangay San Agustin. Karamihan sa mamamayan ng Barangay San Agustin ay nakakaranas na matambakan ng mga basura sa kani-kanilang tahanan dahil hindi nakokolekta ang kanilang mga basura, kapag sila ay hindi nakokolektahan ng basura ay itinatapon na lamang nila ito sa ilog. Naipakita din sa datos na nakuha ng mga mananaliksik karamihan sa mga mamamayan ng Barangay San Agustin ay hindi nagse- segregate ng kanilang mga basura o naghihiwala-hiwalay ng basura.\r\n\r\nInirerekomenda ng mga mananaliksik na mailahad sa kinauukulan ang R.A 9003 upang magkaroon ng wastong sistema sa pagtatapon ng mga basura upang mabigyang proteksyon ang kalusugan ng mga mamamayan sa natukoy na barangay at upang mapanatili ang kalinisan sa kapaligiran at nirerekomenda din ng pag-aaral na ito na ang bawat sambahayan sa nasabing barangay ay magkaroon ng Upgraded Eco bag upang magamit ng mga mamamayan ang ito sa pamamalengke at upang maiwasan ang paggamit ng mga plastic bags.\r\n', 2022, 'Enero, Vanessa S. | Macalinao, Jessa Mae P. | Ople, Marlin A. | Torres, Regine C.'),
(145, 0, '0', 'DEVELOPMENT OF EMPANADA USING (MILKFISH SISIG) WITH VARIATIONS OF FLAVOR', 'The main purpose of the study is to develop the empanada using milkfish sisig with variations of flavor. Empanadas is a type of baked or fried pastry and filling turnover. The empanadas are filled with cod fish or chicken and are comparable to cut-up pies. An empanada is formed by folding a disc of thinly rolled dough into a semicircle over the filling and crimping the edges to seal it. The processed used in the production of Empanada using (Milkfish Sisig) was selection and preparation of raw materials, form a dough then filled with milkfish sisig, frying, and packaging.\r\n\r\nThe sensory properties of the sample were found as follows; the appearance scored a scale 4.48 which is acceptable and it has the lowest score. The taste scored a scale 4.69 which is very acceptable. The aroma scored a scale 4.78 which is very acceptable. The color scored a scale 4.88 which is very acceptable, it has the highest score. Lastly, the texture scored a scale 4.83 which is very acceptable. The overall acceptability of the product is 4.73 which is very acceptable\r\n\r\n', 2022, ' Tiongson Maricurl M. | Tolentino Jessica F. | Dela Cruz Nathalie Rociel Joy L. | Toribio Laiza Mariz M. | Serrano Sharon N. | Molina Dante P. |  Pineda Cielo Ellaine C'),
(146, 0, '0', 'UTILIZATION OF TRADITIONAL METHOD OF MORINGA SHRIMP KROPEK', 'Hagonoy is abundant with the variety of snacks that will be found in any corner of the town. One of the famous that any ages can enjoy was chicharron. It comes with different flavors which is mushroom, pork, sour cream, hot cheese, spicy, garlic etc. and it was very affordable.\r\n\r\nThe moringa or better known as malunggay was also easy to be found in the market specially in the Pamilihang Bayan ng Hagonoy. In every vegetable stall, there are moringa leaves in retail.\r\n\r\nAs it is a snack, it wasnt really healthy so that it didnt really good to make the kids eat them every day. At that note, the researcher come up with the idea to innovate the product. One of the types of chicharron was Kropek. The main ingredient for this was prawn. To make it affordable than the normal kropek, the researcher use shrimp because its cheaper and its more available in Hagonoy market. And to make it much healthier, the addition of moringa leaves was done\r\n', 2022, 'Colete, Sarah B. | Contigino, Arlene Y. |Enriquez, Tricia Mae. | Gomia, Kazandra C. | Igus, Khristalle M. | Mendoza, Erikka JoyM. | Pahati, Mikee M.'),
(147, 0, '0', 'A TRACER STUDY ON ELEMENTARY EDUCATION GRADUATE IN BULACAN STATE UNIVERSITY HAGONOY CAMPUS FROM ACADEMIC YEAR 2015-2018', 'Every university aspires to produce top-notch graduates. From S.Y. 2015 to 2018, a study was conducted to track Bachelor of Elementary Education graduates. This study aimed to determine the employment aspects and assess the extent of the courses contributory factors that helped the graduates develop and the extent of the course on the overall college life experience, and extent of life satisfaction of Bachelor of Elementary Education Major in General Education graduates from 2015 to 2018. The data was gathered via a descriptive survey. In total, 59 BEEd graduates are involved in the research. The data was interpreted using frequencies and percentages. Results showed that graduates from Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus employment rate are positively high\r\n\r\nMoreover, the job placement profile of the respondents after graduation is positively high and effective. Between S.Y. 2015 to 2018, there is a considerable difference in the effects and relevance of acquired skills and abilities among BEEd graduates. The attained skills and abilities of BEEd alumni batch 2015 to 2018 have a significant impact and relevance to the demands of their jobs. Nonetheless, they recommended that the curriculum at Bulacan State University Hagonoy Campus be improved further by providing more ICT-related training/seminars and workshops, continuing to develop, monitor, and strengthen students entrepreneurial and problem- solving skills, creating innovative leadership and institutional reforms, and including a LET-related questionnaire in the examination. The findings can be used to improve the curriculum and instruction through the program.\r\n', 2022, 'Ablaza, Niña Victoria A. | Enriquez, Michelle S. | Samperoy, Erika Mae C. | Talucod, Ma. Janella G'),
(148, 0, '0', 'RIZALS ADVENTURE: A WORD GUESSING GAME', 'The purpose of this study is to develop an educational game for the students. The developers conducted a study to the Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus and confirmed that the students are having difficulties in the History Subject.\r\n\r\nBased on the survey, some of the problems that affect the grade of the students are: The history subject is difficult to understand, the subject history is boring and many dates and persons to remember. The developers developed a new way of learning for the students of Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus.\r\n\r\nIn developing the game, the developers used Agile method because this method involves continuous planning, continuous testing and continuous integration. The developers used different kinds of software to developed this game like unity, photoshop and Adobe Audition The developers used unity as game engine, photoshop used to design characters and other user interface of the game and Adobe Audition to edit the sounds of the game.\r\n\r\nAfter the game was tested for its Design, Performance, Sounds and Compatibility through the questionnaire distributed among the 30 respondents. The developers used rating scale of 1-5 to evaluate the game. Design has a mean of 4.42 while the performance has a mean of 4.5, sounds has a mean of 4.30 and compatibility has a mean of 4.56. According to 30 respondents the Rizal Adventure has an overall mean of 4.45 and it means all the respondents agree to the design and functionality of the game.\r\n\r\nBased on the evaluation, the developers conclude that the Rizals Adventure can be implemented in Bulacan State University - Hagonoy Campus\r\n', 2018, 'Bolilan, Mark Justine C.| Centeno, Marco DG. | Custodio, John Wendell H. | Marcelino, Christian D. | Nabong, Norman L'),
(149, 0, '0', 'AN INNOVATIVE APPLICATION OF SWEET POTATO SPREAD', 'This study investigates the nutritional composition and consumer acceptance of sweet potato spread as a sweet potato food product Sweet potato, a nutrient-rich food, is processed into a spread form by cooking, mashing, and mixing. Close examination revealed the spreads high content of fiber, vitamins, and minerals, with low levels of fat and cholesterol. Evaluation on a diverse consumer panel showed overall positive reception, especially for its natural sweetness and smooth texture. Including sweet potato spreads in the diet offers a convenient and nutritious alternative to traditional spreads, with potential health benefits.\r\n', 2024, 'Agustin, Edielaine D.P. | Alcoriza, Aaron Claire B. | Dela Cruz, Noirene L. | Padilla, Clarisse C. |Umali, Jasmine S'),
(150, 12, 'BSED MATH', 'TRES: EFFECTIVENESS OF DRILL PRACTICE IN ENHANCING GRADE 10 STUDENTS PERFORMANCE IN SOLVING INTEGER OPERATIONS AT SAN PEDRO NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL', 'The curriculum has undergone to a constant change. It is being created by professional who have a distinguished knowledge towards education. This curriculum changes to ensure that the students are properly equipped before working in the industry. Education programs and services in the United States and across the world can only be as good as their curricula. Even the smallest educational institutions have a curriculum at the heart of their operation. The long-term viability and efficacy of higher education depends on the quality of its curriculum (Barnett & Coate, 2005). This research study examines the alignment of the Learning Outcomes of Mathematics Curriculum to the job qualification of the Industry. A study about the match and mismatch was conducted by Kucel (2019). Over education has been shown to be common and persistent in a variety of countries. It is frequently associated with working in a job that is unrelated to ones subject of study (horizontal mismatch) or one that demands fewer talents than one has (skill mismatch). In this study the competencies that the students should acquire from the University is being examine and its alignment to the job qualification of the industry. This quantitative research utilizes the Pearson R Correlation Coefficient between two variables to test the hypothesis. After gathering all the data and performing the statistical treatment, the researchers found out that 75% of the graduates from batch 2016-2017 to the batch 2020-2021 was entered the education industry. Based from the responses, the learning outcomes of mathematics curriculum is aligned with the job qualification of the industry. The changes from the industry will affect the curriculum of the schools\r\n\r\nKeywords: Alignment of the Learning Outcomes, Mathematics Curriculum, Job Qualifications\r\n\r\n', 2022, 'Austria, John Paul L. | Brosas, Jose Jack Rodolfo S. | Cabral, Reinalyn DC. | Dela Cruz, Robert V. | Lobrio, Dan Vincent P. | Santos, James Asley M. ');
